          "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is the Foundations board: Marks, captions and chips.\n\nTYPE: NEW (a component specimen board)\n\nATTACH: none. None of these nine components has shipped yet, so there is no host screen to match. Tokens, the type scale and the base icon set come from the published Pantopus design system.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nThis is the first design work for Pantopus and comes before any screen. Every later screen prompt names these nine components exactly, and each screen is designed in a separate project with no memory of this one. Once the founder accepts this board, the founder adds the components to the published Pantopus design system (see PUBLISH). That is the only way the same component comes out identical on 59 surfaces. So draw each component once, precisely, with every variant and every state listed in this prompt, and label everything with its exact name, its keys (B18) and its token names. Everything you need is written in this prompt; you do not need any other document.\n\nThe nine components, in this order (use these names exactly as section and artboard titles):\n1. ProvenanceMark\n2. SourceCaption\n3. ScopeChip\n4. FreshnessLine\n5. OfflineNotice\n6. StatusChip\n7. KindGlyph\n8. AddressChip\n9. ChoiceChip\n\n======================================================================\nBOARD RULES (these apply to every artboard in this project, 00a · ProvenanceMark through 00a · Notes)\n======================================================================\n\nB1. Artboard format. Every artboard is 1440 px wide and as tall as its content needs. Its background is surface.app (light) or dark surface.app (dark). Artboard names on this board follow \"00a · <Component> · <NN-state> · <light|dark>\": the component name takes the place of the house style's platform slot, because one specimen artboard shows all three platforms (this is recorded on Notes). Above the frame, print the exact artboard name from the ARTBOARDS manifest as a visible label in label 13/18/600 text.strong. Inside the frame, the top block is: the component name in h1 30/36/700 text.primary, its one-line purpose in body 16/24 text.secondary, then the \"Used in\" line in caption 12/16 text.secondary, printed exactly as this prompt gives it (a list of surface ids, or for OfflineNotice the sentence given there). Below that come the sections this prompt lists for that artboard, each with an overline 11/16/600 caps heading (for example \"ANATOMY\", \"VARIANT × STATE\", \"AX5 AND 200%\", \"GREYSCALE\", \"INCREASE CONTRAST\", \"ACCESSIBILITY\", \"COPY\", \"PLATFORMS\", \"IN CONTEXT\", \"INSTEAD OF\").\n\nB2. Specimen cells. Draw each specimen on a surface.base card (radius lg 12, shadow sm, 16 px padding) unless the cell says it sits on raised, sunken or app. Under each specimen, print a caption 12/16 text.secondary line naming the cell by its keys (B18), for example \"official · default · S 16pt · on surface.base\".\n\nB3. Callouts. Draw anatomy callouts as 1 px text.secondary leader lines ending in a numbered SQUARE badge (16×16, radius xs 4, surface.sunken fill, label 13/18/600 text.strong numeral). Next to each number, give the measurement and the token name in caption 12/16 text.strong, for example \"① 12pt disc · ink text.secondary\". Use square badges on purpose: circles and rings are reserved for ProvenanceMark (B8). Draw dimension lines as 1 px text.secondary with 4 px end ticks and the number centred on the line.\n\nB4. Units and sizes. Give every size three ways the first time it appears in a section: \"pt (iOS) / dp (Android) / px (web)\". The values are equal, for example \"16pt / 16dp / 16px\". Spacing, padding and gaps use only the 4-px spacing scale (4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64). Type uses only the type scale, plus the AX5 and 200% sizes listed in B9 and the one weight deviation recorded on Notes (KindGlyph's selected tile label). Other dimensions are allowed only where this prompt states them. These include: component sizes (12, 16, 24, 32, 42, 44, 48, 56), radio centres (8, 12), stroke widths (1, 1.5, 2, 3, 7), dash and gap lengths (2), the focus-ring gap (2), dimension-line end ticks (4), the hairline height (2), the OG mark minimum (28 px), the kind-picker cell (KindGlyph ④), the frame and crop widths (158, 175, 176, 186, 240, 320, 338, 358, 360, 390, 393, 412, 720, 1200, 1440) and heights (88, 158), plus any other dimension stated explicitly in a component section.\n\nB5. Tokens, by name. Label every colour ON THE BOARD by token name (text.secondary, surface.sunken, primary.700 and so on). On the board, hex values appear in only one place: the TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE on each 01-anatomy artboard. The hex values below are for you, not for specimen labels. Use this light-to-dark mapping for every dark artboard in this project:\n  surface.base #FFFFFF → dark surface.base #0F172A\n  surface.raised #F9FAFB → dark surface.raised #1E293B\n  surface.sunken #F3F4F6 → dark surface.sunken #0F172A (the same as dark base; see B6)\n  surface.app #F6F7F9 → dark surface.app #020617\n  surface.muted #F8FAFC → dark surface.muted #111827\n  text.primary #111827 → dark text.primary #E5E7EB\n  text.strong #374151 → dark text.strong #F1F5F9\n  text.secondary #6B7280 → dark text.secondary #94A3B8\n  text.muted #9CA3AF → dark text.muted #64748B (disabled controls and placeholders only)\n  border.default #E5E7EB → dark border.default #1F2937 (decoration only)\n  border.strong #D1D5DB → dark border.strong #374151 (decoration only)\n  border.focus #0284c7 → dark border.focus #38BDF8\n  primary.700 #0369a1 (links, selected text, selected edges) → the dark link colour, named on the board as \"primary.400 (dark link)\" (#38BDF8, the same value as dark border.focus). Wherever this prompt says \"primary.400 (dark link)\", it means this colour.\n  primary.500 #0ea5e9: used on this board only as the dark tinted-widget stand-in (ProvenanceMark). It fails 3:1 on light surfaces.\n  primary.50 #f0f9ff (selected fill) → dark selected fill primary.900 #0c4a6e, with dark text.primary on it (7.64:1). primary.400 (dark link) on primary.900 is 4.42:1, so use it there only for glyphs, never for 13 px text.\n  semantic.success #059669, semantic.warning #D97706 and semantic.error #DC2626 keep the same hue in dark mode and are used on glyphs only. semantic.info is #0284c7; this board stands primary.700 in for it (see StatusChip).\n\nB6. Chip fills in dark mode. Dark surface.sunken is the same colour as dark surface.base, so a sunken chip disappears on a dark base card. Where this prompt says a chip is filled with surface.sunken, use dark surface.sunken when the chip sits on dark surface.raised, and dark surface.raised when it sits on dark surface.base or dark surface.app. The glyph and the words carry the meaning, so the chip needs no border.\n\nB7. Contrast numbers, computed from the real tokens (WCAG 2 relative luminance, rounded to 2 decimals at the end). Where a colour is drawn at an opacity, it is first alpha-blended over its surface in sRGB with unrounded channel values, and the ratio is then taken against that surface. Print these on the relevant artboards; do not recompute them.\n  Light: text.secondary on base 4.83 · on raised 4.63 · on app 4.51 · on sunken 4.39 (below 4.5, so text on sunken uses text.strong) · text.strong on sunken 9.37 · on base 10.31 · primary.700 on base 5.93 · on raised 5.68 · on app 5.54 · on primary.50 5.57 · on sunken 5.39 · primary.500 on base 2.77 (FAILS 3:1; never a light tint) · primary.50 on base 1.07 (a fill, never an edge) · text.muted on base 2.54 (disabled only) · border.strong on base 1.47 (decoration only) · border.focus on base 4.10 · semantic.error on sunken 4.39 · semantic.success on sunken 3.42 · semantic.warning on sunken 2.89 (FAILS 3:1) · identity.home on sunken 2.99 (FAILS 3:1) · identity.home on base 3.30.\n  Dark: text.secondary on dark base 6.96 · on dark raised 5.71 · on dark app 7.87 · text.strong on dark raised 13.35 · on dark base 16.30 · text.muted on dark base 3.75 (disabled only) · primary.400 (dark link) on dark base 8.33 · on dark raised 6.83 · on dark app 9.42 · on primary.900 4.42 · primary.500 on dark raised 5.28 · primary.900 on dark base 1.89 (a fill, never an edge) · semantic.warning on dark raised 4.59 · semantic.success on dark raised 3.88 · semantic.error on dark raised 3.03 · on dark base 3.70 · border.strong on dark raised 1.42 (decoration only).\n  Stale mark (50% opacity): text.secondary at 50% on base is 1.98 (FAILS). text.primary at 50% is 3.39 on base, 3.36 on raised, 3.34 on app and 3.32 on sunken. Dark text.primary at 50% is 4.45 on dark base, 4.10 on dark raised and 4.48 on dark app. This is why ProvenanceMark's stale variant uses text.primary at 50% (see component 1). Tints at 50% fail: primary.700 at 50% on base is 2.24, and primary.500 at 50% on dark raised is 2.36, which is why the tinted widget is never dimmed (see component 1).\n\nB8. Circles are reserved. Only ProvenanceMark may draw a solid disc, a ring, or a disc with a knocked-out tick. This rule applies to a glyph's whole silhouette and to drawn standalone dots, bullets and badges: no other component, annotation, bullet, badge, status glyph or decoration uses a plain solid circle or plain ring as its shape. The typographic middle dot (·) in text is allowed; this rule covers drawn shapes only. Round sub-parts inside a larger glyph are fine (a person's head, cart wheels, a map pin's hole); draw them as parts, not as free-standing dots. Groups of dots inside a glyph are drawn as short dashes or small rounded squares. The only exceptions are platform radio indicators, in exactly two places, each flagged on Notes:\n  - KindGlyph's selected tile, on every platform: a ring with a filled centre in the tile corner. Unselected tiles show no indicator.\n  - Android Material 3 radio buttons in the 200% one-column lists (KindGlyph and ChoiceChip), where they are the platform control: a ring with a filled centre when selected, an empty ring when unselected.\n  On iOS (AX5) and web (200% zoom), the one-column lists use no ring at all: the selected row gets a trailing check stroke, as native iOS list selection does, and unselected rows get nothing.\n\nB9. Large text. AX5 frames (iOS) use these sizes: caption 12 → 40pt, label 13 → 44pt, bodySmall 14 → 46pt, body 16 → 53pt. Android 200% frames use caption 24sp, label 26sp, bodySmall 28sp, body 32sp. At both: pairs stack vertically, text wraps and never ends in an ellipsis, pills that must wrap become rounded rectangles (radius lg 12), and hit areas grow with the content. Glyphs and marks scale with the text beside them, capped at 2× their default size (XS 12 → 24, S 16 → 32, M 24 → 48; L 56 does not scale). Draw AX5 frames at 393 pt wide and 200% frames at 412 dp wide, cropped to the component and its row. Web 200% zoom frames are 390 px wide at 200% browser zoom, which is a 195 px effective viewport, so they always show the narrowest layout; where a component also needs its wide zoomed form, this prompt asks for a separate 1440-wide frame at 200% zoom (720 px effective), cropped to the component.\n\nB10. Greyscale. Each light 03 artboard includes a GREYSCALE section: the light variant × state grid again at 50% scale, fully desaturated (0% saturation). Two exceptions: ProvenanceMark's 03 does not redraw its grid, because its 02 grid already has a greyscale column (03 points to that column and adds the WRONG example), and KindGlyph's 03 shows a representative subset (the 17 row-variant glyphs plus the whole of Part B). Next to every cell, print either \"Reads without colour: yes — <the non-colour cue>\" or, where this prompt names a fail, the fail and its fix.\n\nB11. Fixtures. Use only the house-style FIXTURES and the strings quoted in this prompt. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific. Every relative time on this board is computed from that moment (for example, \"observed 7:00 AM\" is \"11 hours ago\"; Mon 26 Oct is \"in 7 days\"; Sat 10 Oct is \"9 days ago\"). Every date row on this board follows one format: the relative count first and then the weekday date (\"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"); \"Tonight\", \"Today\" and \"Tomorrow\" stand alone; a headline naming tomorrow's pickup may show the weekday date alone. Any string that is not in the house style and not quoted in this prompt must be listed on 00a · Notes.\n\nB12. Variant × state grids. Rows are the variants listed in this prompt, in the order given. Columns are the states listed in this prompt, in the order given. Draw every cell. Where this prompt says a cell \"does not apply\", draw the cell with an empty surface.base card and the words \"Does not apply — <reason>\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary. Where a row gives one reason for several cells, print that same reason in each of them. Do not leave any cell blank without text, and do not skip a row or column.\n\nB13. Targets. The minimum hit area is 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android (with 8dp gaps) and 44px on web. This prompt calls that size \"target (B13)\". Draw hit areas as a 1 px dashed text.secondary outline labelled \"target 44pt / 48dp / 44px\". Wherever a mark or glyph sits inside a row, also draw a small \"not a target\" label pointing at the mark.\n\nB14. Focus vs selection. Focus is always a 2 px border.focus ring (dark: dark border.focus) with a 2 px gap outside the control's shape. Selection is always a fill plus a glyph plus a visible edge where stated (and a weight or ink change where stated). Never show selection with a ring alone, and never show focus with a fill.\n\nB15. Motion. No component on this board animates, except the FreshnessLine hairline (component 4). That hairline is the platform's own system indeterminate progress indicator, with no custom duration; it is shown for at most 5s. It is exempt from the house style's 300ms limit because it is a progress indicator, not a transition, and it obeys the house style's \"idle loops stop within 5s\" instead (recorded on Notes). Where motion exists, draw its Reduce Motion pose and its end pose next to it.\n\nB16. Increase Contrast. Each 03 artboard (light, and ProvenanceMark's dark 03) has an INCREASE CONTRAST section: either a frame showing what changes, or the sentence \"Increase Contrast: nothing changes — <why>\". The general rule is that text.secondary ink becomes text.strong (dark: dark text.strong); text.muted on disabled controls stays text.muted, because the disabled reason caption carries the meaning. Each component section below states its own result.\n\nB17. Air readings and the AQI track. Air rows on this board (ProvenanceMark R5, SourceCaption R2 and its in-context crop, FreshnessLine R5, OfflineNotice R1) show the value line and caption only. The AQI track belongs to AqiBand, which is not on this board, so no EPA ColorVision Assist hue appears anywhere here and no text ever sits on an AQI fill. Label one air crop \"track omitted: AqiBand\".\n\nB18. Keys. Every grid row and every grid column carries a short printed key: lowercase, hyphenated, with no \"/\" and no spaces, printed in caption 12/16 text.secondary as \"key: <key>\" under its label. Row and column labels may be longer and may quote fixture strings, but the key never contains a fixture string or a date. The keys for each grid are listed in that component's section. The publish names on Notes (section E) use only these keys.\n\n======================================================================\n1. ProvenanceMark\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01, 02, 03 and 04, each in light and dark (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE (print this line): The only way the product says how sure it is about a fact: three shapes, one meaning each, used everywhere.\n\nUsed in (print this list): x-provenance-sheet, x-date-sheet, x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet, f7-widget-tap-landing, f1-today-tab, f3-household-calendar, f3-household-notifications, f8-scale-strips, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-sheet, f8-og-compare-card, f8-seasonal-aha, f6-place-section-details, f10-extraction-confirm, f10-bill-provenance, f10-bill-trend, f10-mail-day-triage, f11-keeper-strip, f1-claim-receipt.\n\nANATOMY (on 01-anatomy; draw each silhouette at L 56pt with callouts, then all four sizes in a row)\n- OFFICIAL: a solid disc. Diameter equals the size.\n- UNCONFIRMED: a ring with the same outer diameter and a transparent centre. Stroke width: XS 12 → 1.5px, S 16 → 2px, M 24 → 3px, L 56 → 7px. Never thinner than 1.5px.\n- YOU ADDED: a solid disc with a tick KNOCKED OUT of it. The tick is a true cut-out, so the surface behind shows through. It is not a second colour painted on top. The tick spans the middle 56% of the diameter, and its stroke width equals the ring stroke for that size (XS 1.5, S 2, M 3, L 7), with round caps and joins. Draw it this way so the shape survives one-colour tinting.\n- Ink: text.secondary (4.83:1 on base) or darker in light mode, and dark text.secondary in dark mode. Show a crossed-out swatch row labelled \"never border.* · never text.muted\" (border.default is 1.24:1, text.muted is 2.54:1).\n- Sizes, each with its use printed under it:\n  XS 12pt/dp/px: the smallest size at which the three shapes can still be told apart (strip cells, widget, tray previews).\n  S 16pt: list rows and captions.\n  M 24pt: the sheet legend.\n  L 56pt: the provenance sheet header.\n  OG 28px at 1200 wide: the share card minimum.\n- Below 12pt, no mark is drawn. Show a row at \"10pt → no mark\" where the row prints the words instead: \"Pickup day · Thursday · On record, not confirmed\".\n- Spacing: 8pt (spacing.2) between the mark and its text. Show it with a dimension line.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.secondary #6B7280 4.83:1 on base; dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96:1 on dark base and 5.71:1 on dark raised; text.primary #111827 at 50% 3.39:1 on base (stale); dark text.primary #E5E7EB at 50% 4.45:1 on dark base (stale); tinted widget: primary.700 #0369a1 on surface.base 5.93:1 (light) and primary.500 #0ea5e9 on dark surface.raised 5.28:1 (dark), never dimmed (at 50% they drop to 2.24:1 and 2.36:1); primary.500 on surface.base 2.77:1 (never); border.default 1.24:1 (never); text.muted 2.54:1 (never).\n- LEGEND specimen (print it on 01-anatomy at M 24pt, stacked): [drawn official mark] \"Official\" · [drawn unconfirmed mark] \"On record, not confirmed\" · [drawn you-added mark] \"You added this\". The same legend is often written as \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\". The ●, ○ and ✓ characters stand for the DRAWN marks; always render the vector mark, never a font character.\n- 01-anatomy · dark carries the three silhouettes, the size row, the legend and the token and contrast table in dark tokens. It does not repeat the ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS or INSTEAD OF blocks.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (on 02-variants-states; 6 rows × 5 columns; each cell is a 358-wide row at S 16pt on surface.base, except where stated)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · stale (dimmed + age words) → stale · inside tap target → in-target · tinted/accented widget rendering (silhouette only) → tinted-widget · greyscale → greyscale.\nRows (label → key). Row content is used in every column of that row, except where a column rule below says otherwise:\n R1 official (filled) → official: \"Flood zone\" / \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\", caption \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\".\n R2 unconfirmed (hollow) → unconfirmed: \"Pickup day\" / \"Thursday\", caption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" (Place B).\n R3 you-added (filled + knocked-out tick) → you-added: \"Warranty ends\" / \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\", caption \"You added this\" (Home A).\n R4 read-from-your-photo → read-from-photo: a pre-commit machine read. Draw it with the UNCONFIRMED ring. Row \"Clark Public Utilities\" / \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". Under the uncertain value only (the due date), add the flag line \"We weren't sure — check this\" in caption 12/16 text.strong with a 12pt text.strong pencil glyph (not a circle). Beside the cell, draw a small arrow to a copy of the row after commit, where the mark becomes YOU ADDED, labelled \"on commit → you-added\".\n R5 stale → stale: the same shape as the fact's own provenance (draw the official disc for air), at 50% opacity of text.primary (3.39:1). Row \"Air quality\" / \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17), paired with the FreshnessLine words \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\" in caption text.secondary.\n R6 reported → reported: shape unchanged (draw the unconfirmed ring for the Place B pickup row), plus a status line under the row: \"You reported this · checking\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary, with no glyph.\nColumn rules:\n - default: as above.\n - stale: dim the mark to text.primary at 50% and replace the caption with that row's own stale caption. The dimming is never the only cue; the age words always appear. Per row:\n   R1: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   R2: dimmed ring, caption \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\".\n   R3: Does not apply — your own entry does not age.\n   R4: Does not apply — a pre-commit read is not refreshed.\n   R5: print \"same as stale variant\" (R5 is already stale).\n   R6: dimmed ring, the R2 stale caption, and the \"You reported this · checking\" line under it.\n - inside tap target: draw the whole row at 44pt min height (iOS) with the dashed target (B13) around the row and a \"not a target\" label on the mark. Add \"48dp on Android · 44px on web\".\n - tinted-widget: draw the row at XS 12pt inside a 158×158 widget crop rendered in a single accent hue. Light cell: widget background surface.base, tint primary.700, labelled \"system tint stand-in · 5.93:1\". (primary.500 is not used in light mode: 2.77:1 on white.) All three silhouettes are one colour. The YOU ADDED tick stays a transparent cut-out that shows the widget background. Print the provenance word next to every mark, because a widget is a standalone surface.\n   R5 tinted-widget: no dimming under tinted rendering. Draw the full-strength tint (5.93:1 light, 5.28:1 dark) and let the age words \"— 11 hours ago\" carry the stale state. Label it \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\".\n - greyscale: the default cell at 0% saturation, labelled \"shape carries the meaning\".\nDark twin (02-variants-states · dark): the same 30 cells using the dark tokens (B5). The tinted column uses widget background dark surface.raised with tint primary.500, labelled \"system tint stand-in · 5.28:1\"; its R5 cell follows the same no-dimming rule.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (on 03-scaling-greyscale)\n- AX5 (iOS 393 wide): R1, R2 and R3 stacked. The mark scales with Dynamic Type relative to the caption style, capped at 32pt. The row text wraps. The mark top-aligns to the first line. The legend becomes one entry per line.\n- 200% (Android 412 wide): the same three rows with sp scaling, mark capped at 32dp.\n- Web at 200% browser zoom (390 wide, B9): the same, with the SVG sized in em.\n- XS legibility strip: the three marks at XS 12pt on surface.base, surface.sunken, dark surface.base and dark surface.raised, plus the two tinted-widget backgrounds from the grid, labelled \"must be told apart at 12pt\".\n- GREYSCALE (B10 exception): do not redraw the grid. Print \"Greyscale: see the greyscale column on 02-variants-states — every cell reads yes — shape\". Draw one deliberate FAIL example, labelled \"WRONG\": two discs that differ only in hue. Its fix label reads \"fix: shape, not colour\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: the three marks in text.strong (light), labelled \"Increase Contrast ink\".\nDark twin (03 · dark): the AX5 and 200% frames in dark tokens, the XS strip, and the three marks in dark text.strong labelled \"Increase Contrast ink\". It omits the web zoom frame and the greyscale pointer, because greyscale does not depend on theme.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Spoken names are fixed: \"official\", \"on record, not confirmed\", \"you added this\". The name is appended to the row's merged label. Examples:\n  \"Flood zone, Zone X, minimal flood hazard, FEMA, official\"\n  \"Pickup day Thursday, City of Camas, on record, not confirmed\"\n  \"Warranty ends, water heater, in 54 days, Saturday 12 December, you added this\"\n- Non-colour encoding: the shape. Colour is never used to tell the marks apart.\n- Target rule: the mark is never a tap target on its own. The enclosing row or cell is the target (B13).\n- Contrast: at least 3:1 in both themes, including the tinted widget (see B7).\n- Scaling: with Dynamic Type or sp up to AX5 / 200%.\n- Each surface shows a legend or a first-occurrence word once.\n\nCOPY (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Legend strings, exactly: \"Official\" · \"On record, not confirmed\" · \"You added this\".\n- Print the word next to the mark once per surface. On standalone surfaces (widget, OG card, push landing), print it next to every mark.\n- In a push, the caveat goes at the front of the title: \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\".\n- Glossary: never \"verified\", \"confirmed\" or \"trusted\" for official data; never \"unverified\", \"estimated\", \"guessed\", \"pending\" or \"probable\" for the hollow mark; never \"user-entered\", \"self-reported\" or \"manual\" for the tick.\n\nPLATFORMS (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- iOS widgets: the mark is widgetAccentable, and the tick stays knocked out under accented rendering.\n- Android widgets: fixed ink (text.secondary / dark text.secondary), not a Material dynamic colour role.\n- Web: inline SVG with role=\"img\" and an aria-label holding the spoken name.\n- OG card: at least 28px at 1200 wide.\n\nIN CONTEXT (on 04-in-context; three 390-wide crops, each labelled with its surface id; dark twin on 04 · dark with the same three crops)\n a) x-place-file, Place B: a legend strip at the top (\"Official · On record, not confirmed · You added this\" with drawn M-size marks), then rows: \"Flood zone · Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" (official), \"Radon zone · Zone 1 — highest potential\" (official, caption \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\"), \"Pickup day · Thursday\" (unconfirmed), \"Pickup frequency · Not set\" (no mark, because nothing is on record).\n b) f5-today-calendar-strip, Home A. At the top of the crop, above the strip, a legend line: [drawn official mark] \"Official\" · [drawn unconfirmed mark] \"On record, not confirmed\" · [drawn you-added mark] \"You added this\", with the marks at S 16pt, labelled \"legend once per surface\". Then a 14-cell FourteenDayStrip from Mon 19 Oct to Sun 1 Nov with marks at XS 12pt, one ink colour. Draw every fixture date in the window:\n   Tue 20 Oct: unconfirmed ring (recycling and garbage, city schedule).\n   Fri 23 Oct: you-added mark (Clark Public Utilities bill).\n   Mon 26 Oct: voter registration, a statewide rule, drawn as a full-height bar spanning the cell, with no mark. Label it \"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\".\n   Tue 27 Oct: unconfirmed ring (garbage only).\n   Wed 28 Oct: you-added mark (City of Vancouver water bill).\n   Sun 1 Nov: you-added mark (HOA dues).\n   All other cells are empty. No cell holds more than 3 marks; print the rule \"at most 3 marks per cell, then +N\" beside the strip.\n Under the strip, draw the matching rows at S 16pt, each with its mark:\n   \"Recycling and garbage\" / \"Tomorrow\" (unconfirmed)\n   \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18\" / \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" (you added)\n   \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" / \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (official)\n   \"Garbage only\" / \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\" (unconfirmed)\n   \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00\" / \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\" (you added)\n   \"HOA dues · $285\" / \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\" (you added)\n Label: \"the strip is one element; rows are the targets\".\n c) f7-today-widget, 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\": marks at XS 12pt, each with its word printed beside it (\"On record, not confirmed\" next to \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\").\n\nINSTEAD OF (print on 01-anatomy · light)\n- Instead of filled vs hollow for any other meaning (sender vs you in compare, taken vs open founding slots, density), draw those with labelled pointers, or with solid vs hatched segments plus a numeral — because filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else.\n- Instead of a confidence percentage, bar or star, draw one of the three marks plus its word — because the product never grades certainty.\n- Instead of a hollow mark on an official public dataset (EPA radon zone, USFS wildfire hazard), draw the filled mark and put the limit in the caption's scope word (\"county-wide estimate\") — because hollow means \"not confirmed\", not \"coarse\".\n- Instead of a tick painted in a second colour on top of the disc, knock the tick out — because a second colour disappears under one-colour widget tinting.\n- Instead of a light tinted widget in primary.500, use primary.700 on surface.base — because primary.500 is 2.77:1 on white and marks need 3:1.\n- Instead of dimming a tinted widget mark for stale, keep the full tint and add the age words — because a dimmed tint drops below 3:1.\n- Instead of making an 8px dot the tap target, make the enclosing row or cell the target (B13) — because a small mark cannot be hit reliably.\n- Instead of a bare \"Unverified\" suffix on every row, show the word once per surface in a legend — because repetition becomes noise and \"unverified\" is a forbidden term.\n- Instead of text.secondary at 50% for stale, use text.primary at 50% — because the first drops to 1.98:1.\n- Instead of one age suffix on every row, give each fact its own stale caption — because an effective date or your own entry does not age.\n\n======================================================================\n2. SourceCaption\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: Puts the minimum provenance on the value itself: who says it, what it covers, and when.\nUsed in: f8-scale-strips, f6-place-section-details, f1-today-air-band, f8-seasonal-aha, f8-compare-arrival-header, f8-compare-reveal, f8-og-compare-card, f8-compare-sheet, x-provenance-sheet, x-place-file, f4-today-pickup-card, f5-today-calendar-strip, f3-household-calendar, f10-bill-trend.\nPrint this rationale under the purpose: \"Almost nobody opens the provenance sheet, so the caption carries the caveat.\"\n\nANATOMY (callouts on a 358-wide specimen: \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\" with the external-link glyph)\n- ① ProvenanceMark S 16pt, leading, top-aligned to the first line, 8pt gap.\n- ② Authority, ③ \" · \" separator, ④ scope word, ⑤ \" · \", ⑥ as-of. All in caption 12/16/400.\n- Ink: text.secondary on base, raised or app surfaces; text.strong on sunken (text.secondary on sunken is 4.39:1). Draw two copies side by side, on base and on sunken, labelled with their tokens and ratios.\n- It wraps to two lines at default size and never truncates the authority with an ellipsis. Draw a 240-wide wrap example: \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\".\n- ⑦ Optional trailing external-link glyph (12pt, arrow out of a square, not a circle), shown only when a source URL exists. When a URL exists, the authority word is primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)) with an underline, and the caption line's hit area is a target (B13). When no URL exists, everything is text.secondary, with no underline, no glyph, and no target.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.secondary #6B7280 4.83 base / 4.63 raised / 4.51 app; text.strong #374151 9.37 on sunken; primary.700 #0369a1 5.93 on base; primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 8.33 on dark base; dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (6 rows × 3 columns; each cell shows the value line in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary above the caption)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · stale (the as-of age appended) → stale · offline (\"as of\" date) → offline.\n R1 dated static → dated-static. Value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n   default \"FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\"\n   stale: Does not apply — an effective date does not age.\n   offline: unchanged; draw the default caption and label it \"static captions do not change offline\".\n R2 live → live. Value \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17).\n   default \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today\"\n   stale \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM today — 11 hours ago\"\n   offline \"AirNow · nearest monitors · as of 7:00 AM\"\n R3 frozen token (a compare card's saved reading) → frozen. Value \"AQI 42 · Good\".\n   default \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\"\n   stale: Does not apply — a frozen reading is dated, never \"ago\".\n   offline: unchanged; label as in R1.\n R4 county scope → county. Value \"Zone 1 — highest potential\".\n   default \"EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\"\n   stale: Does not apply — a county zone does not age.\n   offline: unchanged.\n R5 collapsed sources line, only at 320–360 wide → collapsed. Draw it in a 320-wide cell under four value rows (Flood, Wildfire, Air, Radon).\n   default \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\". The air row keeps its own time on its row: \"observed 7:00 AM today\".\n   stale: the sources line is unchanged; only the air row appends \"— 11 hours ago\".\n   offline: the sources line is unchanged; the air row reads \"as of 7:00 AM\".\n R6 no URL: a flat caption, not tappable → no-url. Value \"Thursday\" (Place B pickup day).\n   default \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\", with no glyph and no underline, labelled \"not a target\".\n   stale: Does not apply — the schedule is dated by its as-of, which is already shown.\n   offline: unchanged.\nNext to R1, also draw a \"with URL\" twin (key: dated-static-link), default state only, showing the underlined authority and trailing glyph, so the difference between R1 and R6 is visible.\nDark twin: all 18 cells and the twin in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5: R2 and R4 at caption 40pt with the mark at 32pt, wrapping to as many lines as needed and never ending in an ellipsis.\n- 200%: the same at 24sp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the same.\n- GREYSCALE per B10. The link is still identifiable by its underline and glyph: \"yes — underline + glyph\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R2 default with the caption in text.strong; the link stays primary.700 with its underline.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Contrast is at least 4.5:1 (see the table).\n- It is read after the value in the row's merged label: \"Air quality, AQI 42, Good, AirNow, nearest monitors, observed 7:00 AM today, official\".\n- The non-colour cue for a link is the underline plus the external-link glyph.\n- Target rule: a caption is a target (B13) only when a URL exists. A caption with no URL is never a target.\n- There is no hover-only content.\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Always authority · scope · as-of.\n- Use the authority's own word, \"hazard\" or \"potential\"; never \"risk\" unless the source says risk.\n- Deadlines received by a date say \"must arrive by\" (\"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\").\n- Never write \"Sources:\" at widths above 360.\n- Never write \"provider\", \"feed\" or \"partner\" for the source.\n- Never label a frozen reading \"today\".\n\nPLATFORMS (01)\n- Same on iOS, Android and web.\n- On the OG image, the caption is at least 28px and may be merged into one sources line; the full captions go in og:description. Draw a 1200-wide strip crop showing \"Sources: FEMA, USFS, AirNow, EPA\" at 28px.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three 390-wide crops)\n a) f8-scale-strips: the flood row \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" with the R1 caption under the strip.\n b) f1-today-air-band, Place B: \"AQI 42 · Good\" with the R2 caption. Add an alert-variant copy: \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\" with \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 4:00 PM today\". Both crops show the value line and caption only; label them \"track omitted: AqiBand\" (B17).\n c) f8-compare-arrival-header, Friend C: \"Dana · Camas, WA\" card with \"Air on Sat 12 Sep\" and the R3 caption \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\".\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of hiding the source behind a tooltip or \"learn more\", print authority · scope · as-of on the value — because almost nobody opens the sheet.\n- Instead of labelling a frozen reading \"today\", write \"on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" — because a shared card is read days later.\n- Instead of making a caption with no URL tappable, draw it flat — because a target that goes nowhere breaks trust.\n- Instead of \"Sources:\" on wide layouts, give every row its own caption — because the collapsed line exists only for 320–360 widths.\n- Instead of ellipsising a long authority, wrap to a second line — because the authority is the caveat.\n\n======================================================================\n3. ScopeChip\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: States who can see this address data, only you or your household, on every surface that shows address data.\nUsed in: f1-today-tab, f1-today-air-band, f1-your-places, f1-add-place-sheet, f1-save-confirmation, f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-claim-receipt, x-date-sheet, x-place-file, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-widget-tap-landing, f9-privacy-mirror, f11-keeper-naming, f11-keeper-strip, f3-household-notifications, f10-mail-day-triage, f10-snap-capture-tray, f10-mail-snap-privacy, f10-mail-piece-photo.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on \"Saved place · Only you\" and \"Your household\")\n- ① Pill, radius pill, height 24pt/dp/px.\n- ② Horizontal padding 8 (spacing.2) and a 4 (spacing.1) gap between glyph and label.\n- ③ A 12pt glyph: person = Only you; house = household. It is a line glyph with a 1.5px stroke in text.strong. The house glyph may use identity.home only if it reaches 3:1, and on surface.sunken identity.home is 2.99:1, so draw it in text.strong and print \"identity.home fails 3:1 on sunken (2.99) → text.strong\".\n- ④ Label in label 13/18/600, text.strong (9.37:1 on sunken). The \" · \" separator is a typographic middle dot with a space on each side.\n- ⑤ Fill surface.sunken, with no border.\n- ⑥ Hit area: a target (B13) only when the chip opens the control that changes scope. Draw both a \"label only, no target\" copy and an \"opens scope control\" copy with the dashed target and a trailing 12pt chevron in text.strong.\n- Footer sentence form (used in sheets): a 16pt glyph and a sentence in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary on base, with no pill.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37; identity.home #16A34A on sunken 2.99 (not used); text.secondary #6B7280 on base 4.83; dark text.strong #F1F5F9 on dark raised 13.35.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (5 rows × 4 columns)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · pending share (dashed house glyph) → pending · declined share (person → person) → declined · struck (old scope on the claim receipt) → struck.\n R1 saved place → saved-place: \"Saved place · Only you\" with the person glyph.\n   default: as specified.\n   pending and declined: Does not apply — pending and declined exist only in the scope-change pair (R4).\n   struck: the chip with a 1px text.strong strike line through the label, followed by a 4pt gap, a 12pt arrow glyph, another 4pt gap and a \"Your household\" chip, captioned \"old scope on the claim receipt\". The strike is never the only cue: the new chip is always beside it.\n R2 claimed home → claimed-home: \"Your household\" with the house glyph.\n   default: as specified. pending, declined and struck: Does not apply — a claimed home's chip has no pending share or older scope of its own.\n R3 named home (multi-home contexts) → named-home: \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\" with the house glyph.\n   default: as specified. pending, declined and struck: Does not apply — same reason as R2.\n R4 scope-change pair (claim receipt, trailing edge of a carried row) → scope-change-pair: glyph-only, 12pt person glyph → 12pt arrow → 12pt house glyph, in text.strong. Show it on a row \"Warranty ends · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\".\n   default: person → house, both solid lines (shared).\n   pending share: person → house with the house drawn in a DASHED 1.5px stroke (2px dash, 2px gap), shown until the user chooses. Under the row, the consent question \"Share the 2 dates you entered with Sam?\" and two equal-weight buttons, \"Share with the household\" and \"Keep them private to me\" (glossary tension flagged on Notes).\n   declined share: person → person (both solid).\n   struck: Does not apply — the pair itself shows the change.\n R5 footer sentence form (sheets) → footer-sentence:\n   default: two copies, person glyph + \"Only you will see this.\" and house glyph + \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\n   pending, declined and struck: Does not apply — the sentence describes the current scope only.\nDark twin: all 20 cells in dark tokens, using the chip fill rule from B6.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5: R1 and R3 at label 44pt. The chip wraps to two lines and becomes a rounded rectangle (radius lg 12) with the glyph (scaled to 24pt) top-aligned. The height grows to fit. Nothing is truncated.\n- 200%: the same at 26sp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the same.\n- GREYSCALE per B10: \"yes — glyph + words\". The dashed house reads as dashed.\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: the chip is unchanged (it is already text.strong); the R5 footer sentence becomes text.strong.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Spoken: \"Visible to only you\" (R1), \"Visible to your household\" (R2, R3; R3 is prefixed with \"Larkspur Loop,\"). Pair, pending: \"Visible to only you; will be visible to your household if you share\". Pair, declined: \"Visible to only you\". Pair, default: \"Visible to your household\".\n- Never colour-only: the glyph plus the words.\n- Target rule: a target (B13) only when it opens the scope control; otherwise it is not a target.\n- It wraps at AX sizes.\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Exactly these chip strings: \"Saved place · Only you\" and \"Your household\" (with an optional leading home label, as in \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\").\n- Exactly these sentences: \"Only you will see this.\" and \"Everyone in this household will see this.\"\n- Draw a crossed-out \"Retired wording\" list: \"Only you see this\" · \"Only you can see these\" · \"private to your home\" · \"Saved place - Only you\" (hyphen instead of a middle dot).\n- A saved place never uses the words home, household or claim.\n- Where finance permissions differ, name the people instead: \"You and Sam can see these photos\".\n\nPLATFORMS (01)\n- Identical on iOS, Android and web.\n- On push landings, it sits next to the address in the location row.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three 390-wide crops)\n a) f1-today-tab, Place B: the location row \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" with \"Saved place · Only you\" beside it (wrapping under it if the row is too narrow), and the FreshnessLine \"Updated 12m ago\" below.\n b) x-date-sheet, Home A: the sheet title \"Add a date\" at the top of the crop, then (with the sheet body cropped between) the footer sentence \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" directly above the sheet's primary button \"Save\".\n c) f1-claim-receipt, Home A: the header with the struck \"Saved place · Only you\" → \"Your household\", then two carried rows with pending pairs and the consent block from R4.\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of a green \"verified-looking\" chip to mean membership, draw the neutral sunken chip with the house glyph — because green reads as verification, which is a different thing.\n- Instead of dropping the chip from an alert landing, keep it next to the address — because an alert is when people most need to know who else sees it.\n- Instead of \"Everyone in this household\" where finance permissions differ, name the people (\"You and Sam can see these photos\") — because the sentence would be false.\n- Instead of an identity.home fill, use surface.sunken with text.strong — because the colour is not the message and fails contrast on sunken.\n- Instead of any new wording, use the two chip strings and two sentences — because five earlier wordings drifted.\n\n======================================================================\n4. FreshnessLine\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: One persistent line that states how old the content is: refresh, stale and offline all go here instead of a toast.\nUsed in: f1-today-tab, f7-widget-tap-landing, f7-today-widget, f1-today-air-band, x-place-file, f9-invite-rewards-card, f9-nearby-cells-map, f11-keeper-strip, f10-bill-trend, f3-bills-list, f3-members-roster, f1-your-places.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on a card header \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" + \"Saved place · Only you\", with the line under it)\n- ① Placement: directly under the location row or card header, 4pt (spacing.1) below it.\n- ② Caption 12/16/400 in text.secondary (text.strong on sunken).\n- ③ Optional leading 16pt glyph: offline (a cloud with a slash) or retry (a circular arrow drawn as an open arc with an arrowhead, not a closed ring), in text.secondary, with an 8pt gap.\n- ④ Optional 2pt indeterminate hairline under the header, full card width, primary.700 (5.93:1 on base; at least 3:1 on its surface). It is the platform's own system indeterminate progress indicator (iOS linear ProgressView, Android M3 LinearProgressIndicator, web an indeterminate progress bar), tinted primary.700, with no custom duration or easing. It runs only if the refresh takes 1s or longer. Draw three poses side by side:\n   running: a short segment partway along the track, with the note \"system indeterminate progress indicator · no custom duration · exempt from the 300ms rule, stopped within 5s (see Notes)\".\n   after 5s: the hairline stops and is removed; \"Updating…\" stays in the line until the result arrives, then the line becomes \"Updated just now\" or the failed line (R3). Label it \"idle loops stop within 5s\".\n   Reduce Motion: no hairline at all; the word \"Updating…\" carries the state.\n- ⑤ \"Retry\" is an inline text button in label 13/18/600 primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)), with a target (B13) drawn dashed.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.secondary #6B7280 4.83 on base; text.strong #374151 9.37 on sunken; primary.700 #0369a1 5.93 on base; primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 6.83 on dark raised.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (6 rows × 5 columns; each cell is the 358-wide header plus line from the anatomy)\nColumns (label → key): fresh → fresh · refreshing → refreshing · stale → stale · failed → failed · offline → offline.\nEach variant exists in exactly one state. Draw that one cell as described, and fill the row's other four cells with \"Does not apply — this line appears only while <that state>\" (B12).\n Variant → state map (row label → key → state):\n R1 \"Updating…\" → updating → refreshing. Draw two sub-cells, \"under 1s: no hairline\" and \"1s or longer: hairline\".\n R2 \"Updated just now\" / \"Updated 12m ago\" / \"Updated 2h ago\" (the system relative date) → updated → fresh, all three strings stacked as specimen text. In the stale cell, print the reason \"Does not apply — stale is stated per fact (R5)\".\n R3 \"Couldn't refresh · Retry\" → failed → failed, with the retry glyph and the Retry target.\n R4 \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" → offline → offline, with the offline glyph.\n R5 per-fact stale: \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\", placed under the air row (B17), not the header → fact-stale → stale. The rest of the card stays undimmed.\n R6 widget past horizon: \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\", in a 338×158 widget crop → widget-horizon → stale. (The time is today's, so no weekday is shown.)\nBeside the grid, draw a \"what does not change\" strip: the same card in fresh and refreshing states with identical layout, labelled \"no dim, no skeleton, no reflow while refreshing\".\nDark twin: all 30 cells in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5: R3 and R4 at caption 40pt. The line wraps, and \"Retry\" moves to its own line as a full-width 44pt text button. The glyph scales to 32pt.\n- 200%: the same at 24sp, with the button at 48dp.\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the same.\n- GREYSCALE per B10: \"yes — words state the state\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R3 and R4 with the line and glyph in text.strong; Retry stays primary.700.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Changes are announced in a polite live region, never an assertive one (iOS UIAccessibility announcement with polite priority; Android accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"; web aria-live=\"polite\").\n- Non-colour: stale is stated in words.\n- Target rule: Retry is a target (B13).\n- Ageing text is announced once, not every minute.\n- Spoken example: \"You're offline, as of 7:04 AM\".\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Relative time for recency (\"Updated 12m ago\"). \"As of\" plus an absolute time for offline or frozen data (\"as of 7:04 AM\"); add the weekday only when the time is not today.\n- Never \"Last synced\", \"refreshed at\" or \"last seen\".\n- Never a disappearing toast as the only proof.\n\nPLATFORMS (01)\n- iOS widgets use the system Text(date, style: .relative).\n- Android widgets use the equivalent system relative-time text.\n- The hairline is each platform's system indeterminate progress indicator.\n- Web: a polite live region.\n- Same wording everywhere.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three crops)\n a) f1-today-tab, Place B, 390 wide: the location row, the ScopeChip, \"Updated 12m ago\", and then the air row with R5 beneath it only when stale.\n b) f7-today-widget, 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\", with R6. The rest of the widget stays at full ink; only the stated line changes.\n c) f3-bills-list, Home A, web 390: the header \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills · 3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" with \"Updated just now\" under it.\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of dimming, skeletoning or reflowing a warm screen while refreshing, keep it and show \"Updating…\" (and the hairline after 1s) — because stale content is still useful.\n- Instead of a hairline that loops until the request ends, stop it at 5s and leave \"Updating…\" — because idle loops stop within 5s.\n- Instead of a custom animated hairline, use the platform's system indeterminate indicator — because a custom loop is a motion spec nobody needs to maintain.\n- Instead of greying a whole widget when only AQI is old, put the age words on the air line — because the other facts are still current.\n- Instead of a toast, use this line — because toasts vanish before people read them.\n- Instead of \"Last synced\", write \"Updated\" or \"As of\" — because \"synced\" is jargon.\n\n======================================================================\n5. OfflineNotice\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: One pattern for no connection: cached content stays readable, and actions are disabled with a stated reason.\nUsed in: print exactly \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\" as the used-in line; do not list ids.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on a 390-wide Today crop for Place B)\n- ① FreshnessLine in its offline variant at the top: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\".\n- ② Cached content at full ink (not dimmed).\n- ③ A disabled control, e.g. the secondary button \"Compare with a friend\": label in text.muted on surface.sunken (disabled is the one allowed use of text.muted), 44pt tall.\n- ④ A reason caption directly under that control, 4pt below: \"Compare needs a connection.\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary (4.83:1).\n- ⑤ Background: no banner colour. Either plain (on base or app) or a surface.sunken strip with text.strong. Draw both and label them.\n- ⑥ The disabled control keeps a focus ring when focused (B14), showing that it stays focusable.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.secondary #6B7280 4.83; text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37; text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled label only); dark text.secondary #94A3B8 6.96.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (3 rows × 3 columns; each cell is a 390-wide crop; all 9 cells apply)\nColumns (label → key): offline → offline · reconnecting → reconnecting · back online (the line reverts to FreshnessLine) → back-online.\n R1 read-only cached screen → cached-screen (f1-today-tab, Place B: air row \"AQI 42 · Good\" (value line only, B17), the \"Compare with a friend\" button).\n   offline: as in the anatomy.\n   reconnecting: the line reads \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\"; the button is still disabled with its reason.\n   back online: the line reads \"Updating…\" and then \"Updated just now\" (draw both as two sub-cells); the button is enabled and the reason caption is gone.\n R2 queued writes → queued-writes (f10-snap-capture-tray, Home A, three mail-snap thumbnails).\n   offline: the line \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" and under it \"You're offline. You can keep taking photos.\"; each thumbnail has the caption \"Will upload when you're back online\".\n   reconnecting: the line reads \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\"; the thumbnails keep their captions.\n   back online: the live status line \"Uploading 1 of 3\"; the thumbnail captions disappear one by one (draw the moment after the first upload).\n R3 form offline → form (f1-add-place-sheet, signed in): a disabled address field with the message \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.strong on a surface.sunken strip above the field. The sheet keeps a visible \"Close\".\n   offline: as described.\n   reconnecting: the same message, with \"Reconnecting\" as a caption under it.\n   back online: the field is enabled and the message is gone. No FreshnessLine appears, because a form has no content age; note this on the cell.\nDark twin: all 9 cells in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5: R1 offline. The line wraps, the button goes full width, and the reason caption wraps under it at 40pt.\n- 200%: the same.\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the same.\n- GREYSCALE per B10: \"yes — words; disabled is stated, not only greyed\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R1 offline with the reason caption in text.strong; the disabled label stays text.muted, because the reason caption carries the meaning (B16).\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Disabled controls stay focusable and read their reason:\n  iOS: \"Compare with a friend, dimmed, Compare needs a connection.\"\n  Android: \"Compare with a friend, disabled, Compare needs a connection.\"\n  Web: aria-disabled=\"true\" (not the disabled attribute) with aria-describedby pointing at the reason caption.\n- Status changes are announced politely.\n- Target rule: the disabled control keeps its target size (B13).\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Start with \"You're offline.\" and then say what still works.\n- Exact strings: \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Compare needs a connection.\" · \"Will upload when you're back online\" · \"You're offline. We can't look up an address right now.\"\n- Never \"No internet\", \"Connection lost\" or \"Network error\".\n\nPLATFORMS (01): the same on iOS, Android and web.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three crops)\n a) f8-native-share-compare, iOS 393: \"Compare with a friend\" disabled with \"Compare needs a connection.\"\n b) f1-add-place-sheet, Android 412: R3 offline.\n c) f10-snap-capture-tray, iOS 393: R2 offline.\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of a full-page offline illustration, keep the cached screen readable with the offline line on top — because people still need what they already had.\n- Instead of silent dead buttons, disable the control and put the reason under it — because a button that does nothing looks broken.\n- Instead of a red or amber banner, use plain or surface.sunken with text.strong — because being offline is a condition, not an error.\n- Instead of blanking stale data, keep it with \"as of 7:04 AM\" — because a blank throws away true information.\n\n======================================================================\n6. StatusChip\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: One status per object (bills and invites), stated in words.\nUsed in: f3-bills-list, f3-bill-detail-web, f3-members-roster, f8-seasonal-aha, f10-bill-provenance, f9-block-founders-panel.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on \"Overdue\")\n- ① Pill, radius pill, height 24pt/dp/px.\n- ② Padding 8 horizontal, 4 gap.\n- ③ A leading 12pt glyph, the only place a semantic hue may appear. No glyph is a plain circle or ring (B8).\n- ④ Text in captionMedium 12/16/500, text.strong.\n- ⑤ Fill surface.sunken (dark: rule B6). No border by default.\n- The chip is not a target; its row is.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.strong #374151 on sunken 9.37; semantic.error #DC2626 on sunken 4.39; semantic.success #059669 on sunken 3.42; semantic.warning #D97706 on sunken 2.89 (fails, so light mode uses text.strong for warning glyphs); primary.700 #0369a1 on sunken 5.39; semantic.warning on dark raised 4.59; semantic.error on dark raised 3.03; primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on dark raised 6.83.\n\nGlyph for each variant (draw these exactly):\n- Upcoming: calendar outline, text.strong.\n- Due today: clock face drawn as a rounded square with hands, not a circle. Light: text.strong (warning fails on sunken). Dark: semantic.warning.\n- Overdue: exclamation mark inside a triangle outline, semantic.error (the error glyph).\n- Paid: a plain check stroke with no enclosing shape, semantic.success.\n- Expires <date>: hourglass, text.strong.\n- Declined · <date>: × stroke, text.strong.\n- Waiting for your OK: speech-bubble outline with three short dashes inside (not dots; B8), in primary.700 (standing in for semantic.info) in light and primary.400 (dark link) in dark.\n- Deadline chip: calendar outline, text.strong. For \"Today\": calendar outline, text.strong in light and semantic.warning in dark.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (9 chips × the single state, \"default\"; draw each chip on three backgrounds: surface.base row, surface.raised card, surface.app list)\nRows (specimen text → key). The specimen text is what the chip shows; the key never contains it:\n 1 \"Upcoming\" → upcoming\n 2 \"Due today\" → due-today\n 3 \"Overdue\" → overdue\n 4 \"Paid\" → paid\n 5 \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" → expires\n 6 \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" → declined\n 7 \"Waiting for your OK\" → waiting\n 8 \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (deadline chip; relative count first, as the house style and DateRow order it) → deadline\n 9 \"Today\" (deadline chip) → deadline-today\nLabel the column \"default (the only state)\", key: default. The three backgrounds show one published chip in three contexts; they are not separate variants.\nDark twin: all 27 cells in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5: a bill row \"Comcast · $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" with \"Upcoming\". The pair stacks, the chip moves under the title, and the chip becomes a wrapping rounded rectangle (radius lg) at 40pt with a 24pt glyph. Add chip 5 at AX5 to show the longest string wrapping.\n- 200%: the same.\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the same.\n- GREYSCALE per B10: \"yes — the word carries the state\". Add a WRONG example: two chips that differ only in fill hue, with the text \"fix: words, one chip\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: \"nothing changes — chip text is already text.strong; glyph hues are decorative because the word carries the state\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- The text carries the state. It is read at the end of the row label: \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99, due in 14 days, Monday 2 November, Upcoming\". The glyph is decorative (hidden from assistive tech).\n- Non-colour: the word.\n- Target rule: the chip is never a target; the row is (B13).\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Exactly one chip per row.\n- Sentence case.\n- Dates show the weekday.\n- Beyond tomorrow, deadlines, due dates and expiries put the relative count first: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". Tonight, today and tomorrow stand alone (\"Today\").\n- Past dates show the date only: \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\".\n- Never \"Paid\" as a verb in notifications (\"marked … paid\").\n\nPLATFORMS (01): no platform differences.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three crops)\n a) f3-bills-list, Home A, iOS 393: rows \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" (Upcoming), \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00 · due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\" (Upcoming), \"Comcast · $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\" (Upcoming), one chip each.\n b) f3-members-roster, Home A, web 390: \"Maya Chen · Owner\" and \"Sam Ortega · Member\" with NO chips, and an invite row \"priya@example.com\" with \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\".\n c) f8-seasonal-aha, Place B, Android 412: \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\" with the deadline chip \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\", captioned \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct\".\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of warning-hue text on warningBg, use text.strong on surface.sunken with the hue only on the glyph — because warning text on its tint is about 3:1.\n- Instead of two chips on one row, pick the one status that matters — because two chips compete and get misread.\n- Instead of a status chip on a person (\"Verified\", \"Active\"), state the role in plain text — because people are not statuses.\n- Instead of a warning-tinted countdown pill (founding window), draw a neutral date chip — because countdowns pressure people.\n- Instead of the date before the count (\"Mon 26 Oct · in 7 days\"), write \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" — because the house style and DateRow lead with the count, and every surface copies this chip.\n- Instead of a disc-shaped status dot, use the listed glyphs — because circles belong to ProvenanceMark.\n\n======================================================================\n7. KindGlyph\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: One drawn glyph per dated kind, used in tiles, rows, the pickup card and the widget.\nUsed in: x-date-sheet, f5-today-calendar-strip, f4-today-pickup-card, f7-today-widget, f10-extraction-confirm, f3-household-calendar, x-place-file.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on \"Recycling\" at 24pt, which shows glyph 2, and on the \"Pickup day\" tile at 42pt, which shows glyph 3, garbage+recycling)\n- ① Line icon on a 24pt/dp/px grid, 2pt stroke, round caps and joins, text.strong. Use the Pantopus design system's icon style; if the set lacks a glyph, draw it in that style.\n- ② Tile variant: a 42pt rounded square, radius lg 12, fill surface.sunken, with the 24pt glyph centred.\n- ③ The tile label under the tile, 8pt below, in label 13/18/600 text.strong. It wraps to two lines and is centred.\n- ④ The whole tile + label cell is the target (B13). The kind picker is a 2-column grid inside the date sheet, with 8pt gaps between cells, so each cell is half the sheet's content width minus half a gap: 176 wide on iOS 393 (16pt side margins), 186 wide on Android 412, 175 wide on web 390. Every cell is 88 tall. Draw the dimension lines for the iOS cell.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.strong #374151 on base 10.31 and on sunken 9.37; text.primary #111827 (selected label); text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled only); primary.700 #0369a1 on primary.50 5.57; dark text.strong #F1F5F9 13.35 on dark raised; primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42 (radio and check only).\n\nTHE SET (draw all 17, in this order, each labelled with its kind name and its key):\n 1 garbage (key garbage): lidded wheeled cart\n 2 recycling (key recycling): cart with three chasing arrows on its body\n 3 garbage+recycling (key garbage-recycling): two carts overlapping\n 4 bulk (key bulk): armchair\n 5 move-in (key move-in): open box with an arrow entering it\n 6 lease ends (key lease-ends): key over a door outline\n 7 notice deadline (key notice-deadline): envelope with a small flag\n 8 insurance renews (key insurance-renews): shield with a circular arrow drawn as an open arc\n 9 warranty ends (key warranty-ends): tag with a wrench\n 10 HOA dues (key hoa-dues): three adjoining rooftops\n 11 property-tax appeal (key property-tax-appeal): document with an upward arrow\n 12 property-tax due (key property-tax-due): document with a dollar sign\n 13 voter registration (key voter-registration): ballot entering a slotted box\n 14 bill (key bill): receipt with a zigzag bottom edge\n 15 home event (key home-event): house outline with a small calendar page\n 16 task (key task): rounded-square checkbox with a check stroke\n 17 package (key package): parcel with tape\n(Property tax is one kind with two uses, appeal and due; draw it as two glyphs sharing the document base and note this on Notes.)\nCart wheels are round sub-parts of a larger glyph and are allowed (B8).\n\nTILE → GLYPH MAP (print this table on 01-anatomy):\n Pickup day → 3 garbage+recycling\n Move-in date → 5 move-in\n Lease ends → 6 lease ends\n Notice deadline → 7 notice deadline\n Insurance renews → 8 insurance renews\n Warranty ends → 9 warranty ends\n HOA dues → 10 HOA dues\n Property-tax appeal → 11 property-tax appeal\n Voter registration → 13 voter registration\n Bill → 14 bill\n No tile (rows, the pickup card, the widget and the tray only):\n  pickup rows and the pickup card choose by which bins go out: \"Garbage only\" → 1 garbage; \"Recycling and garbage\" → 3 garbage+recycling; a recycling-only pickup (a city that collects recycling on its own day, which is not the case at Home A or Place B) → 2 recycling;\n  4 bulk, 12 property-tax due, 15 home event, 16 task and 17 package.\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (on 02)\nPart A, variants: 17 glyphs × 4 variants, all in the default state. Variant keys (used as <size|platform> in publish names): row · tile · widget · tray.\n - row 24pt (key row): glyph + visible kind label in bodySmall to its right.\n - tile 42pt (key tile): tile + label (glyphs with no tile get \"Does not apply — no picker tile; see the map\").\n - widget 16pt (key widget): glyph at 16pt with a 1.5pt stroke, with the word beside it in caption.\n - tray, monochrome (key tray): 16pt, one ink, drawn on the dark mail-snap tray (dark surface.raised) in dark text.primary. Label: \"tray: monochrome, one ink\".\nPart B, states: drawn for the \"Pickup day\" kind (glyph 3). 4 rows (row · tile · widget · tray) × 5 columns. Columns (label → key): default → default · selected tile → selected · disabled → disabled · focused, not selected → focus · selected + focused → selected-focus. Every row has all five columns; each \"does not apply\" cell carries its reason.\n - tile row:\n   default: as specified. No radio indicator is drawn on an unselected tile.\n   selected: fill primary.50 (dark: primary.900); label weight 700 (a type-scale deviation, recorded on Notes) and ink text.primary instead of text.strong (dark: dark text.primary). In the tile's top-right corner, a 16pt platform radio indicator in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)): a 1.5px ring with an 8pt filled centre (flagged on Notes, B8). Print \"selected = fill + radio dot + bold label\".\n   disabled: glyph and label in text.muted, fill surface.muted, with a reason caption under the label in caption text.secondary: \"Already on file\".\n   focus: the B14 focus ring only, no fill, no dot.\n   selected-focus: the selected tile plus the B14 focus ring.\n - row 24pt:\n   selected: Does not apply — rows are not selectable.\n   disabled: glyph in text.muted with the label in text.muted, and the reason as a caption in text.secondary.\n   focus and selected-focus: Does not apply — the glyph is decorative; its DateRow owns focus.\n - widget 16pt: selected, disabled, focus and selected-focus: Does not apply — the widget is read-only.\n - tray (monochrome): selected, disabled, focus and selected-focus: Does not apply — the tray is read-only.\nThen draw all 10 tile labels in the default state as one 2-column kind-picker grid, in the order of the map.\nDark twin: Parts A and B in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): the kind picker drops from two columns to one. Each tile becomes a full-width list row: the 42pt tile on the leading edge and the label at 44pt wrapping to its right. Draw \"Warranty ends\" selected and the rest unselected. The selected row gets the primary.50 fill, the bold text.primary label, and a trailing 24pt check stroke in primary.700; unselected rows show no indicator at all (native iOS list selection). No ring is drawn on iOS. The row glyph scales to 48pt at most.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same one-column list at 26sp, with Material 3 radio buttons on the trailing edge, because they are the Android platform control: the selected row shows a 2px primary.700 ring with a 12pt filled centre, and unselected rows show an empty 2px ring in text.secondary (both flagged on Notes, B8).\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the one-column list in the iOS form (trailing check on the selected row, nothing on the others), built as role=\"radio\" rows.\n- GREYSCALE per B10 (subset): the 17 row-variant glyphs and all of Part B. Verdict: \"yes — shape + label\". Selected reads by dot (tile) or check (iOS/web rows) plus bold weight, not by fill hue alone.\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: \"nothing changes — glyphs and labels are already text.strong; on Android, the unselected radio ring becomes text.strong\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Decorative (hidden) when a text label is adjacent.\n- Otherwise labelled with the kind name (for example \"Recycling\").\n- Always paired with visible text; the widget and tray glyphs carry their word.\n- Tiles are one element each: \"Pickup day, selected, 1 of 10\" (iOS button with the selected trait; Android RadioButton semantics; web role=\"radio\" inside role=\"radiogroup\").\n- Non-colour: shape + label; selection = dot or check + weight.\n- Target rule: the tile cell or row, never the glyph alone, is the target (B13).\n\nCOPY (01)\nTile labels, exactly: Pickup day · Move-in date · Lease ends · Notice deadline · Insurance renews · Warranty ends · HOA dues · Property-tax appeal · Voter registration · Bill.\nGlossary: \"Pickup day\", never \"trash day\", \"garbage day\" or \"bin day\"; \"Date\", never \"event\" or \"deadline item\".\n\nPLATFORMS (01)\nDraw the same glyph on all three platforms; the widget glyph follows the same silhouette-safe drawing as ProvenanceMark (see Notes). The one-column large-text list differs by platform: trailing check on iOS and web, Material 3 radio buttons on Android.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three crops)\n a) x-date-sheet, iOS 393, Home A: the sheet title \"Add a date\", the 10-tile kind picker in 2 columns with \"Warranty ends\" selected, and the sheet's visible \"Close\".\n b) f4-today-pickup-card, Home A, Android 412: the pickup card on surface.base, radius lg. It contains, top to bottom: the 42pt tile variant with glyph 3 (garbage+recycling); the h3 headline \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\"; the instruction \"Bins out tonight — carts out by 6:30 AM\"; a SourceCaption with the unconfirmed mark reading \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of Mon 19 Oct\", with the words \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" printed once beside the mark; then two outlined peer buttons of identical weight, \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\".\n c) f7-today-widget, 338×158pt, \"Larkspur Loop\": 16pt glyphs for recycling + garbage (glyph 3, \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\"), bill (\"Clark Public Utilities · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\") and HOA dues (\"HOA dues · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\"), each with its word.\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of hue-coded glyphs as the only class cue, give each kind its own silhouette plus a label — because hue alone fails in greyscale and for colour-blind users.\n- Instead of an unlabelled glyph, always show the kind name beside it — because the glyphs are not universal.\n- Instead of guessing a tile's glyph, use the TILE → GLYPH map — because every later picker copies this one.\n- Instead of showing selection with the focus ring, use fill + radio dot + bold label — because selection must look different from focus.\n- Instead of an empty-ring radio on iOS large-text rows, use a trailing check on the selected row — because iOS has no radio control and an empty ring is the unconfirmed mark's shape.\n- Instead of emoji or a second icon set, use the Pantopus icon style — because the house style forbids a new icon set.\n\n======================================================================\n8. AddressChip\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: Shows a held or selected address as a label: never a map, never coordinates.\nUsed in: f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-save-confirmation, f1-add-place-sheet, f8-compare-arrival-header.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on the held chip for Place B)\n- ① Pill, radius pill, fill surface.raised, 1px border.default as decoration (1.24:1). The chip's meaning never depends on its edge.\n- ② 16pt pin glyph in text.strong, with an 8pt gap. Its round hole is a sub-part (B8).\n- ③ Street \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct\" in bodySmallMedium 14/20/500, text.primary.\n- ④ City \"Camas, WA 98607\" in caption 12/16, text.secondary (4.63:1 on raised), on the line below the street.\n- ⑤ Padding 12 horizontal and 8 vertical; minimum height 44pt.\n- ⑥ At 390 wide it wraps (street and city each wrap and are never truncated).\n- ⑦ Optional \"Save it\" action, used only when the chip is a selectable suggestion row: a text button in label 13/18/600 primary.700, with a target (B13).\n- ⑧ Followed by the ScopeChip sentence, 8pt below: \"Only you will see this.\" The one exception is the sender label (R4): it describes someone else's place, so it carries no sentence; the sentence goes under the recipient's own address field instead (see in-context c).\n- Dark: fill dark surface.raised. dark border.default on dark raised is invisible (about 1:1), so use no border in dark mode; the pin and text carry the chip.\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: text.primary #111827 on raised; text.secondary #6B7280 on raised 4.63; primary.700 #0369a1 on base 5.93 and on primary.50 5.57; border.default #E5E7EB 1.24 (decoration only); dark text.secondary #94A3B8 on dark raised 5.71; primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 on primary.900 4.42 (edge and check only).\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (4 rows × 3 columns)\nThe addresses in these rows are specimens: R1–R3 all use the Place B address to show each form, even though in the fixture story Jordan has already saved it (recorded on Notes).\nColumns (label → key): default → default · selected → selected · expired (neutral) → expired.\n R1 held → held (f1-email-verify-handoff): the chip, then \"We're holding it for 7 days\", then \"Only you will see this.\"\n   default: as described.\n   selected: fill primary.50 (dark: primary.900), a 1.5px primary.700 edge (dark: primary.400 (dark link)), and a trailing 16pt check stroke in primary.700 (dark: primary.400 (dark link)). Text stays text.primary (dark: dark text.primary).\n   expired: fill surface.sunken, text in text.strong, the caption \"We're no longer holding this address.\" and a text button \"Search again\" that opens search already filled with \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas\". Use no warning or error hue.\n R2 selectable recovery row → recovery-row (f1-save-confirmation): a full-width 44pt row reading \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\", where \"Save it\" is the action.\n   default: as described.\n   selected: the selected treatment from R1, with \"Save it\" replaced by the check.\n   expired: the R1 expired treatment in row form.\n R3 duplicate → duplicate (f1-add-place-sheet): the chip, then You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today — where \"Use for Today\" is a 44pt text button.\n   default: as described.\n   selected: the selected treatment, after \"Use for Today\" is chosen.\n   expired: Does not apply — a saved place does not expire.\n R4 sender label → sender (f8-compare-arrival-header): the chip with the pin glyph, reading \"Dana\" in bodySmallMedium and \"Camas, WA\" in caption. Its compact form reads \"Dana · Camas, WA\". No scope sentence under it (anatomy ⑧).\n   default: as described.\n   selected and expired: Does not apply — a sender label is neither selectable nor held.\nDark twin: all 12 cells in dark tokens.\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5: R1 and R2. The street and city wrap onto several lines, the pill becomes a rounded rectangle (radius lg), and \"Save it\" moves under the address as a full-width 44pt button. The pin glyph scales to 32pt.\n- 200%: the same.\n- Web 200% zoom (390 wide, B9): the same.\n- GREYSCALE per B10: \"yes — pin + text; selected = check + edge\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R1 default with the city line in text.strong; the decorative border is unchanged.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Reads the full address:\n  \"1107 Northeast Birchfield Court, Camas, Washington 98607\"\n  Selected: \"…, selected\".\n  Sender: \"Dana, Camas, Washington\".\n- Non-colour: selected = check + edge; expired = words.\n- Target rule: the chip itself is a label. Its actions (\"Save it\", \"Use for Today\", \"Search again\") are targets (B13).\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Always paired with the ScopeChip sentence, except the sender label.\n- Exact strings: \"We're holding it for 7 days\" · \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\" · You already saved this as “Mom’s house” · Use for Today · \"Dana · Camas, WA\".\n- Glossary: \"Saved place\", never \"bookmark\", \"preview\" or \"draft\".\n\nPLATFORMS (01): no platform differences. Draw the same chip on all three.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three crops)\n a) f1-email-verify-handoff, web 390: \"Check your email\" context, with R1 default under it.\n b) f1-save-confirmation, iOS 393: R2 default.\n c) f8-compare-arrival-header, web 1440 crop (720 wide): the R4 sender chip over Dana's column (no scope sentence), and in the empty second column the recipient's address field with \"Only you will see this.\" under it.\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of a blank retype field when the server holds the address, show the held AddressChip — because retyping loses people between steps.\n- Instead of a map or coordinates, show the street and city as text — because a label is enough and a map leaks location.\n- Instead of an alarm colour for an expired hold, use a neutral sunken chip with \"Search again\" — because expiry is not an error.\n- Instead of a held or selectable chip without its scope sentence, always add \"Only you will see this.\" — because a held address must say who sees it.\n- Instead of \"Only you will see this.\" under a sender's chip, put it under the recipient's own field — because the sentence would be false about the sender's place.\n\n======================================================================\n9. ChoiceChip\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS: 01 light · 02 light and dark · 03 light · 04 light (full names in the manifest).\n\nPURPOSE: Small single-choice chips for channel, role, time and filter; they are never status badges.\nUsed in: f3-invite-composer, f4-briefing-optin-card, f10-mail-piece-photo, f3-bills-list, f4-notification-settings.\n\nANATOMY (callouts on the time group \"6:30 AM · 7:00 AM · 7:30 AM · 8:00 AM\" with 7:00 AM selected)\n- ① Height 32pt/dp/px visual, with a target (B13) around it (draw both outlines).\n- ② Radius pill, padding 12 horizontal, 8 gap between chips.\n- ③ Label 13/18/600.\n- ④ Selected: fill primary.50, a 1px primary.700 outline (5.93:1 against base, so the shape stays visible although the fill is only 1.07:1), text primary.700 (5.57:1 on the fill), and a leading 12pt check stroke in primary.700 with a 4pt gap. Dark: fill primary.900, 1px primary.400 (dark link) outline (8.33:1 on dark base), text dark text.primary, check primary.400 (dark link).\n- ⑤ Unselected: a 1px outline and text.strong. The component spec names border.strong for the outline, but border.strong is 1.47:1 and the house style says an input's only edge uses text.secondary ink or darker. So draw the outline in text.secondary (4.83:1) and print \"spec border.strong → text.secondary (see Notes)\".\n- ⑥ Focus: the B14 ring, drawn on the unselected and on the selected chip.\n- ⑦ Disabled: text and a 1px outline both in text.muted (2.54:1 on base; dark text.muted, 3.75:1 on dark base), no check, plus a reason caption under the group in text.secondary. No border token is used as the edge. Print \"disabled controls are exempt from WCAG contrast; the reason caption carries the meaning (see Notes)\".\n- TOKEN AND CONTRAST TABLE: primary.700 #0369a1 on primary.50 5.57 and on base 5.93 (selected outline); primary.50 #f0f9ff on base 1.07 (fill only); text.strong #374151 on base 10.31; text.secondary #6B7280 4.83 (unselected outline); text.muted #9CA3AF 2.54 (disabled text and outline); border.strong #D1D5DB 1.47 (not used as the edge); border.focus #0284c7 4.10; dark: text.primary #E5E7EB on primary.900 #0c4a6e 7.64, primary.400 (dark link) #38BDF8 outline 8.33 on dark base and 6.83 on dark raised, check 4.42 on primary.900, dark text.secondary #94A3B8 outline 6.96, dark text.muted #64748B 3.75 on dark base (disabled).\n\nVARIANT × STATE GRID (5 rows × 5 columns)\nColumns (label → key): default → default · selected → selected · disabled → disabled · focus → focus · selected + focus → selected-focus (the last shows that selection and focus look different).\nIn R1–R4, the disabled cell shows every chip in the group disabled, with the row's own reason caption under the group. R5 is different (see R5).\n R1 channel → channel (f3-invite-composer): \"Email\" · \"Username\" · \"Share instead\". Default: all unselected. Selected: \"Email\". Disabled reason: \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" Focus: focus on \"Username\". Selected + focus: \"Email\" selected and focused.\n R2 role → role (f3-invite-composer): \"Member\" · \"Guest\". A capability caption under the group, in caption text.secondary, describes the selected role only. Member: \"Sees and edits the calendar, sees bills and who paid, sees who lives here\". Guest: \"Same as Member until Sun 1 Nov\".\n   Default: both unselected and no capability caption; print the cell note \"caption appears after a role is chosen\".\n   Selected: \"Member\", with the Member caption.\n   Disabled: both chips disabled, no capability caption, reason \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" (the same surface as R1).\n   Focus: focus on \"Guest\", nothing selected, no capability caption.\n   Selected + focus: \"Member\" selected and focused, with the Member caption.\n R3 time → time (f4-briefing-optin-card): \"6:30 AM\" · \"7:00 AM\" · \"7:30 AM\" · \"8:00 AM\". Selected: \"7:00 AM\". Disabled reason: \"You're offline. Your briefing time will save when you're back online.\" Focus: focus on \"7:30 AM\". Selected + focus: \"7:00 AM\".\n R4 filter → filter (f10-mail-piece-photo drawer): \"Photographed\", a single toggle chip. Default: off. Selected: on. Disabled reason: \"You're offline. Filters need a connection.\" Focus: off and focused. Selected + focus: on and focused.\n R5 segment → segment (f3-bills-list): \"Upcoming\" · \"Paid\" · \"All\". Selected: \"Upcoming\". Disabled: \"Upcoming\" stays enabled and selected (cached bills still show), while \"Paid\" and \"All\" are disabled, with the reason \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\" Focus: focus on \"Paid\". Selected + focus: \"Upcoming\". Draw the web/Android chip form here; the iOS segmented form is on 01-anatomy (PLATFORMS).\nDark twin: all 25 cells in dark tokens (selected fill primary.900, outline and check primary.400 (dark link), text dark text.primary, disabled text and outline dark text.muted).\n\nSCALING AND GREYSCALE (03)\n- AX5 (iOS 393): R1 and R3 turn into one-column rows. Each option is a full-width row at least 44pt tall with the label at 44pt, wrapping. The selected row gets the primary.50 fill, the label in primary.700, and a trailing 24pt check stroke in primary.700; unselected rows show no indicator (native iOS list selection). No ring is drawn on iOS. R2's capability caption sits under each row. The iOS segmented control (R5) also becomes these rows at AX sizes.\n- 200% (Android 412): the same rows at 48dp with Material 3 radio buttons on the leading edge, because they are the Android platform control: unselected rows show an empty 2px ring in text.secondary; the selected row shows a 2px primary.700 ring with a 12pt filled centre (both flagged on Notes, B8).\n- Web 200% zoom, two frames:\n  390 wide at 200% (195 px effective, B9): below the 360 px switch point, so draw the one-column rows in the iOS form (trailing check, no ring), built as role=\"radio\" rows.\n  1440 wide at 200% (720 px effective), cropped to the chip group: the chips wrap onto several lines and stay chips.\n  Print the rule \"switch to rows below 360 px effective width\".\n- GREYSCALE per B10: \"yes — selected = check + fill + outline; focus = ring\". Add a WRONG example where the selected chip differs only by hue, with \"fix: add the check\".\n- INCREASE CONTRAST: R3 with the unselected outlines in text.strong, and the unselected Android radio rings in text.strong; the selected chip is unchanged; disabled chips stay text.muted (B16).\n\nACCESSIBILITY (01)\n- Selection is shown by the check + fill + outline, not by colour alone.\n- Each group is one radio group:\n  iOS: buttons with the selected trait, e.g. \"7:00 AM, selected, 2 of 4\".\n  Android: selectable semantics, \"7:00 AM, selected\".\n  Web: role=\"radiogroup\" with role=\"radio\" and aria-checked; arrow keys move between chips.\n- The filter chip is a toggle: \"Photographed, off\" / \"Photographed, on\".\n- Disabled chips stay focusable and read their reason.\n- Target rule: a target (B13) around a 32 visual, with 8pt gaps.\n- Focus ring is distinct from selection.\n\nCOPY (01)\n- Sentence case. Exact strings as listed in the grid.\n- Times are written \"7:00 AM\" (a space, AM in capitals).\n- Never \"6:00pm\" or \"7:40 am\".\n\nPLATFORMS (01; on 01-anatomy, draw all three platforms side by side for R5 and R3)\n- iOS: R5 is a native segmented control (UISegmentedControl look, 32pt, with the selected segment raised), where native. R1–R4 are Pantopus chips.\n- Android: Material 3 filter chips (leading check when selected, 32dp visual, 48dp target), using Pantopus tokens and the pill radius rather than the M3 default 8dp corner (see Notes). R5 on Android is a single-select row of the same filter chips.\n- Web: the chips as specified, with a :focus-visible ring and no hover-only affordance.\n- Large text: iOS and web use trailing-check rows; Android uses Material 3 radio buttons.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04; three crops)\n a) f3-invite-composer, iOS 393, Home A: channel chips (Email selected) above the field \"priya@example.com\", then role chips (Member selected) with the capability caption, then the primary button \"Send invite\".\n b) f4-briefing-optin-card, Android 412: \"A morning heads-up?\" with the time chips, 7:00 AM selected, and equal-weight \"Not now\" and \"No thanks\".\n c) f3-bills-list, web 1440 crop (720 wide) and iOS 393: \"Upcoming / Paid / All\" as chips (web) and as a segmented control (iOS).\n\nINSTEAD OF (01)\n- Instead of using a ChoiceChip as a status badge, use StatusChip — because a choice chip looks tappable.\n- Instead of a status chip on a person, write the role in plain text — because people are not statuses.\n- Instead of a border.strong outline (1.47:1) as an unselected chip's only edge, use text.secondary — because an input's edge must be visible.\n- Instead of a border.default outline on a disabled chip, use text.muted for its outline — because border tokens are never an input's only edge.\n- Instead of a selected chip whose only boundary is the primary.50 fill (1.07:1), add a 1px primary.700 outline — because the chip's shape must stay visible, as AddressChip's selected edge does.\n- Instead of showing selection with colour alone, add the leading check — because it must read in greyscale.\n- Instead of the focus ring doubling as selection, keep the ring for focus and fill + check + outline for selection — because they are different states.\n- Instead of truncating long labels at large text, switch to one-column rows — because truncated choices cannot be told apart.\n- Instead of disabling a segment that still has cached content, keep it enabled and disable only the segments that need a connection — because the reason must match what is disabled.\n\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS (exact names; print each name above its frame)\n======================================================================\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light — three silhouettes at L with callouts, sizes XS–L and OG, legend, contrast table, accessibility, copy, platforms, INSTEAD OF\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark — silhouettes, sizes, legend and contrast table in dark tokens (no text blocks)\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light — the 6 × 5 grid (official, unconfirmed, you-added, read-from-photo, stale, reported × default, stale, in-target, tinted-widget, greyscale)\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 30 cells in dark tokens\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, web zoom, XS legibility strip, greyscale pointer + WRONG example, Increase Contrast ink\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark — AX5, 200%, the XS strip and Increase Contrast ink in dark tokens\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light — x-place-file legend + rows, f5-today-calendar-strip legend + every fixture date, f7-today-widget with words\n00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark — the same three crops in dark tokens\n00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light — caption pattern with callouts, base vs sunken ink, wrap, link vs no-link, OG strip, accessibility, copy, INSTEAD OF\n00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light — the 6 × 3 grid (dated-static, live, frozen, county, collapsed, no-url × default, stale, offline) + the dated-static-link twin\n00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark — the same cells in dark tokens\n00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, web zoom, greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light — f8-scale-strips, f1-today-air-band (default + alert, no track), f8-compare-arrival-header frozen row\n00a · ScopeChip · 01-anatomy · light — pill with callouts, glyphs, target vs label-only, footer sentence, retired wording, INSTEAD OF\n00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · light — the 5 × 4 grid (saved-place, claimed-home, named-home, scope-change-pair, footer-sentence × default, pending, declined, struck)\n00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 20 cells in dark tokens\n00a · ScopeChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, web zoom, greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n00a · ScopeChip · 04-in-context · light — f1-today-tab location row, x-date-sheet footer above Save, f1-claim-receipt pairs + consent\n00a · FreshnessLine · 01-anatomy · light — placement, glyphs, system hairline (running, 5s stop, Reduce Motion), Retry target, INSTEAD OF\n00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · light — the 6 × 5 grid (updating, updated, failed, offline, fact-stale, widget-horizon × fresh, refreshing, stale, failed, offline) + the no-reflow strip\n00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 30 cells in dark tokens\n00a · FreshnessLine · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, web zoom, greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n00a · FreshnessLine · 04-in-context · light — f1-today-tab, f7-today-widget past horizon, f3-bills-list header\n00a · OfflineNotice · 01-anatomy · light — offline line, disabled control + reason, plain vs sunken, focusable disabled, INSTEAD OF\n00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · light — the 3 × 3 grid (cached-screen, queued-writes, form × offline, reconnecting, back-online)\n00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 9 cells in dark tokens\n00a · OfflineNotice · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, web zoom, greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n00a · OfflineNotice · 04-in-context · light — f8-native-share-compare, f1-add-place-sheet, f10-snap-capture-tray\n00a · StatusChip · 01-anatomy · light — pill with callouts, the glyph for each variant, contrast table with the warning fail, INSTEAD OF\n00a · StatusChip · 02-variants-states · light — 9 chips × default on base, raised and app\n00a · StatusChip · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 27 cells in dark tokens\n00a · StatusChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5 stacked bill row, 200%, web zoom, greyscale grid + WRONG example, Increase Contrast\n00a · StatusChip · 04-in-context · light — f3-bills-list, f3-members-roster invite row, f8-seasonal-aha deadline\n00a · KindGlyph · 01-anatomy · light — grid, stroke, tile, label, 2-column target cell, the 17-glyph set with keys, TILE → GLYPH map, INSTEAD OF\n00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · light — Part A: 17 glyphs × row, tile, widget, tray; Part B: 4 × 5 states + the 10-tile 2-column picker\n00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · dark — Parts A and B in dark tokens\n00a · KindGlyph · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5 one-column list (trailing check), Android 200% (M3 radios), web zoom, greyscale subset, Increase Contrast\n00a · KindGlyph · 04-in-context · light — x-date-sheet picker, f4-today-pickup-card (42pt tile), f7-today-widget\n00a · AddressChip · 01-anatomy · light — chip with callouts, Save it action, scope sentence and its sender exception, dark edge rule, INSTEAD OF\n00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · light — the 4 × 3 grid (held, recovery-row, duplicate, sender × default, selected, expired)\n00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 12 cells in dark tokens\n00a · AddressChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, web zoom, greyscale grid, Increase Contrast\n00a · AddressChip · 04-in-context · light — f1-email-verify-handoff, f1-save-confirmation, f8-compare-arrival-header\n00a · ChoiceChip · 01-anatomy · light — chip with callouts, selected vs unselected vs focus vs disabled, outline deviations, iOS/Android/web comparison for R5 and R3, INSTEAD OF\n00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · light — the 5 × 5 grid (channel, role, time, filter, segment × default, selected, disabled, focus, selected-focus)\n00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · dark — the same 25 cells in dark tokens\n00a · ChoiceChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light — AX5 rows (trailing check), Android 200% (M3 radios), web zoom at 390 and 1440, greyscale grid + WRONG example, Increase Contrast\n00a · ChoiceChip · 04-in-context · light — f3-invite-composer, f4-briefing-optin-card, f3-bills-list (web chips vs iOS segmented)\n00a · Notes — contract deviations, invented strings, omitted states, open questions, publish index\n\nTotal: 49 artboards.\n\n======================================================================\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn; after each turn, stop and wait for \"continue\")\n======================================================================\nOrder: ProvenanceMark's full set comes first, including its dark twins, because it is designed first and every other component on this board embeds its marks. After that, each component is finished as a unit (it is published as a unit) in house-style priority order: 01 anatomy, 02 grid, 04 in context, 03 scaling and greyscale, then the dark 02 twin.\n\nTurn 1:\n 1. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark\n 6. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 02-variants-states · dark\nTurn 2:\n 1. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 04-in-context · dark\n 2. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark\n 3. 00a · SourceCaption · 01-anatomy · light\n 4. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · light\n 5. 00a · SourceCaption · 04-in-context · light\n 6. 00a · SourceCaption · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\nTurn 3:\n 1. 00a · SourceCaption · 02-variants-states · dark\n 2. 00a · ScopeChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 3. 00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 4. 00a · ScopeChip · 04-in-context · light\n 5. 00a · ScopeChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 6. 00a · ScopeChip · 02-variants-states · dark\nTurn 4:\n 1. 00a · FreshnessLine · 01-anatomy · light\n 2. 00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · light\n 3. 00a · FreshnessLine · 04-in-context · light\n 4. 00a · FreshnessLine · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 5. 00a · FreshnessLine · 02-variants-states · dark\n 6. 00a · OfflineNotice · 01-anatomy · light\nTurn 5:\n 1. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · light\n 2. 00a · OfflineNotice · 04-in-context · light\n 3. 00a · OfflineNotice · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 4. 00a · OfflineNotice · 02-variants-states · dark\n 5. 00a · StatusChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 6. 00a · StatusChip · 02-variants-states · light\nTurn 6:\n 1. 00a · StatusChip · 04-in-context · light\n 2. 00a · StatusChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 3. 00a · StatusChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 4. 00a · KindGlyph · 01-anatomy · light\n 5. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · light\n 6. 00a · KindGlyph · 04-in-context · light\nTurn 7:\n 1. 00a · KindGlyph · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 2. 00a · KindGlyph · 02-variants-states · dark\n 3. 00a · AddressChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 4. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 5. 00a · AddressChip · 04-in-context · light\n 6. 00a · AddressChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\nTurn 8:\n 1. 00a · AddressChip · 02-variants-states · dark\n 2. 00a · ChoiceChip · 01-anatomy · light\n 3. 00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · light\n 4. 00a · ChoiceChip · 04-in-context · light\n 5. 00a · ChoiceChip · 03-scaling-greyscale · light\n 6. 00a · ChoiceChip · 02-variants-states · dark\nTurn 9:\n 1. 00a · Notes\nIf a turn cannot fit all six, finish the artboards in the listed order and say which ones moved to the next turn.\n\n======================================================================\n00a · Notes (what the Notes artboard must contain)\n======================================================================\nPrint these as numbered lists in body 16/24 text.primary on surface.base.\n\nA. Contract deviations and decisions (each needs a founder yes or no):\n 1. ProvenanceMark stale ink: text.primary at 50% instead of the contract's plain \"50% opacity\", because text.secondary at 50% is 1.98:1 and marks need 3:1.\n 2. ProvenanceMark stale captions are per row, not one shared suffix: the pickup schedule reads \"as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\"; the official effective-date row, your own entry and a pre-commit photo read are \"does not apply\", because they do not age.\n 3. ProvenanceMark tinted widget is never dimmed for stale: the full tint stays (5.93:1 light, 5.28:1 dark) and the age words carry the state, because a 50% tint drops to 2.24:1 (light) and 2.36:1 (dark).\n 4. Tinted widget stand-in: primary.700 on surface.base in light (5.93:1) and primary.500 on dark surface.raised in dark (5.28:1). primary.500 on white is 2.77:1, so it is not used in light mode.\n 5. ChoiceChip unselected outline: text.secondary instead of the contract's border.strong (1.47:1), following the house-style edge rule.\n 6. ChoiceChip disabled chip: text and outline in text.muted (2.54:1 light, 3.75:1 dark) instead of a border.default outline (1.24:1), because border tokens are never an input's only edge. Disabled controls are exempt from WCAG contrast; the reason caption under the group carries the meaning.\n 7. Selected ChoiceChip gets a 1px primary.700 outline (dark: primary.400 (dark link)); the contract names only the fill. Without it, the selected chip's boundary is the 1.07:1 primary.50 fill.\n 8. ChoiceChip R5 (segment) disabled cell keeps \"Upcoming\" enabled and selected, because cached bills still show; only \"Paid\" and \"All\" are disabled, matching the reason \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\"\n 9. ChoiceChip R2 (role) shows a capability caption only for the selected role; with nothing selected (default and focus cells) no caption is shown.\n 10. Android ChoiceChip keeps the pill radius instead of the M3 default 8dp corner.\n 11. Radio indicators vs invariant 1 (\"filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else\"). Kept in two places: (a) the selected KindGlyph tile's corner indicator (ring with a filled centre; unselected tiles show nothing), which the contract asks for (\"filled radio dot\"); (b) Android Material 3 radio buttons in the 200% one-column lists (KindGlyph and ChoiceChip), where they are the platform control and the unselected option is an empty ring, the same silhouette as the UNCONFIRMED mark. iOS (AX5) and web (200% zoom) lists use a trailing check on the selected row and nothing on the others, because iOS has no native radio control. Open question for the founder: keep (b) as platform-native, or use the trailing-check form on Android too; and whether (a) should become a check stroke in the tile corner.\n 12. KindGlyph selected tile label uses weight 700, which is not in the type scale (label is 13/18/600), because the contract asks for a bold label; its ink also changes from text.strong to text.primary. Alternative if rejected: keep 600 and rely on the ink change, fill and radio dot.\n 13. KindGlyph Part B has five state columns for every variant (default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus); the contract lists default · selected tile · disabled, and focus is added to show selection differs from focus.\n 14. Mark and glyph scaling at AX5 / 200% is capped at 2× (S 16 → 32). The contract says only \"scales up to AX5\".\n 15. Ring and tick stroke widths per size (1.5 / 2 / 3 / 7) and the 56% tick span are this board's geometry; the contract sets only the 1.5px minimum.\n 16. KindGlyph widget stroke is 1.5pt at 16pt, and the widget glyph uses ProvenanceMark's silhouette-safe accented rendering. The contract has no platform notes for KindGlyph.\n 17. \"property-tax (appeal / due)\" is drawn as two glyphs sharing a document base.\n 18. Glyph 2 (recycling) has no tile; it is used for a recycling-only pickup row and in the anatomy specimen. Neither Home A nor Place B has a recycling-only day.\n 19. ScopeChip house glyph: text.strong, because identity.home is 2.99:1 on surface.sunken.\n 20. ScopeChip footer sentence type: bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary with a 16pt glyph. The contract does not set a type style.\n 21. StatusChip warning glyphs (Due today, Today): text.strong in light mode (semantic.warning is 2.89:1 on sunken) and semantic.warning in dark mode (4.59:1). The \"Waiting for your OK\" glyph uses primary.700 in place of semantic.info.\n 22. Dark substitute for primary.50: primary.900 with dark text.primary. There is no dark primary.50 token. The dark link colour is named \"primary.400 (dark link)\", the same value as dark border.focus.\n 23. Dark surface.sunken equals dark surface.base, so chips on dark base use dark surface.raised (rule B6).\n 24. AddressChip dark mode has no border, because dark border.default on dark raised is about 1:1.\n 25. AddressChip sender label (R4) has no ScopeChip sentence, because \"Only you will see this.\" would be false about the sender's place; the sentence sits under the recipient's own address field. The contract says the chip is always paired with the sentence.\n 26. AddressChip rows R1–R3 all use the Place B address as specimens, although in the fixture story Jordan already saved it on Sat 10 Oct. The contract's duplicate string (You already saved this as “Mom’s house”) is kept verbatim, with curly inner quotes, for the specimen only.\n 27. OfflineNotice form variant: back online shows no FreshnessLine, because a form has no content age.\n 28. FreshnessLine hairline: it is the platform's system indeterminate progress indicator with no custom duration. It is exempt from the house style's 300ms motion limit because it is a progress indicator, not a transition; instead it is capped at 5s, per \"idle loops stop within 5s\", after which \"Updating…\" carries the state.\n 29. Contract example strings were re-dated to the house-style fixtures (TODAY Mon 19 Oct 2026) and to the weekday date format: \"effective Sep 24, 2021\" → \"effective Sep 2021\"; \"observed 3:10 PM today\" → \"observed 7:00 AM today\"; \"on Sep 12, 2026\" → \"on Sat 12 Sep 2026\"; \"— 9 hours ago\" → \"— 11 hours ago\"; \"Observed 6:00 AM · AirNow — 9 hours ago\" → \"Observed 7:00 AM · AirNow — 11 hours ago\"; \"as of Sep 15\" → \"as of 7:00 AM\"; \"As of Mon 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" → \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (the time is today, so the weekday is dropped); \"Expires Sep 23\" → \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"Declined · Sep 15\" → \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\"; \"Oct 26 · 18 days\" → \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"Maple St · Your household\" → \"Larkspur Loop · Your household\"; \"1402 NE 3rd Ave, Camas — Save it\" → \"1107 NE Birchfield Ct, Camas — Save it\".\n 30. Deadline-chip ORDER CHANGED: the contract's StatusChip writes the date first (\"Oct 26 · 18 days\"). This board puts the relative count first (\"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"), matching the house style, research brief section 6 and the contract's own DateRow (\"in 11 days · Fri 30 Oct\"). If the founder wants date-first for chips only, say so before publishing, because all 59 surfaces copy this chip.\n 31. The invite expiry chip also leads with the count: \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (the house-style date rule applied to expiries). Alternative if rejected: \"Expires Mon 26 Oct\".\n 32. Every dated row on this board follows DateRow's format (relative count first beyond tomorrow; \"Tonight\", \"Today\" and \"Tomorrow\" alone), including bill rows (\"due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\") and widget rows. DateRow owns the date format; later surfaces copy it from there. The pickup-card headline \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\" names tomorrow and shows the weekday date alone.\n 33. The contract's spoken example \"Trash day Tuesday, City of Camas, …\" became \"Pickup day Thursday, City of Camas, on record, not confirmed\", following the glossary (\"Pickup day\") and the Place B fixture (Thursday per the City of Camas).\n 34. Glossary tension: the sourced consent button \"Keep them private to me\" (f1-claim-receipt research) sits close to the glossary's forbidden \"private to you\" and to the retired \"private to your home\". Proposed alternative: \"Just me\" (the house style's neutral decline).\n 35. Kind picker: 2 columns (from the contract's DateSheet), with the TILE → GLYPH map on 01-anatomy. \"Pickup day\" uses glyph 3, garbage+recycling.\n 36. The f4-today-pickup-card crop follows the contract's PickupCard (42pt tile, the words \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\" once), with the Home A instruction adapted to the fixture's \"carts out by 6:30 AM\".\n 37. Mon 26 Oct voter registration in the calendar-strip crop is drawn as FourteenDayStrip's full-height civic bar, per that component's anatomy (\"a civic/state/county rule is a full-height bar spanning the cell\"), not as a mark. Its row title uses the \"must arrive by\" deadline wording.\n 38. The calendar-strip crop prints the legend once above the strip, so its surface shows each mark's word once (invariant 1).\n 39. No AQI track and no EPA hue appear on this board (B17); the AQI track belongs to AqiBand.\n 40. Artboard names on this board use \"00a · <Component> · <NN-state> · <light|dark>\", replacing the house style's platform slot with the component name, because each specimen artboard covers all three platforms.\n 41. Web 200% zoom frames are 390 px wide (195 px effective viewport) and so show the narrowest layout; ChoiceChip adds a 1440-wide 200% frame (720 px effective) for its wrapping-chip form.\n 42. Every grid row and column carries a key (B18); publish names use only keys, never fixture strings or dates.\n 43. Contrast figures on this board are WCAG 2 ratios computed from the real tokens; colours drawn at an opacity are first alpha-blended over their surface in sRGB with unrounded channel values, and every ratio is rounded to 2 decimals at the end. Stale values: 3.39 base, 3.36 raised, 3.34 app, 3.32 sunken; dark 4.45 base, 4.10 raised, 4.48 app.\n\nB. Invented strings (not in the house style or the contract):\n \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct\" · \"City of Camas · city pickup schedule · as of Sat 10 Oct — 9 days ago\" · \"AirNow · nearest monitors · as of 7:00 AM\" · \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide · as of Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Waste Connections · city pickup schedule · as of Mon 19 Oct\" · \"Bins out tonight — carts out by 6:30 AM\" (contract pattern with the fixture time) · \"Recycling and garbage · Tue 20 Oct\" · \"Recycling and garbage · Tomorrow\" · \"Reconnecting · as of 7:04 AM\" · \"Reconnecting\" · \"You're offline. You can keep taking photos.\" · \"You're offline. Invites need a connection.\" · \"You're offline. Your briefing time will save when you're back online.\" · \"You're offline. Filters need a connection.\" · \"You're offline. Paid and All need a connection.\" · \"We're no longer holding this address.\" · \"Search again\" · \"Already on file\" · \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" (house-style pattern) · \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Same as Member until Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Send invite\" · \"Water heater · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"Warranty ends · in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec\" · \"$142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\" · the bill rows (\"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 · due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"; \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00 · due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\"; \"Comcast · $79.99 · due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\") · the widget rows (\"Clark Public Utilities · in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"; \"HOA dues · in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\") · \"Pickup frequency · Not set\" · \"Pickup day · Thursday · On record, not confirmed\" · the calendar-strip rows (\"Recycling and garbage / Tomorrow\"; \"Clark Public Utilities · $142.18 / in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\"; \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct / in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\"; \"Garbage only / in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct\"; \"City of Vancouver water · $84.00 / in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\"; \"HOA dues · $285 / in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\") · \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" (re-dated contract string) · board annotations (\"civic bar (FourteenDayStrip)\"; \"legend once per surface\"; \"track omitted: AqiBand\"; \"idle loops stop within 5s\"; \"tint is never dimmed; the words carry stale\"; \"caption appears after a role is chosen\"; \"switch to rows below 360 px effective width\"; \"Does not apply — …\" reasons) · the spoken labels on this board (\"Flood zone, Zone X, minimal flood hazard, FEMA, official\"; \"Warranty ends, water heater, in 54 days, Saturday 12 December, you added this\"; \"Visible to only you; will be visible to your household if you share\"; \"Compare with a friend, dimmed, Compare needs a connection.\"; \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99, due in 14 days, Monday 2 November, Upcoming\"; \"Pickup day, selected, 1 of 10\"; \"7:00 AM, selected, 2 of 4\"; \"Photographed, off\"; \"Dana, Camas, Washington\") · the glyph descriptions and keys for the 17 kinds.\n Strings taken from the research brief, the contract and earlier specs, not invented: \"Uploading 1 of 3\" (pattern from brief section 5); \"Share the 2 dates you entered with Sam?\", \"Share with the household\" and \"Keep them private to me\" (f1-claim-receipt research); the Member capability caption (f3-invite-composer research); \"6:30 AM · 7:00 AM · 7:30 AM · 8:00 AM\" (f4-briefing-optin-card); \"Everyone at Larkspur Loop can see these bills · 3 upcoming · $306.17 through Mon 2 Nov\" (f3-bills-list research); \"A morning heads-up?\" (glossary); \"City schedule, not yet confirmed\", \"Yes, Tuesday is right\" and \"Change pickup day\" (contract PickupCard); \"Add a date\" and \"Save\" (contract DateSheet title and primary button).\n\nC. Omitted or merged states: list any cell you could not draw and why. If you drew every cell, write \"none\".\n\nD. Open questions: list only questions where two readings would give materially different components. Always include the radio-indicator question from A11.\n\nE. Publish index: every name the founder will add to the design system, one per line, in the grammar from PUBLISH, grouped by component.\n\n======================================================================\nDONE WHEN\n======================================================================\n- All 49 artboards exist, each with its exact name from the ARTBOARDS manifest printed above the frame.\n- Each of the nine components has its exact name as the h1 on its artboards and its one-line purpose printed.\n- Every variant and every state listed in this prompt appears as a row or column in that component's grid, with its printed key (B18). Every cell is drawn, including \"Does not apply\" cells with their reason.\n- Every light 01-anatomy artboard has numbered square callouts with sizes in pt/dp/px and token names, a token and contrast table, and the ACCESSIBILITY, COPY, PLATFORMS and INSTEAD OF blocks. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 01-anatomy · dark has the silhouettes, sizes, legend and table only.\n- ProvenanceMark has full light and dark sets (01–04). Every other component has a dark 02 grid.\n- Every light 03 artboard has an AX5 frame (iOS 393), a 200% frame (Android 412), a web 200% zoom frame (390; ChoiceChip also 1440), a greyscale section per B10 with a \"reads without colour\" verdict on each cell (ProvenanceMark points to its 02 greyscale column; KindGlyph shows its subset), and an INCREASE CONTRAST section. 00a · ProvenanceMark · 03-scaling-greyscale · dark has the AX5 and 200% frames, the XS strip and the Increase Contrast ink only.\n- Every surface crop that shows more than one ProvenanceMark prints the legend or a first-occurrence word once; standalone crops (widget) print the word next to every mark.\n- ProvenanceMark's stale column uses each row's own stale caption, and its tinted-widget stale cells are drawn at full tint.\n- The deadline chip reads \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" everywhere it appears, and every date row leads with the relative count beyond tomorrow.\n- No mark is drawn below 12pt, no ring stroke is under 1.5px, and the you-added tick is a cut-out in every rendering, including both tinted widget cells, each of which prints its background, tint and ratio.\n- No component other than ProvenanceMark draws a plain disc or ring, except the flagged radio indicators (B8): the selected KindGlyph tile corner and Android M3 radio buttons. No iOS or web frame draws an empty ring.\n- Every selected state has a fill, a glyph and a visible edge or weight change; the selected ChoiceChip has its 1px primary.700 outline.\n- No border token is the only edge of any chip, mark or input, including disabled ChoiceChips.\n- The kind picker is 2 columns, and every tile shows the glyph from the TILE → GLYPH map.\n- The name \"FourteenDayStrip\" is used for the calendar strip; no other name for it appears.\n- No text uses text.muted except disabled controls. Text on sunken uses text.strong. No semantic hue is used on text. No EPA AQI hue appears. No hex value appears on the board outside the token and contrast tables.\n- Every target is drawn at 44pt / 48dp / 44px (B13), and no mark or glyph is a target on its own.\n- Selection and focus look different wherever both appear.\n- Every string is from the house-style FIXTURES, from this prompt, or listed on 00a · Notes.\n- 00a · Notes contains sections A–E, and every name in section E is built only from printed keys.\n\n======================================================================\nPUBLISH (a founder step; you only prepare the index)\n======================================================================\nPublishing is done by the founder, not inside this project: once the founder accepts the board, the founder exports it and adds the nine components to the published Pantopus design system, so every later screen project can use them by name. Your job is to make that step mechanical: list every name on 00a · Notes, section E.\nThe nine component names are: ProvenanceMark · SourceCaption · ScopeChip · FreshnessLine · OfflineNotice · StatusChip · KindGlyph · AddressChip · ChoiceChip.\nName every published specimen with this grammar, one name per drawn grid cell (\"Does not apply\" cells get no name):\n  <Component> / <variant> / <state> / <size|platform> / <light|dark>\n- <variant> and <state> are the printed row and column keys (B18) exactly: lowercase, hyphenated, never containing \"/\", a fixture string or a date. The row and column labels themselves are never used in names.\n- <size|platform>:\n  ProvenanceMark: the size key the cell is drawn at (XS, S, M, L, OG); tinted-widget cells are XS.\n  KindGlyph: the variant key (row, tile, widget, tray); <variant> is the kind key (for example garbage-recycling).\n  ChoiceChip: \"any\" for every 02 grid cell; the segment and time forms drawn per platform on 01-anatomy are published as ios, android and web.\n  All other components: \"any\".\n- StatusChip's three backgrounds are one published chip; publish one name per chip per theme.\n- The complete key sets are:\n  ProvenanceMark variants official · unconfirmed · you-added · read-from-photo · stale · reported; states default · stale · in-target · tinted-widget · greyscale.\n  SourceCaption variants dated-static · dated-static-link · live · frozen · county · collapsed · no-url; states default · stale · offline.\n  ScopeChip variants saved-place · claimed-home · named-home · scope-change-pair · footer-sentence; states default · pending · declined · struck.\n  FreshnessLine variants updating · updated · failed · offline · fact-stale · widget-horizon; states fresh · refreshing · stale · failed · offline.\n  OfflineNotice variants cached-screen · queued-writes · form; states offline · reconnecting · back-online.\n  StatusChip variants upcoming · due-today · overdue · paid · expires · declined · waiting · deadline · deadline-today; state default.\n  KindGlyph variants: the 17 kind keys; states default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus; size keys row · tile · widget · tray.\n  AddressChip variants held · recovery-row · duplicate · sender; states default · selected · expired.\n  ChoiceChip variants channel · role · time · filter · segment; states default · selected · disabled · focus · selected-focus.\n- Examples: \"ProvenanceMark / official / default / S / light\" · \"ProvenanceMark / you-added / tinted-widget / XS / dark\" · \"FreshnessLine / updating / refreshing / any / light\" · \"StatusChip / overdue / default / any / light\" · \"StatusChip / deadline / default / any / dark\" · \"KindGlyph / garbage-recycling / selected / tile / light\" · \"ChoiceChip / time / selected / any / dark\" · \"ChoiceChip / segment / selected / ios / light\"."
