                  "fix": "Reword these to \"every variant and state listed in this prompt\", and state the borrowed anatomy inline (as the prompt mostly already does) without pointing to the contract."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "The x-date-sheet crop gives the sheet's primary button the wrong label.",
                  "evidence": "ScopeChip in-context b: \"above the sheet's primary button 'Add a date'\". In the contract's DateSheet, 'Add a date' is the create-mode title and the primary button is 'Save'.",
                  "fix": "Label the primary button \"Save\" and, if needed, show \"Add a date\" as the sheet title."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "The hairline's 1.2s loop reads as a conflict with the house-style rule that motion lasts 300ms or less, and the prompt does not address it.",
                  "evidence": "\"slides left to right, 1.2s loop, stops when done\" vs the house style's \"Motion must have a purpose and last 300ms or less; idle loops stop within 5s.\"",
                  "fix": "Call it the platform's system indeterminate progress indicator (no custom duration), or add a Notes A entry explaining why a progress loop is exempt from the 300ms rule."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "Rule B8 bans standalone dots and bullets, which a literal model could apply to the ' · ' middle-dot separator used in almost every string.",
                  "evidence": "B8: \"no other component, annotation, bullet, badge ... uses a plain solid circle\". Meanwhile ScopeChip ④ requires \"a middle dot with a space on each side\".",
                  "fix": "Add one sentence to B8: \"The typographic middle dot (·) in text is allowed; this rule covers drawn shapes only.\""
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "The B4 size whitelist leaves out dimensions the prompt itself uses, which could make a literal model hesitate.",
                  "evidence": "B4 says other dimensions are allowed \"as written and nowhere else\", but the prompt also uses a 360 width (\"320–360 wide\", \"below 360 px\"), a 2px dash, a 2px focus gap, 4 px end ticks, a 2pt hairline and 1px strike lines, none of which are enumerated.",
                  "fix": "Add 360 to the widths list, or soften B4 to \"plus any dimension stated explicitly in a component section\"."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "OfflineNotice has no list of consuming surface ids, although B1 requires one on every artboard.",
                  "evidence": "\"Used in: every surface with an offline state (43 of 59 prompts).\"",
                  "fix": "Either list the 43 ids or tell the model to print exactly \"every surface with an offline state (43 of 59)\" as the used-in line."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "Some KindGlyph and ChoiceChip grid details are ambiguous: the grid gets ragged extra cells, one glyph never appears in the map, and one caption rule has no default.",
                  "evidence": "KindGlyph Part B adds a \"fourth cell\" and \"fifth\" (the focus cells) only to the tile row of a 3-column grid. Glyph 2 (recycling) has no mapping in the TILE → GLYPH section. ChoiceChip R2 says \"Show only the caption for the selected role\", but the default cell has nothing selected.",
                  "fix": "Make focus and selected+focus columns 4 and 5 for every KindGlyph Part B row, with a reason on each 'does not apply' cell. Say when glyph 2 is used, for example a recycling-only reminder row. State which R2 caption, if any, appears in the default cell."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "A few fixture uses sit awkwardly with the house-style fixtures.",
                  "evidence": "AddressChip R1 'held' and R3 'duplicate … Mom’s house' both use Place B, which Jordan already saved on Sat 10 Oct as his own address. FreshnessLine R6 \"As of Mon 7:40 AM\" names today's weekday for a same-day time. The calendar-strip row \"Voter registration must arrive\" is an incomplete sentence.",
                  "fix": "Add a Notes line saying the AddressChip rows are specimen-only (Note 20 partly covers this). Use \"As of 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\" for a same-day time. Use \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\", matching the SourceCaption copy rule."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "Some content repeats or adds noise without helping the model.",
                  "evidence": "ProvenanceMark 02 already has a greyscale column, and B10 then asks for the whole 30-cell grid again in greyscale on 03. The KindGlyph greyscale repeat is 68+ cells. Notes A.29 says \"corrected stale values\", which refers to earlier drafts the model never saw. Artboard lists are repeated in each component header, the manifest, the batch plan and DONE WHEN.",
                  "fix": "Let ProvenanceMark 03 point to its 02 greyscale column instead of redrawing it. Allow KindGlyph's greyscale to show a representative subset: the 17 row glyphs plus Part B. Delete the word \"corrected\" from A.29."
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "clean": false
      },
      {
        "prompt": {
          "id": "00b",
          "name": "Foundations board: Data instruments",
          "componentsCovered": [
            "ScaleStrip",
            "AqiBand",
            "FourteenDayStrip",
            "YearBand",
            "SlotMeter",
            "PublicPointMap",
            "FactCount"
          ],
          "artboardCount": 57,
          "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is the Foundations board: Data instruments.\n\nTYPE: NEW (a component specimen board). This board designs no screens. It draws seven components as reference specimens: ScaleStrip, AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, SlotMeter, PublicPointMap and FactCount. Fifty-nine later screen prompts will ask for these components by exact name. Each of those screens is designed in a separate project that cannot see this one, so once this board is published, its specimen is the only definition of each component. Draw every number, token and string exactly as written here.\n\nPREREQUISITES: boards 00a, 00c and 00d should be published in the Pantopus design system before this board, because this board borrows parts from them. If one of them is not published yet, draw each borrowed part as a stand-in from the anatomy below. Label each stand-in in the gutter \"stand-in — the 00a/00c/00d specimen replaces it\". Do not design these parts any further.\n- 00a · ProvenanceMark: see C11.\n- 00a · SourceCaption: one caption line (12/16) in text.secondary (text.strong on sunken): [ProvenanceMark S] authority · scope word · as-of. It wraps and never truncates.\n- 00a · FreshnessLine: one caption line in text.secondary, with an optional 16pt leading glyph. It states age in words.\n- 00a · ScopeChip: a 24pt pill on surface.sunken with a 12pt person or house glyph and the label in label 13/18 text.strong.\n- 00a · KindGlyph: a 24pt outline icon in text.secondary.\n- 00c · InlineErrorRow: a row in the component's own slot. It holds a 16pt error glyph (semantic.error on the glyph only), the sentence in body text.primary, and a 44pt \"Retry\" text button (primary.700). No tinted background.\n- 00c · DateRow: a row at least 56pt tall. It holds a leading 24pt KindGlyph, the title in body text.primary, and line 2 in caption. Line 2 gives the relative and absolute date (\"Tomorrow\", or \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\") and a short SourceCaption. A ProvenanceMark S sits at the trailing edge. Highlighted state (light): an infoBg wash plus a 1px semantic.info outline. For the dark highlighted state, see C6.\n- 00c · FactRow: a 56pt row. The label is in bodySmall text.secondary, above the value in body text.primary. The row also holds a ProvenanceMark and a trailing chevron.\n- 00c · TextActionRow (outbound variant): a bordered row with a 1px text.secondary edge, at least 44pt tall. It holds a verb-led label in primary.700 and a trailing external-link glyph \"↗\".\n- 00d · WarmingSkeleton: surface.sunken shapes with the component's final geometry and radius, and no text. It reserves the exact final height. It shimmers by default and is static under Reduce Motion.\n- 00d · QuietDayReceipt (the strip line and the year-band line only): one line with a 16pt bare stroked check glyph in text.secondary (a line-drawn check with no disc; see grammar rule 4) and the sentence in bodySmall text.primary. The sentence always starts with the word \"Checked\".\n\nATTACH: no screenshots are required. The founder may attach current shipped screenshots of the Today air band (surface f1-today-air-band), the privacy map (f9-privacy-mirror), the cells map (f9-nearby-cells-map) and the Block Founders panel (f9-block-founders-panel). If they do, treat the screenshots only as a record of what exists today. The specimens on this board replace the instrument parts of those screens, so do not copy an attached instrument's colours, ramps or geometry.\n\nWHAT THIS BOARD IS FOR\nThe board holds the reading instruments: scales, strips, bands, meters, maps and counts. They share one grammar:\n(1) Each instrument states a fact in words and numbers. The graphic repeats the fact and never replaces it.\n(2) Nothing adds up to a grade, score, percentage or verdict.\n(3) Nothing depends on colour alone. The AQI hues are the one sanctioned colour scale, and even there the category is printed in words.\n(4) Three shapes mean provenance (00a · ProvenanceMark) and nothing else, including inside these instruments: a filled disc, a ring, and a disc with a knocked-out tick. That is why position markers are never discs or rings; they are vertical capsules or triangle pointers. There is one exception: the bare stroked check in a QuietDayReceipt line. It has no disc, it is always followed by the word \"Checked\", and it never appears at a mark position. This exception is listed on Notes as an open question for 00d.\n(5) A mark or cell is never a tap target by itself. The target is the row, the whole strip, or a labelled button.\n(6) Each instrument has a one-sentence summary and a spoken label, and the same facts appear nearby as a list.\n(7) Every provenance mark keeps at least 3:1 contrast in every state. Staleness is stated in words and never shown by dimming a mark.\n\n======================================================================\nBOARD CONVENTIONS (these apply to every artboard on this board)\n======================================================================\nC0 · Artboard naming. This board overrides the house artboard pattern. Name every artboard \"00b · <Component> · <NN-name> · <light|dark>\", exactly as written in the ARTBOARDS manifest. The last artboard is \"00b · Notes\".\nC1 · Canvas. Each artboard is 1440 wide, with whatever height it needs. Use surface.app for light artboards and dark surface.app #020617 for dark ones. Print the artboard name above the artboard in label 13/18 text.strong, exactly as written in the ARTBOARDS manifest.\nC2 · Specimen frames. Draw specimens at true size (1pt = 1px on the artboard) inside plain frames: iOS 393 wide, Android 412 wide, web-390 and web-1440, as named.\n- Phone frames (iOS 393, Android 412 and web-390): draw the specimen card 358 wide with 16pt padding, which leaves 326pt of content width, and centre the card in the frame. The 16pt side-margin rule describes web-390 only; in the wider frames the leftover space is split evenly. All phone geometry below assumes 326pt content width unless it says otherwise. Widgets use their own sizes.\n- Web-1440 card widths: ScaleStrip 640px (608px content); FourteenDayStrip 648px (616px content, so each cell is 44px); YearBand 880px (848px content). The AqiBand instrument row takes the ScaleStrip right column. FactCount keeps its 160pt maximum width.\n- Cards use surface.base, radius lg 12, shadow sm and padding 16. In dark mode, cards use dark surface.raised #1E293B with a 1px dark border.strong #374151 edge, because border.default has no contrast on raised.\nC3 · Callouts. Draw callouts in an annotation gutter outside the UI, in caption 12/16 text.strong. Leader lines are 1px text.secondary and end in a short perpendicular tick, not a dot, so an annotation is never mistaken for a provenance mark. Each callout names the part, its size in pt/dp/px and its token name, for example \"Track · 12pt · fill surface.raised · keyline 1px text.secondary\". Callouts appear only on 01-anatomy artboards and where an artboard below asks for them.\nC4 · Grids. A variant × state grid has a header row for states and a header column for variants, both in label 13/18 text.strong. Each cell holds one specimen at true size. If a combination has no meaning, the cell prints \"n/a — <reason>\" in caption text.secondary and draws nothing else. Each n/a cell has exactly one reason, as given below. Never leave a cell blank.\nC5 · Absence specimens. When a state renders nothing (fail-closed), draw the host context around the gap. In the gutter, add a dashed 1px text.secondary annotation box reading \"Nothing renders here. No space is reserved and no message is shown.\" The box is an annotation, not UI. Only SlotMeter has absence states. An error state that shows an InlineErrorRow is not an absence state and is not drawn per C5.\nC6 · Dark artboards. Use only these dark values:\n- Surfaces: base #0F172A · raised #1E293B · app #020617 · sunken #0F172A · muted #111827.\n- Text: primary #E5E7EB · secondary #94A3B8 · strong #F1F5F9.\n- Borders: default #1F2937 · strong #374151.\n- Focus and link: #38BDF8.\n- These light tokens keep their light values in dark mode, with their contrast on dark raised #1E293B checked: semantic.error glyph (3.03:1), semantic.warning glyph (4.59:1) and the primary.600 fill (3.57:1). Draw them by token name.\n- Every \"text.secondary\" ink becomes #94A3B8, every \"text.primary\" becomes #E5E7EB and every \"text.strong\" becomes #F1F5F9.\n- The primary.700 text buttons and links (\"+ Add a date\", \"See the spot\", \"List cells\" and \"Retry\") become #38BDF8. The SlotMeter taken-segment edge (primary.700 in light) also becomes #38BDF8, because primary.700 is 2.47:1 on #1E293B.\n- Dark highlighted DateRow: a dark base #0F172A wash plus a 1px #38BDF8 outline. Its text is #E5E7EB, at 14.4:1. The light infoBg wash is never used on dark.\n- On dark cards (raised #1E293B), surface.sunken fills (#0F172A) look darker than the card. That is intended; their keylines and text carry the edges.\n- AqiBand segment gaps use the host surface, which is dark raised #1E293B on cards. Marker and pointer halos stay dark base #0F172A, so the two-tone marker keeps one fixed dark tone.\n- The AQI hues do not change in dark mode.\n- No selection state is drawn on this board.\nC7 · AX5 and 200% artboards.\n- iOS AX5 sizes to draw: h1 → 58 · h2 → 58 · h3 → 55 · body/bodyMedium → 53 · bodySmall → 49 · label → 44 · caption → 43 · overline → 40.\n- Android 200% sizes to draw (Android 14 non-linear scaling): h1 → 38 · h2 → 36 · h3 → 34 · body → 28 · bodySmall → 26 · label → 25 · caption → 24 · overline → 22.\n- Web: 200% browser zoom on web-1440, which gives an effective layout of 720 CSS px.\n- Graphic geometry keeps its size, and text reflows around it. This covers tracks, cells, segments, markers, glyph-only buttons, and the marks inside strip cells, lanes and tracks. Marks that sit inside text lines (SourceCaption, DateRow, legends) scale with their text.\n- Text wraps and never truncates or ellipsises. Pairs that sit side by side stack.\nC8 · Greyscale artboards. Redraw the listed specimens at 100% desaturation. Under each one, print a caption in text.secondary that names the non-colour cue that still carries the meaning, for example \"Occupied band: 2px outline + printed name\".\nC9 · Motion. Show motion as static annotated frames, never as a loop. Annotate Reduce Motion wherever it changes something: skeletons become static, and highlights appear without animation.\nC10 · Fixtures and clocks. Use the house-style FIXTURES exactly. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific. Air specimens use these clocks, because AirNow readings are hourly and a reading's age decides its state:\n- Ready and offline Air specimens (and every instrument or crop that contains one) are drawn at specimen time 7:10 AM on Mon 19 Oct, so \"observed 7:00 AM\" is a fresh reading.\n- Alert and still-above specimens are drawn at specimen time 4:10 PM.\n- Stale Air specimens use TODAY, 6:10 PM, which gives \"— 11 hours ago\".\n- Print \"specimen time 7:10 AM\" or \"specimen time 4:10 PM\" once in the gutter of every artboard that shows such a specimen.\nAny string that is not in the fixtures, the contract or this prompt must be listed on 00b · Notes. When a specimen shows a value that is not tied to a fixture address (for example Zone AE), label it \"specimen value\" in the gutter.\nC11 · Provenance marks inside instruments are 00a · ProvenanceMark, drawn at size XS (12pt) or S (16pt).\n- OFFICIAL is a solid disc.\n- ON RECORD, NOT CONFIRMED is a ring with a stroke of at least 1.5px.\n- YOU ADDED is a solid disc with a knocked-out tick.\n- The ink is text.secondary or darker, always at full opacity.\n- Stale style on this board: the same shape at full ink, paired with the age words. The contract's 50% opacity is not used, because text.secondary at 50% is 1.9–2.0:1 on base and sunken, below the 3:1 graphics rule. This deviation is listed on Notes.\nSource lines are 00a · SourceCaption (authority · scope word · as-of). Freshness lines are 00a · FreshnessLine, and skeletons are 00d · WarmingSkeleton. Draw each of them exactly as named, and do not redesign them here.\nC12 · Focus on web. Keyboard focus is a 2px border.focus outline with a 2px offset around the focusable element (a row, a strip or a button). In dark mode the outline is #38BDF8.\nC13 · Micro-geometry. A few offsets below are deliberately off the 4px spacing scale: 6pt, 3pt, 2pt and 1pt, used for cell padding, bar offsets, mark shifts and numeral nudges. They are intentional micro-geometry inside an instrument. Draw them as written, and do not use them for layout spacing anywhere else.\nC14 · Standalone words. Widgets and the OG card are standalone surfaces, so they print the provenance word next to each mark or include an in-block legend line. Every widget block below says how it does this.\n\n======================================================================\n1 · ScaleStrip\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: The four-layer reading instrument. It has one row per authority, drawn on that authority's own ordered bands, and it never adds up to a grade.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light, with a callout on every part):\n- Row order is fixed and never re-sorted: Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon.\n- Each row, from top to bottom:\n  - the layer name in label 13/18/600 text.strong\n  - the value line \"Word · number\" in bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary\n  - the track\n  - the band names under the track\n  - a 00a · SourceCaption.\n- Layout by container width:\n  - Below 560pt (phones, web-390, and the compare size at 390): text above the track, with the track at full content width (326pt).\n  - 560pt and wider (web-1440): two columns with a 16pt gap. The left column (40%) stacks the layer name, the value line and the SourceCaption. The right column (60%) holds the track zone with the band names under it, and its top aligns with the value line.\n  - AX5 or 200%: always stacked, with the track at full width.\n  - OG: its own recipe (see 05-og-column).\n- Row padding is 12pt top and bottom. Gaps: 4pt between the layer name and the value line, 8pt between the value line and the track zone, 4pt between the track zone and the band names, and 8pt between the band names and the SourceCaption.\n- Row height is at least 48pt at detail size. The whole row is one target: at least 44pt on iOS and web, and 48dp on Android.\n- Track zone: 24pt tall, with a 12pt track centred vertically.\n- Track:\n  - Bands have equal width within a layer, and each layer has its own bands. There is no shared axis across layers.\n  - Band fill is surface.raised.\n  - Bands are divided by 1.5px separators in text.secondary ink (4.83:1).\n  - A 1px text.secondary keyline with radius xs 4 surrounds the whole track.\n  - The least hazard is on the left and the most hazard on the right.\n- Occupied band: a 2px text.primary outline drawn inside that band's edges.\n- Marker: a vertical capsule 4pt wide × 20pt tall, radius pill, with a text.primary core and a 2px surface.base halo (8pt × 24pt overall). It is centred horizontally in the occupied band and extends 4pt above and 4pt below the 12pt track. It is never a disc, so it cannot be read as the \"Official\" mark.\n- Band names under the track, in caption 12/16 text.secondary. Each name may take up to 2 lines and is never truncated.\n  - 3-band layers (Flood, Radon) print every band name under its band.\n  - The 5-band layer (Wildfire) prints only the two end names and the occupied band's name.\n  - The occupied band's name is always in captionMedium 12/16/500 text.primary, directly under the marker. If it would come within 8pt of an end name, it replaces that end name.\n  - The Air row prints the AqiBand range labels (\"0–50\" · \"51–100\" · \"101–150\" · \"151–200\" · \"201–300\" · \"301+\") instead of band names, with the occupied range in captionMedium text.primary.\n- Layers and their bands:\n  - Flood (3 bands, by annual chance): \"Minimal (X)\" · \"0.2% a year (shaded X)\" · \"1% a year or more (A/V zones)\". The value line prints the actual zone code.\n  - Wildfire (5 USFS classes): \"Very low\" · \"Low\" · \"Moderate\" · \"High\" · \"Very high\".\n  - Radon (3 bands, ordered Zone 3 → Zone 2 → Zone 1): \"Zone 3 · low potential\" · \"Zone 2 · moderate potential\" · \"Zone 1 · highest potential\". Radon never uses \"N of M\".\n  - Air: the track is AqiBand in its instrument-row variant (12pt tall, EPA hues), the only coloured track in the instrument. Its value line is \"AQI 42 · Good\"; the pollutant is left out inside the instrument.\n- Sizes to draw: detail (full phone width, 326pt content), compare (390 frame) and the OG column (see 05-og-column).\n- Fixture rows at detail size (HOME A readings; the Air row is at specimen time 7:10 AM):\n  - Flood · label \"Flood zone\" · value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · band 1 occupied · caption \"● FEMA · area zone · effective Sep 2021\"\n  - Wildfire · label \"Wildfire hazard potential\" · value \"Moderate · 3 of 5\" · band 3 occupied · caption \"● USFS · quarter-mile area · 2023\"\n  - Air · label \"Air quality index (AQI)\" · value \"AQI 42 · Good\" · marker at 84% of the Good segment · caption \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\"\n  - Radon · label \"Radon zone\" · value \"Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\" · band 3 occupied · caption \"● EPA · county-wide estimate — only a test tells you about this home\"\n  - All four sources are Official (filled). The scope word carries the county scope.\n- Summary: the four value lines are the visible summary. The instrument's one-sentence summary is the web text alternative and the native group label: \"Flood Zone X, minimal flood hazard. Wildfire Moderate, 3 of 5. Air AQI 42, Good. Radon Zone 1, county-wide.\" Print it under the 01 fixture instrument.\n- Specimen value (label it \"specimen value\" in the gutter): the flood value \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\", with band 3 occupied.\n\nVARIANTS (every one must appear on this board):\nV1 Flood · V2 Wildfire · V3 Radon · V4 Air (AqiBand instrument row). These appear on 01 and 02.\nV5 compare (on 03, 06 and 08):\n- Two pointers on one track. In compare mode, the capsule marker is not drawn.\n- Compare track zone, top to bottom: a 16pt line holding \"Dana\" (captionMedium text.primary) · an 8pt sender pointer · the 12pt track · an 8pt \"You\" pointer · a 16pt line holding \"You\" (captionMedium text.primary). Total: 60pt. The band names sit 4pt below the \"You\" line.\n- The sender pointer is a downward triangle, 12pt wide × 8pt tall, in text.primary with a 2px surface.base halo. Its tip touches the top edge of the track.\n- The \"You\" pointer is the same triangle mirrored upward, with its tip touching the bottom edge of the track.\n- Both pointers have the same form, size and ink. Each is centred in its band; on the Air row, each is placed by value within its segment.\n- Each occupied band gets the 2px text.primary outline. When both readings fall in the same band, only that one band is outlined.\n- \"You\" is the recipient's own address, not HOME A. Its readings are specimen values; label them so in the gutter.\n- Value lines: if the readings differ, the row prints two value lines, \"Dana: <value>\" and \"You: <value>\". If they share a band, it prints one value line prefixed \"Both:\".\n- If both readings fall in the same band, the two pointers share one x position and the row shows the merged label chip \"Same band\". If they differ, the row shows the neutral chip \"Different band\".\n- Chip: a pill 24pt tall with a surface.sunken fill, in captionMedium text.strong, with no glyph and no hue. It is right-aligned on the layer-name line.\n- The header above a compare instrument reads \"Dana · Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\".\nV6 no data (on 02): a greyed track (bands filled surface.sunken; keyline and separators unchanged), with no marker and no occupied outline. The value line reads \"Not on record\". V6 applies to Flood, Wildfire and Radon. The Air row shows the AqiBand no-reading row instead (see the 02 cell rules).\nV7 not studied, Flood only (on 02): a greyed track with no marker. The value line reads \"FEMA hasn't mapped flood hazard here\".\nV8 non-burnable, Wildfire only (on 02): a greyed track with no marker. The value line reads \"Non-burnable land cover (USFS)\".\nV6, V7 and V8 must each look different from Wildfire \"Very low\", which is a normal track with band 1 occupied.\nV9 frozen (on 02 and 03): every caption ends with \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\", and the frozen Air caption reads \"AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\". The value line for frozen air reads \"AQI 42 · Good · on Sat 12 Sep\".\nV10 collapsed text line (the arrival header below 640px; on 03 and 08): one row of body text that wraps, at least 44pt tall, with the whole row as the target: \"Dana · Camas, WA · Flood X · Wildfire Moderate · Air 42 · Radon Zone 1 ›\". This variant draws no tracks.\n\nSTATES (every one must appear on this board):\n- loading (02, 04): a 00d · WarmingSkeleton showing the track keyline and separators only, with no fill, no marker and no text. The label and value line become surface.sunken bars (60×12 and 140×16). The exact row height is reserved.\n- ready (01–04).\n- partial, loading (04): some rows are ready while others are still loading.\n- partial, failed (04): the Air row shows a 00c · InlineErrorRow, \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" + Retry (44pt), in its own slot. The other three rows stay ready.\n- differs tag (03, 06): the neutral chip \"Different band\".\n- stale air row (02, 04): drawn at TODAY 6:10 PM. The Air row keeps its value and marker. Its caption becomes \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", and its ProvenanceMark stays at full ink (C11). The age words carry the staleness. The other three rows are unchanged.\n- AX5 (06): text stacked above a full-width track.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light and · dark:\n  - one detail-size Wildfire row with every callout from ANATOMY\n  - the full 4-row fixture instrument in an iOS 393 frame, with its summary sentence under it\n  - the same instrument in two columns on web-1440 (640px card), with a callout on the column split.\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon.\n  - Grid columns: loading · ready · no data · not studied / non-burnable · stale · frozen.\n  - Cell rules:\n    - Flood × not studied is V7. The Flood ready cell also shows the Zone AE specimen value under the Zone X row.\n    - Wildfire × not studied / non-burnable is V8.\n    - Air × no data is the AqiBand V4 no-reading instrument row (greyed segments, \"No reading for this address right now\"), not V6.\n    - Air × not studied / non-burnable: \"n/a — AirNow has no such class; see AqiBand no reading\".\n    - Radon × not studied / non-burnable: \"n/a — EPA zones cover every county\".\n    - Stale applies to Air only. Flood, Wildfire and Radon print \"n/a — dated datasets carry their effective date, not an age\".\n  - Add one extra row, \"Wildfire very low (for contrast)\". It shows ready with band 1 occupied, next to V6 and V8, so the difference is visible.\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light and · dark:\n  - A compare instrument in a web-390 frame for \"Dana · Camas, WA\" vs You, with the rows in the order Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon:\n    - Flood: both in band 1, \"Same band\", value line \"Both: Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n    - Wildfire: Dana Moderate 3 of 5 vs You Low 2 of 5, \"Different band\", value lines \"Dana: Moderate · 3 of 5\" and \"You: Low · 2 of 5\".\n    - Air: Dana has AQI 42, frozen \"on Sat 12 Sep\"; You have AQI 42 today, observed 7:00 AM (specimen time 7:10 AM). Both are in Good, \"Same band\". The pointers sit inside the Good segment. Value line \"Both: AQI 42 · Good\". The row shows two captions, one per line: \"Dana: AirNow · on Sat 12 Sep 2026\" and \"You: AirNow · observed 7:00 AM\".\n    - Radon: both Zone 1, \"Same band\", value line \"Both: Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n  - Under the instrument, print the compare spoken label (see ACCESSIBILITY).\n  - Beside it: the V10 collapsed text line at 390 and at 320 wide, where it wraps to 3 lines.\n  - Then the compare row in the two-column layout on web-1440.\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light and · dark:\n  - The full 4-row instrument five times, in iOS 393 frames: loading · ready · partial (Air loading) · partial (Air failed) · stale air row.\n  - Under the ready instrument, print all four row spoken labels.\n  - Under each other instrument, print only the labels that change: loading = the container label \"Loading\" (read once); partial (Air loading) = \"Loading\" for the Air row; partial (Air failed) = the failed Air label; stale air row = the stale Air label.\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 05-og-column · light (light only, because the share card is light only):\n  - One 1200×630 frame with 16px padding at top and bottom. On the left, a 520px-wide text-and-track column for \"Dana · Camas, WA\". Print \"Yours?\" in the empty right-hand column. Do not draw a full card design; f8-og-compare-card owns that.\n  - Header: \"Dana · Camas, WA\" at 40px on a 48px line, then a 24px gap (72px in total).\n  - Four rows, each 112px tall: 8px top · one 40px line (48px line height) holding the layer word and value · an 8px gap · a 40px track zone holding a 30px track · 8px bottom. There are no band names and no per-row captions; the value line carries the band word.\n    - \"Flood · Zone X — minimal\"\n    - \"Wildfire · Moderate · 3 of 5\"\n    - \"Air · AQI 42 · Good\"\n    - \"Radon · Zone 1 (county)\"\n  - OG marker: the capsule scaled to 8px × 40px with a 4px halo, extending 5px above and below the 30px track.\n  - Footer: a 24px gap, then one sources line that spans the full 1168px width, at 28px (36px line height). It holds a 28px ProvenanceMark followed by \"Official · FEMA Sep 2021 · USFS 2023 · AirNow Sat 12 Sep · EPA county-wide\". The word \"Official\" is printed because this is a standalone surface (C14). The 28px size is a recorded deviation from the 40px text minimum (see Notes).\n  - Height budget: 16 + 72 + 4 × 112 + 60 + 16 = 612px, within 630. Print this budget in the gutter.\n  - Each value line stays on one line. If a line would not fit in 520px, the text column may widen to at most 640px and the \"Yours?\" column narrows. Value and header text never drops below 40px.\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 06-ax5-200 · light:\n  - The 4-row instrument at iOS AX5 (393 frame, scrolling as tall as needed).\n  - The same instrument at Android 200% (412 frame).\n  - The compare Wildfire row at AX5. The pointer labels and the \"Different band\" chip move onto their own lines above the track, and the \"You\" label stays below the track.\n  - Web-1440 at 200% zoom, switched to the stacked layout.\n  - One Wildfire row at iOS Increase Contrast, with the separators, keyline and occupied outline in text.primary.\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 07-greyscale · light: artboards 02 and 03 (light) desaturated. The caption under each names its cues: position + printed band name + outline; \"Different band\" in words; the pointer labels \"Dana\" and \"You\".\n- 00b · ScaleStrip · 08-in-context · light: three mini crops, each showing only the host card.\n  (a) f8-scale-strips on web-1440: the instrument in two columns in the /start preview card, with the ProvenanceMark legend line \"● Official\".\n  (b) f6-place-section-details on iOS 393: the instrument in the Place section, with the 00c · TextActionRow \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" under the Radon row.\n  (c) f8-compare-arrival-header on web-390: the V10 collapsed line above the address field. Next to it, f8-compare-reveal on web-390 showing the Wildfire compare row.\n  Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f8-compare-sheet → V5 compare at 390 (phone sheet width) · f8-og-compare-card → the 05-og-column recipe.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- The instrument's one-sentence summary is given in ANATOMY.\n- Each row is one element that reads its full spoken label. Print these on 04 (under the ready instrument):\n  - Flood: \"Flood zone: Zone X, minimal flood hazard, scale Minimal to 1% a year or more. FEMA, effective September 2021. Official.\"\n  - Wildfire: \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate, 3 of 5, scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023. Official.\"\n  - Air: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM. Official.\"\n  - Radon: \"Radon zone: Zone 1, highest potential, scale Zone 3 to Zone 1. EPA, county-wide. Official.\"\n- The changed labels, also printed on 04:\n  - Stale Air: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM, 11 hours ago. Official.\"\n  - Failed Air: \"Air quality: We couldn't reach AirNow just now.\" The Retry button is named \"Retry air quality\".\n  - Loading: \"Loading\", read once for the container.\n- Compare label, printed on 03: \"Wildfire hazard potential. Dana: Moderate, 3 of 5. You: Low, 2 of 5. Different band. Scale Very low to Very high. USFS 2023.\"\n- Meaning comes from position plus a printed name, never from colour.\n- Row target: 44pt on iOS and web, 48dp on Android. The marker and pointers are never targets.\n- A table equivalent is implicit, because every row is text.\n- Web: the row is focusable and has the C12 focus ring.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n- Approved strings, used verbatim:\n  - \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\"\n  - \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year (about 1 in 4 over 30 years)\"\n  - \"Wildfire hazard potential: Moderate · 3 of 5\"\n  - \"Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\"\n- Always pair a word with a number, except for Radon.\n- Sender rows describe places: \"Dana · Camas, WA — what's on record for this area\".\n- Outbound actions start with a verb: \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\".\n- Never write \"100-year floodplain\", \"minimal risk\", \"wildfire risk\", \"better\", \"worse\" or \"wins\".\n\nPLATFORMS: web draws the instrument as SVG. iOS (SwiftUI) and Android (Compose) draw it natively. The geometry is identical everywhere, and only the target minimums differ (44pt iOS · 48dp Android · 44px web). The OG render follows the 05-og-column recipe: header and value text at 40px or more, and the single sources line at 28px (a recorded deviation).\n\nINSTEAD OF (ScaleStrip):\n- Instead of a letter grade, score, star, radar chart or one combined colour ramp across layers, draw four separate rows on each authority's own bands, because the layers come from different authorities and never sum to a verdict.\n- Instead of a shared 0–100 axis, draw equal-width bands per layer, because each authority's classes are different.\n- Instead of re-sorting rows by the distance between two readings, keep the order Flood · Wildfire · Air · Radon, because people compare rows by position.\n- Instead of arrows, trophies or better/worse words, draw the neutral chip \"Different band\" or \"Same band\", because a difference between places is not a ranking.\n- Instead of a disc marker, draw the vertical capsule, because a disc reads as ● Official.\n- Instead of a filled marker for the sender and a ring for \"You\", draw two identical triangle pointers labelled \"Dana\" and \"You\", because filled vs hollow means provenance only.\n- Instead of the four-band flood scale \"X · X shaded · AE · VE\", draw the three annual-chance bands with the zone code in the value line, because the contract groups A and V zones by annual chance.\n- Instead of drawing \"Not on record\" like \"Very low\", draw a greyed track with no marker and the words, because no data is not a low reading.\n- Instead of band names and captions on every OG row, print one value line per row and a single sources line, because text-heavy OG images fail at thumbnail size.\n\n======================================================================\n2 · AqiBand\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: The one officially coloured scale: the EPA AQI with its category name, drawn the same way everywhere air appears.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy with callouts):\n- Six equal-width category segments in the EPA ColorVision Assist hues. These are the only non-token colours in the product. Name them on the board as the swatches aqi.good, aqi.moderate, aqi.usg, aqi.unhealthy, aqi.veryUnhealthy and aqi.hazardous, with their RGB values:\n  - Good 158,255,145\n  - Moderate 255,201,5\n  - Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups 255,130,5\n  - Unhealthy 240,34,0\n  - Very Unhealthy 137,9,151\n  - Hazardous 100,0,21\n- Segment heights: 16pt at detail size (Today), 12pt in the instrument row, and 8pt in the widget micro variant.\n- 2px gaps between segments, in the host surface colour (surface.base on light cards; dark raised #1E293B on dark cards).\n- Each segment has its own 1px keyline in text.secondary ink (dark text.secondary in dark mode), because yellow is 1.07:1 on white and maroon is 1.62:1 on dark base. The outer corners of the first and last segments have radius xs 4.\n- Detail width: (326 − 5×2) ÷ 6 = 52.7pt per segment.\n- Range labels are centred under each segment, in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"0–50\" · \"51–100\" · \"101–150\" · \"151–200\" · \"201–300\" · \"301+\". The occupied segment's label switches to captionMedium text.primary, and the occupied segment gets a 2px text.primary inner outline.\n- Marker: the same vertical capsule as ScaleStrip, 4pt wide with a text.primary core and a 2px surface.base halo (the halo is #0F172A in dark mode). Its height is the segment height + 8pt: 24pt at detail size, 20pt in the instrument row, and 16pt in the widget micro. It passes 3:1 on every hue in both themes, because one of its two tones always contrasts.\n  - Position within the segment = (value − segment low) ÷ (segment high − segment low). AQI 42 sits at 84% of Good, and AQI 118 sits at 35% of Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups.\n  - Values above 500 clamp to the right end of \"301+\", and the number is still printed.\n- Value line above the band, in bodyMedium text.primary: \"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\" (fixture) or \"AQI 118 · Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups · PM2.5\" (alert). The category name and number are always printed on the card in text.primary, never on a fill. The value line is the band's visible one-sentence summary. Inside ScaleStrip the pollutant is left out (\"AQI 42 · Good\").\n- Health statement below the band, in body 16/24 text.primary, verbatim from EPA:\n  - Good: \"Air quality is satisfactory, and air pollution poses little or no risk.\"\n  - Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups: \"Members of sensitive groups may experience health effects. The general public is less likely to be affected.\" It is followed by the PM2.5 sensitive-groups line \"People with heart or lung disease, older adults, children, and people of lower socioeconomic status are the groups most at risk.\" Flag this line on Notes to be checked against EPA TAD Table 4.\n- Pantopus context, when present, goes in a separate block below the statement: the overline \"PANTOPUS NOTE\", then bodySmall text.primary. Draw it only on the alert specimen: \"Your alert level is 101. You can change it in Notifications.\"\n- Optional threshold rule at the user's chosen threshold (101, 151 or 201):\n  - a 1.5px dashed (3 on / 2 off) vertical rule in text.primary at the threshold's position, extending 6pt above and below the band\n  - its number above it, in caption text.primary (\"101\")\n  - the line \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\" in bodySmallMedium text.primary, with a leading 16pt alert glyph in semantic.warning (the hue goes on the glyph only).\n  - The fixture threshold is 101, the server default. Also draw one specimen at 151, labelled \"threshold 151 (not crossed)\".\n- 00a · SourceCaption: \"● AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM\" (alert: \"observed 4:00 PM\").\n\nVARIANTS: V1 detail (Today) · V2 instrument row (inside ScaleStrip, 12pt, no health statement) · V3 widget micro (medium widget; no numbers under the segments, and the name and number sit beside the band) · V4 no reading · V5 alert (threshold rule + 00a · ScopeChip \"Your household\") · V6 still above threshold, no new push.\n\nSTATES:\n- ready (specimen time 7:10 AM).\n- stale (TODAY, 6:10 PM): the hues and marker are unchanged. The caption becomes \"AirNow · nearest monitors · observed 7:00 AM — 11 hours ago\", and the ProvenanceMark stays at full ink (C11).\n- no reading (V4):\n  - Segments are filled surface.sunken and keep their keylines. There is no marker and no occupied outline, and the range labels stay.\n  - The value line is replaced by \"No reading for this address right now\" (body text.primary).\n  - When the provider itself failed, a second specimen adds a 00c · InlineErrorRow: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now\" + Retry.\n- alert (V5, specimen time 4:10 PM): the threshold rule, \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", the ScopeChip \"Your household\" and the PANTOPUS NOTE.\n- still above threshold (V6, specimen time 4:10 PM): the same band as the alert, plus the line \"Still above your alert level (101) since 4:00 PM. No new alert until it drops below 101 and rises again.\" in bodySmall text.primary.\n- offline (specimen time 7:10 AM): the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" above the band, with the band drawn from cache.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light and · dark: the V1 detail card at AQI 42 on iOS 393 with every callout, plus a swatch row showing the six hues with their names and RGB values. In the dark version the hues are unchanged, the gaps use dark raised #1E293B (the card surface), and the marker halo is #0F172A.\n- 00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: detail · instrument row · widget micro.\n  - Grid columns: ready · stale · no reading · alert · still above threshold · offline.\n  - Detail row:\n    - × ready: V1 at AQI 42.\n    - × stale: V1 with the stale caption.\n    - × no reading: V4, with the provider-failed specimen beneath it.\n    - × alert: V5 at AQI 118.\n    - × still above threshold: V6.\n    - × offline: V1 under the FreshnessLine.\n  - Instrument row:\n    - × ready: V2 at AQI 42, with the value \"AQI 42 · Good\" and the range labels.\n    - × stale: V2 with the stale caption.\n    - × no reading: V2 greyed, with \"No reading for this address right now\".\n    - × alert: V2 at AQI 118 with the threshold rule, and no health statement or PANTOPUS NOTE.\n    - × still above threshold: \"n/a — the still-above line belongs to the detail card; the row keeps its alert form\".\n    - × offline: \"n/a — the host instrument shows one FreshnessLine for all four rows\".\n  - Widget micro:\n    - × ready: V3, \"Air · Good 42\".\n    - × stale: \"n/a — widget age is the widget's own 'As of' line (f7-today-widget)\".\n    - × no reading: V3 with greyed segments and \"Air · No reading\".\n    - × alert: V3 at AQI 118, \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\", with no threshold rule.\n    - × still above threshold: \"n/a — widgets show only the current reading\".\n    - × offline: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\".\n  - Under the grid:\n    - the threshold 151 (not crossed) specimen at AQI 118\n    - a clamp specimen at AQI 612 (specimen value), with the marker at the right end and the value line \"AQI 612 · Hazardous · PM2.5\"\n    - six capsule-marker specimens, one on each segment, showing that the two-tone capsule passes 3:1 in both themes.\n- 00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · light and · dark:\n  - A medium widget, 338×158pt, with 306pt of content width. The band is 120×8pt, with no range labels and no health statement.\n  - Beside the band, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"Air · Good 42\". The alert version reads \"Air · Sensitive groups 118\". The short form \"Sensitive groups\" is allowed only in widgets.\n  - The caption line, at 11pt or more, is an XS filled ProvenanceMark followed by \"Official · AirNow · 7:00 AM\". The word \"Official\" is printed because this is a standalone surface (C14).\n  - Draw it three times:\n    - iOS in full colour.\n    - iOS tinted/accented rendering, where every hue flattens to one tint. The gaps and keylines keep the six segments readable, the printed name carries the meaning, and the mark keeps its silhouette.\n    - Android, where the EPA hues stay fixed and never follow dynamic colour, while the rest of the widget follows the house tokens.\n  - Widget composition belongs to f7-today-widget. Draw only this block.\n- 00b · AqiBand · 04-ax5-200 · light:\n  - V5 alert at iOS AX5: the range labels leave the band and become a legend list below it, with one row per category, each at least 44pt tall and growing with its text. Each row holds a 16pt swatch with keyline, the EPA name and the range.\n  - The value line, statement and note wrap, and the band keeps full width.\n  - The same at Android 200%.\n  - At AX sizes the V3 widget falls back to text only: \"Air · Good 42 · Official · AirNow 7:00 AM\".\n- 00b · AqiBand · 05-greyscale · light: 01 and 02 (light) desaturated. Caption: \"Segments separated by gaps and keylines; category printed in words; marker by two-tone capsule.\"\n- 00b · AqiBand · 06-in-context · light:\n  (a) f1-today-air-band on iOS 393: the alert landing card with the ScopeChip \"Your household\" and the header \"2418 NE Larkspur Loop\".\n  (b) x-provenance-sheet on Android 412: the sheet header \"Where this fact comes from\" above the V1 band at AQI 42.\n  (c) f6-place-section-details on web-390: the V2 instrument row inside ScaleStrip.\n  Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f8-scale-strips and f8-compare-reveal → V2 inside ScaleStrip · f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet → V3 widget micro · f7-widget-tap-landing → V1 detail · f8-og-compare-card → the ScaleStrip OG Air row.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Summary: the value line (\"AQI 42 · Good · PM2.5\").\n- The band is one element, with these spoken labels:\n  - Alert: \"Air quality index 118, Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups, category 3 of 6. AirNow, observed 4 PM.\"\n  - Fixture: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM.\"\n  - Stale: \"Air quality index 42, Good, category 1 of 6. AirNow, observed 7 AM, 11 hours ago.\"\n- Separators and keylines keep the band readable in greyscale, and the printed name carries the meaning in tinted widgets.\n- The band itself is not a target. Retry and any row actions are 44pt/48dp/44px.\n- \"Air quality index (AQI)\" is spelled out once per surface.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n- EPA category names verbatim: \"Good\", \"Moderate\", \"Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups\", \"Unhealthy\", \"Very Unhealthy\", \"Hazardous\".\n- EPA health text verbatim.\n- The short form \"Sensitive groups\" is allowed only in widgets.\n- Never write \"satisfactory for everyone\", \"air score\" or \"pollution level\".\n\nPLATFORMS: the Android widget keeps the EPA hues fixed and never uses dynamic colour. The iOS widget supports tinted rendering, as drawn on 03. Otherwise the geometry is identical on all three platforms.\n\nINSTEAD OF (AqiBand):\n- Instead of a proportional 0–500 track, draw six equal-width segments ending in \"301+\", because proportional widths squeeze the everyday 0–100 range and cannot place readings above 500.\n- Instead of brand blue or an invented ramp, draw the six EPA ColorVision Assist hues, because this is the authority's own scale.\n- Instead of printing the category or number on a fill, print them in text.primary on the card, because text on yellow or maroon fails contrast.\n- Instead of a disc marker, draw the two-tone vertical capsule, because a disc reads as ● Official.\n- Instead of \"Air quality is satisfactory for everyone\", print EPA's exact sentence, because a paraphrased health statement is an EPA reporting error.\n- Instead of hiding the band on a good day, draw it at AQI 42 with \"Good\", because a quiet reading is still a reading.\n- Instead of a hard-coded 101 mark, draw the rule at the person's chosen threshold, because the band must show the rule that actually fired.\n\n======================================================================\n3 · FourteenDayStrip\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: The next two weeks at this address, drawn as a shape. The strip sits above list rows, and those rows are the real tap targets.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy with callouts):\n- Header line above the strip: the summary label \"Next 14 days: 6 items\", in label 13/18 text.strong. This is the strip's one-sentence summary.\n- Strip: 14 equal cells across the card's content width, with today on the left. At 326pt the pitch is 23.3pt; the contract range on phones is about 23–26pt.\n  - The cells form one track with radius sm 6, a 1px text.secondary keyline, and 1px text.secondary separators between cells.\n  - Cell height is 76pt: 6pt top padding · up to 3 XS (12pt) ProvenanceMarks stacked with 4pt gaps (44pt) · a 4pt gap · a 16pt line reserved for \"+N\" · 6pt bottom padding. \"+N\" is in caption 12/16 text.strong and appears when a cell has 4 or more mark items. It uses text.strong because the cell is sunken; in dark mode it is #F1F5F9. The reserved line stays empty when there is no overflow.\n  - All marks use one ink (text.secondary, full opacity; graphics need 3:1) and are centred horizontally.\n- Cell fill:\n  - weekday cells: surface.sunken at 100%\n  - weekend cells: surface.sunken at 40%. The weekend is shown by lower opacity, not by a hue, and it is also named by the initials (or by the \"Sat–Sun\" labels where there are no initials; see V2 and 05).\n- Civic, state or county rule: a solid bar 4pt wide spanning the full cell height, in text.strong ink.\n  - If the cell has no other marks, the bar is centred.\n  - Otherwise the bar sits 2pt from the cell's left edge and the marks shift 3pt right.\n  - A bar never counts toward the 3-mark limit.\n  - A statewide or county rule is never drawn as a dot. The same bar rule applies in YearBand.\n- Holiday move: the mark is drawn on the moved day. The usual day gets a struck ghost: the same mark shape in full text.secondary ink (at least 3:1), crossed by a 1.5px diagonal strike in text.primary (dark #E5E7EB). The strike carries the meaning, and the DateRow names the move in words.\n- Labels under the strip:\n  - Row 1: weekday initials under every cell, in caption text.secondary (\"M T W T F S S M T W T F S S\"). Initials appear only where the pitch is 20pt or more, and they are never spoken.\n  - Row 2: anchors in captionMedium text.strong. \"Today\" is left-aligned under cell 1, and the week-start date \"Mon 26 Oct\" is left-aligned under cell 8.\n- Below the strip: one 00c · DateRow per item. The foot is a persistent 48pt row, \"+ Add a date\" (plus glyph and label in primary.700; dark #38BDF8).\n- Fixture window for HOME A, \"Your household\", Mon 19 Oct–Sun 1 Nov:\n\n  | Cell | Day | Item | Mark |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | 2 | Tue 20 Oct | Recycling and garbage | hollow (city schedule, not confirmed) |\n  | 5 | Fri 23 Oct | Clark Public Utilities bill | tick |\n  | 8 | Mon 26 Oct | Voter registration, online or mail, must arrive by | state bar |\n  | 9 | Tue 27 Oct | Garbage only | hollow |\n  | 10 | Wed 28 Oct | City of Vancouver water bill | tick |\n  | 14 | Sun 1 Nov | HOA dues | tick, weekend cell |\n\n  That is 6 items, so the summary is \"Next 14 days: 6 items\".\n- Anatomy extras (label each one \"specimen\" in the gutter):\n  - Overflow cell for Mon 2 Nov (bar plus overflow): the county rule \"Property tax 2nd half\" is the full-height bar, 2pt from the left edge. The cell has four mark items (Comcast bill, tick · \"Swap furnace filter\", tick · \"Library books due\", tick · \"Drop off old paint\", tick). Draw 3 of the marks, shifted 3pt right, and then \"+1\" in text.strong on the reserved line. Callout: \"Bar = county rule, not counted in +N; 4 marks → 3 + '+1'; 6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6 = 76pt\".\n  - A holiday-move pair for PLACE B: the Thanksgiving notice for Thursday routes moves the usual Thu 26 Nov pickup to Fri 27 Nov. Draw the mark on Fri 27 Nov and the struck ghost on Thu 26 Nov, with the row \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\".\n\nVARIANTS:\n- V1 Today card (described above). Appears on 01, 02, 04, 05 and 07.\n- V2 widget medium (on 02 and 03). This variant is budgeted for the 338×158 widget, which has 306 × 126pt of content:\n  - Full 306pt content width, so the pitch is 21.9pt.\n  - Cell height 60pt: 6pt top · at most 2 XS marks with a 4pt gap (28pt) · 4pt · a 16pt \"+N\" line · 6pt bottom. With 3 or more mark items, the cell shows 1 mark and then \"+N\".\n  - Under the strip: one 16pt line with the anchor labels only (\"Today\" and \"Mon 26 Oct\", 11pt or larger, no initials), plus \"Sat–Sun\" at 11pt text.secondary, centred under cells 6–7 and cells 13–14.\n  - Then one 16pt legend line at 11pt text.secondary with S-size inline marks: \"● Official · ○ On record · ✓ You added\". This line prints the provenance words, because the widget is a standalone surface (C14).\n  - Height used: 60 + 4 + 16 + 4 + 16 = 100pt. The remaining 26pt belongs to f7-today-widget's header line; print this budget in the gutter.\n  - No rows and no add row are drawn in the widget.\n- V3 year-band shaded window (x-place-file; on 03 and 07): the same 14 days drawn as the shaded window inside YearBand (see YearBand).\n- V4 empty (on 02): the cells are drawn with no marks, followed by the 00d · QuietDayReceipt strip line \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" and the \"+ Add a date\" row. The summary label reads \"Next 14 days: nothing on file\".\n\nSTATES:\n- loading: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with 14 cell outlines on surface.sunken, no marks and no text, and a bar in place of the header. It reserves the full height (header + 76pt strip + label rows). It is static under Reduce Motion.\n- ready.\n- empty: V4.\n- stale: the marks keep full ink (C11), and the 00a · FreshnessLine \"Updated 2h ago\" appears under the header. The words carry the staleness.\n- permission-denied: the viewer may not add dates. The \"+ Add a date\" row is absent, and nothing ghosted replaces it. The strip and rows are unchanged.\n- T1: PLACE B, \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  - One hollow mark on Thu 22 Oct, the next Thursday only, because the frequency is Not set. Its row title is \"Pickup day · frequency not set\", with the source City of Camas.\n  - The state bar on Mon 26 Oct.\n  - Summary: \"Next 14 days: 2 items\".\n  - The \"+ Add a date\" row is present, and dates added here stay Only you.\n- error: no strip is drawn. The strip's slot shows only a 00c · InlineErrorRow, \"We couldn't load your dates just now\" + Retry. This is not an absence state and is not drawn per C5.\n- highlighted row on push arrival: after the push \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\", the Tue 20 Oct DateRow shows its highlighted state (light: infoBg wash + info outline; dark: see C6), and accessibility focus moves to that row. The highlight fades out over 300ms after 4s. Under Reduce Motion it appears and disappears without animation. The strip itself is unchanged.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light: V1 on iOS 393 with every callout, including a callout on the 76pt cell height budget. Add the overflow cell and the holiday-move pair magnified 4×, each labelled.\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: Today card · widget medium.\n  - Grid columns: loading · ready · empty (V4) · stale · permission-denied · T1 · error · highlighted row.\n  - Today card row: every column is drawn as described in STATES. Empty is V4, and error is the InlineErrorRow alone in the slot.\n  - Widget medium row:\n    - × loading: \"n/a — widgets never show skeletons\"\n    - × ready: V2 with the HOME A marks and the legend line\n    - × empty (V4): V2 cells with no marks, and \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" at 11pt in place of the legend line\n    - × stale: \"n/a — widget age is the widget's own 'As of' line (f7-today-widget)\"\n    - × permission-denied: \"n/a — the widget has no rows or add row\"\n    - × T1: V2 with the PLACE B marks (Thu 22 Oct hollow; state bar on Mon 26 Oct) and the legend line\n    - × error: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n    - × highlighted row: \"n/a — the widget has no rows\"\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light and · dark: V2 at true size inside a 338×158 outline. Leave the rest of the widget blank and label it \"owned by f7-today-widget\", with the 100pt budget in the gutter. Beside it, V3: the YearBand phone specimen with the Mon 19 Oct–Sun 1 Nov window shaded, and a leader line to the V1 strip showing that they are the same data. The bars match in both (the state bar on 26 Oct).\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light:\n  - iOS: the strip as one adjustable element, with a focus outline around the whole strip. Show four consecutive steps (each swipe up or down moves one day), each in a speech bubble:\n    - \"Tuesday 20 October: Recycling and garbage, city schedule, on record, not confirmed\"\n    - \"Wednesday 21 October: nothing on file\"\n    - \"Thursday 22 October: nothing on file\"\n    - \"Friday 23 October: Clark Public Utilities bill, you added this\"\n    - A tap on the strip scrolls to the rows.\n  - Android: the same element, with the TalkBack custom actions \"Next day\" and \"Previous day\".\n  - Web-390: the strip is hidden from assistive tech because the rows duplicate it. Annotate this, and add \"otherwise a list of full-date labels\".\n  - Web-1440 (648px card, 616px content): per-cell tap is allowed only on desktop web.\n    - Each cell is a 44px-wide button with its own focus ring (C12).\n    - Activating a cell moves focus to that day's first row.\n    - Hover reveals nothing that is not already on screen.\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light:\n  - V1 at iOS AX5. The cells keep their size.\n    - Initials are dropped: the pitch is still 23pt, but 43pt initials do not fit.\n    - The anchors become lines above the strip: \"Today · Mon 19 Oct\" and \"Mon 26 Oct\", on separate wrapped lines.\n    - A caption line below the strip keeps the weekend cue: \"Lighter cells are Sat and Sun\".\n    - The summary wraps, and the rows and add row grow.\n  - The same at Android 200%.\n  - At AX sizes the V2 widget falls back to text only: \"Next 14 days: 6 items · Tomorrow: Recycling and garbage\".\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light: 02 (light) desaturated. Caption: \"Provenance by shape; rules by bar; weekends by opacity plus initials or 'Sat–Sun'; moves by strike; widget words by legend line.\"\n- 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light:\n  (a) f5-today-calendar-strip on iOS 393: V1 with its rows and the legend line \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\".\n  (b) f1-today-tab on Android 412: the strip card inside Today, under the ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  (c) x-place-file on web-1440: V1 with per-cell buttons, beside the YearBand showing the shaded window.\n  Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f7-today-widget, f7-widget-gallery, f7-widget-howto-sheet → V2 widget medium · f7-widget-tap-landing → V1 with the highlighted row.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Summary: the header label (\"Next 14 days: 6 items\").\n- On native, the strip is one adjustable element whose day readout follows the pattern above. Cells are not individual targets, and a tap on the strip scrolls to the list.\n- On web, the strip is hidden when rows duplicate it; otherwise it is a list of full-date labels.\n- Initials are never spoken.\n- Non-colour encoding: provenance by mark shape, rules by bar, holiday moves by strike, and weekends by opacity plus initials (or \"Sat–Sun\").\n- The add row is 48pt. Rows follow DateRow.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n- Summary label pattern: \"Next 14 days: N items\" (the fixture reads \"Next 14 days: 6 items\").\n- Dates always include the weekday.\n- Pickup rows name the bins (\"Recycling and garbage\", \"Garbage only\").\n- Deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n- The add row reads exactly \"+ Add a date\".\n\nPLATFORMS: per-cell tap exists only on desktop web. iOS uses an adjustable element, and Android uses custom actions. Web-390 has no per-cell targets.\n\nINSTEAD OF (FourteenDayStrip):\n- Instead of colouring marks by class (pickup, civic, money, yours) as the only cue, draw one ink and let the DateRow KindGlyph carry the class, because hue alone fails for colour-blind viewers and tinted views.\n- Instead of 6pt dots with ticks, draw 12pt XS ProvenanceMarks, because below 12pt the three shapes cannot be told apart.\n- Instead of 14 tiny tap targets, make the strip one element and the rows the targets, because 23pt cells fail the 44pt/48dp rule.\n- Instead of a dot for a statewide or county deadline, draw a full-height bar, because a rule for the whole state or county is not an item at this address.\n- Instead of an even weekly rhythm through a holiday week, draw the moved day and a struck ghost, because holiday moves are the core pickup job.\n- Instead of dimming stale or ghost marks, keep full ink and state the age or the move in words, because a dimmed mark falls below 3:1 and its shape can no longer be read.\n- Instead of text.secondary for \"+N\" on a sunken cell, use text.strong, because text.secondary on sunken is 4.39:1.\n\n======================================================================\n4 · YearBand\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: Twelve months of dated rules in four source lanes: the same data as FourteenDayStrip at a longer zoom.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone with callouts):\n- Summary header, in label 13/18 text.strong: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates. Next, in 4 days: Clark Public Utilities bill due Fri 23 Oct.\" The pickup rhythm is not counted as dates (see Notes).\n- 12 month columns, starting with the current month, with three-letter labels in caption text.secondary: \"Oct Nov Dec Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep\". The caption \"2027\" sits above \"Jan\".\n- Phone geometry: 326pt wide, so each column is 27.2pt.\n- Four labelled lanes, in this order and with these exact labels: \"You\" · \"Your city\" · \"Your county\" · \"Your state\".\n  - On phones, each lane label sits above its lane in captionMedium text.strong (16pt line). At 768px and above, the labels sit in a 128px left column.\n  - Each lane track is 24pt tall with a surface.base fill, a 1px text.secondary keyline, radius xs 4, and 1px text.secondary month separators. Lanes are 4pt apart.\n- On phones, markers are grouped per month per lane:\n  - one XS 12pt ProvenanceMark, centred in the month column\n  - a count numeral in captionMedium text.primary, 1pt to the right of the mark, when there are 2 or more items\n  - if a cluster mixes provenance, draw the hollow mark (the least certain) and let the rows list each item.\n  - Exact-day placement happens only at 768px and above.\n- Rules (county and state) are solid bars, 4pt wide and the full lane height, in text.strong, in the \"Your county\" and \"Your state\" lanes. This is the same bar rule as FourteenDayStrip. On phones the bar is centred in its month column, with a count numeral when there are 2 or more.\n- Collision rule at 768px and above: build clusters from left to right within each lane. A mark or bar whose centre is less than 14px from the first item of the current cluster joins that cluster. A cluster is drawn as one item at its earliest day, with a count numeral 1pt to its right. A mixed-provenance cluster shows the hollow mark, as on phones.\n- Today rule: a 1.5px text.primary vertical line through all four lanes at 19 Oct (19/31 of the Oct column), with \"Today\" in caption text.primary above the month labels.\n- Shaded 14-day window: a surface.sunken wash behind the marks from 19 Oct to 1 Nov across all lanes, with a 1px dashed text.secondary edge at 1 Nov. The legend line below the band reads \"Shaded: next 14 days\".\n- Pickup rhythm (in the \"Your city\" lane):\n  - The lane's provenance goes on its label line: after \"Your city\", an XS hollow ProvenanceMark and the lane caption \"Pickup every Tuesday · city schedule\" in caption text.secondary. At 768px and above, the mark and caption sit in the label column under \"Your city\".\n  - The rhythm itself is drawn as 1.5px × 8pt ticks in text.secondary (4.83:1), one per service week, centred vertically.\n  - After the last published city calendar (Dec 2026), the lane keyline for Jan–Sep turns dashed (3/2), with a second lane caption \"Projected after Dec 2026 (last published city calendar)\".\n  - Holiday moves on phones: that week's tick is drawn 11pt tall with a 1.5px strike. At 768px and above, when the moved day is at least 14px from the usual day, the tick moves to the real day and a struck ghost (full ink, as in FourteenDayStrip) sits on the usual day. When the two days are closer than 14px, use the phone form.\n- The band reserves its full height while loading.\n- Caption under the band, in text.secondary: \"The same dates are listed below.\" Then 00c · FactRow/DateRow rows follow; those rows are the table.\n- Fixture data for HOME A:\n  - You: an Oct cluster \"2\" (Clark Public Utilities bill Fri 23 Oct; City of Vancouver water bill Wed 28 Oct), ticks · a Nov cluster \"2\" (HOA dues Sun 1 Nov; Comcast bill Mon 2 Nov), ticks · a Dec tick (water-heater warranty ends Sat 12 Dec) · a Mar cluster \"2\" (lease notice deadline Mon 1 Mar; lease ends Wed 31 Mar), ticks.\n  - Your city: the weekly Tuesday pickup rhythm, on record but not confirmed (the hollow mark and caption on the label line), with no holiday move in the published window.\n  - Your county: a bar in Nov (property tax 2nd half due Mon 2 Nov). The detail row may add \"moved from Sat 31 Oct\".\n  - Your state: bars in Oct (voter registration, online or mail, must arrive by Mon 26 Oct) and Nov (in person until 8:00 PM Tue 3 Nov).\n  - That makes 10 dates in total: 7 in You, 1 in Your county and 2 in Your state.\n\nVARIANTS:\n- V1 place file (HOME A, described above). A second place-file row uses PLACE B, \"Saved place · Only you\":\n  - The \"You\" lane is empty.\n  - \"Your city\" has no weekly rhythm, because the frequency is Not set. It shows one tick on the next Thursday (Thu 22 Oct) and the Thanksgiving move in Nov (\"moved to Fri 27 Nov\", from the published 2026 calendar, not projected), with the XS hollow mark and the lane caption \"Pickup day Thursday · frequency not set\".\n  - \"Your county\": a bar in Nov.\n  - \"Your state\": bars in Oct and Nov.\n  - Summary: \"Next 12 months: 3 dates. Next, in 7 days: voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct.\"\n- V2 widget large, 338×354pt, with 306pt of content width:\n  - Columns are 25.5pt wide. Lane labels use place names: \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\" (for PLACE B: \"You · Camas · Clark County · Washington\").\n  - The city lane's hollow mark is followed by the printed word \"On record\".\n  - Under the band, one legend line at 11pt text.secondary with S-size inline marks: \"● Official · ○ On record · ✓ You added · ▮ Rule\". It prints the words for the filled, ticked and bar items, because the widget is a standalone surface (C14).\n  - Count numerals sit below the mark. All text is at least 11pt.\n  - The widget label is \"Larkspur Loop\".\n  - At AX sizes it drops to text.\n- V3 gallery sample: V2 with the same HOME A data, drawn static inside a gallery preview frame.\n- V4 empty checked: the lanes, month labels and today rule are drawn, with no marks, bars or rhythm, followed by the 00d · QuietDayReceipt line \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\".\n\nSTATES:\n- loading: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with four lane outlines on surface.sunken, reserving the exact final height. It is static under Reduce Motion.\n- ready.\n- empty checked: V4.\n- error: the band is not drawn. The band's slot shows only a 00c · InlineErrorRow, \"We couldn't load the next 12 months just now\" + Retry. This is not an absence state and is not drawn per C5.\n- offline: the band is drawn from cache under the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\".\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light: V1 HOME A on iOS 393 with every callout, including one callout on the county bar (\"county rule = bar, same as FourteenDayStrip\").\n- 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: place file (HOME A) · place file (PLACE B) · widget large · gallery sample · empty checked.\n  - Grid columns: loading · ready · empty checked · error · offline.\n  - Place file (HOME A) and place file (PLACE B): every column is drawn as in STATES. Empty checked is V4 with that place's header.\n  - Widget large:\n    - × loading: \"n/a — widgets never show skeletons\"\n    - × ready: V2\n    - × empty checked: V2 with no marks and \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" in place of the legend line\n    - × error: \"n/a — the widget keeps its last snapshot (f7-today-widget)\"\n    - × offline: V2 under the FreshnessLine form \"As of Mon 7:40 AM · Open to refresh\"\n  - Gallery sample:\n    - × ready: V3\n    - × loading, × empty checked, × error and × offline: \"n/a — the gallery shows a static sample\"\n  - Empty checked:\n    - × empty checked: V4\n    - × loading: the HOME A skeleton\n    - × ready: \"n/a — V4 is the empty state\"\n    - × error: \"n/a — an error is not a checked result; see the place file rows\"\n    - × offline: V4 under the FreshnessLine\n- 00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light:\n  - V1 on web-1440, in an 880px-wide card (848px content), with the 128px label column and 60px month columns (128 + 12 × 60 = 848px).\n  - Every mark and bar sits on its exact day, subject to the collision rule. The state bars sit at 26 Oct and 3 Nov, and the county bar at 2 Nov.\n  - In the You lane, 23 Oct and 28 Oct are about 10px apart, so they draw as one mark at 23 Oct with \"2\". 1 Nov and 2 Nov are about 2px apart, so they draw as one mark at 1 Nov with \"2\". 1 Mar and 31 Mar stay separate. Draw a callout on the 1 Nov + 2 Nov pair: \"less than 14px apart → one mark + count numeral\".\n  - The Tuesday ticks sit on exact Tuesdays, about 13.5px apart.\n  - Add a PLACE B inset band below. Its Thanksgiving move (Thu 26 Nov → Fri 27 Nov) is about 2px apart, so it uses the phone form: an 11pt struck tick. Callout: \"moved day under 14px from usual day → phone form\".\n  - Marks are not targets; the rows below are.\n- 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light and · dark:\n  - V2 at true size, including its legend line, with the rest of the widget labelled \"owned by f7-today-widget\".\n  - V3 inside an iOS gallery preview and an Android widget-picker preview.\n  - V2 under iOS tinted rendering.\n- 00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light:\n  - V1 at iOS AX5. The lanes keep their geometry, and the month labels drop to every third month (\"Oct\", \"Jan\", \"Apr\", \"Jul\") on a line above the band.\n  - The lane labels and lane captions wrap above the lanes, and the summary wraps.\n  - The same at Android 200%.\n  - At AX sizes V2 drops to text: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates\", then \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · Clark Public Utilities bill\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Voter registration must arrive by\" · \"in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct · City of Vancouver water bill\". No amounts appear in the widget.\n- 00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light: 02 (light) desaturated. Caption: \"Lanes by label; county and state rules by bar; city lane provenance by hollow mark and caption; projected by dashed keyline and caption; window by wash plus dashed edge; widget words by legend line.\"\n- 00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light:\n  (a) x-place-file on iOS 393: the band under the place file header, with its rows.\n  (b) x-place-file on Android 412: the PLACE B place file with the ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\".\n  (c) f7-widget-gallery on iOS: the V3 sample in the gallery.\n  Under the crops, one line in caption text.strong: \"Also used in: f7-today-widget → V2 widget large.\"\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Summary: \"Next 12 months: 10 dates. Next, in 4 days: Clark Public Utilities bill due Fri 23 Oct.\" The rows below are the table, and the band says so.\n- On native, the band is one element whose month cells are adjustable (each swipe up or down moves one month). October reads: \"October: 3 dates. Clark Public Utilities bill due Friday 23 October, you added this. Voter registration must arrive by Monday 26 October, Washington, official. City of Vancouver water bill due Wednesday 28 October, you added this. Pickup every Tuesday, city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\" November includes \"Property tax 2nd half due Monday 2 November, Clark County, official.\"\n- On web, the band is one image with the summary as its text alternative.\n- Marks are never targets.\n\nCOPY RULES: lane labels are exactly \"You · Your city · Your county · Your state\". On widgets they are place names: \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\" for HOME A.\n\nPLATFORMS: none beyond geometry. Phones group markers by month, and screens 768px and wider place them on the exact day under the collision rule. Native uses adjustable month cells.\n\nINSTEAD OF (YearBand):\n- Instead of a heatmap of busy months, draw marks with count numerals in labelled lanes, because colour intensity hides what the dates are and who set them.\n- Instead of collapsing the four lanes into one row, keep You · Your city · Your county · Your state, because the source of a rule matters as much as its date.\n- Instead of day-accurate dots on a phone, draw one cluster per month with a count, because 27pt columns cannot place days legibly.\n- Instead of overlapping marks on desktop, merge marks less than 14px apart into one mark with a count, because overlapping 12pt shapes cannot be read.\n- Instead of a filled dot for a county rule, draw a full-height bar, because the strip and the band show the same data and must encode it the same way.\n- Instead of an unlabelled 1px rhythm, draw 1.5px ticks with a hollow mark and the \"city schedule\" caption, because an unconfirmed schedule must look unconfirmed.\n\n======================================================================\n5 · SlotMeter\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: An honest, dated Founding Neighbor window. When anything is uncertain, it fails closed.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy with callouts):\n- Heading \"Founding Neighbor\" in bodyMedium text.primary.\n- Five bounded capsule segments, each 40×12pt, radius pill, with 4pt gaps (216pt in total). Taken segments come first, from the left.\n  - Taken: a solid primary.600 fill with a 1.5px primary.700 edge (#38BDF8 in dark mode, per C6).\n  - Open: a surface.base fill with 45° diagonal hatch lines (1.5px, every 4pt) in text.secondary ink, and a 1.5px text.secondary edge.\n- Numeral label 8pt to the right of the segments, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"3 of 5 open\". The fixture has 2 taken and 3 open. This count of open slots is the one sanctioned \"N of M\" here: it counts what is left and never measures progress.\n- Elapsed bar, 8pt below the segments: 4pt tall × 216pt, radius pill. The elapsed part is a solid text.secondary fill, and the remaining part is an unfilled 1px text.secondary outline (no border tokens). The bar is decorative and hidden from assistive tech, because the date pill carries the meaning. The fixture window opened Mon 5 Oct and closes Tue 27 Oct, so about 64% of it has elapsed.\n- Date caption, 8pt below the bar: a neutral pill, 24pt tall, with a surface.sunken fill, a 12pt calendar glyph and label 13/18 text, both in text.strong: \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\".\n- RankBadge (part of this specimen). It always sits below the meter, at least 24pt away, and never in the same row or sentence as the tier.\n  - A separate squared shape, 120×64pt, radius md 8, with a surface.sunken fill, a 1px text.secondary edge, 12pt horizontal padding (96pt of text width) and 8pt vertical padding.\n  - The overline \"BLOCK FOUNDER\" in 11/16/600 caps +0.5 text.strong.\n  - The numeral \"#3\" in h2 24/32/600 text.primary.\n  - If the overline measures wider than 96pt, it breaks as \"BLOCK / FOUNDER\" and the badge grows to 80pt tall.\n\nVARIANTS:\n- V1 preview card (f9-founding-meter-preview, PLACE B): a card holding the heading, the meter, the date pill and the caption \"A badge — no money or fee change. You can still claim this address.\"\n- V2 Block Founders panel (f9-block-founders-panel, HOME A): the meter and date pill in the panel's tier section, with the RankBadge \"#3\" in a separate rank section below.\n- V3 wall line replacement: body text.primary only, with no meter: \"3 Founding Neighbor slots are still open on this block.\"\n\nSTATES:\n- open.\n- closed: absent. Draw it per C5. Zero open slots counts as closed, so an empty meter is never drawn.\n- lookup failed: the entire card is absent. Draw it per C5, including for V3, where the line is absent.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light: V1 at true size with every callout, the RankBadge below it (24pt away), and a pair of segments (taken and open) magnified 4×.\n- 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: preview card · Block Founders panel · wall line.\n  - Grid columns: open · closed (absent) · lookup failed (absent).\n  - Under the grid, one extra absence specimen, with the gutter label \"0 of 5 open → treated as closed\".\n  - In dark mode, the taken fill stays primary.600 (3.57:1 on dark raised #1E293B) with a #38BDF8 edge. The hatch, the open edges and the elapsed bar use dark text.secondary.\n- 00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light: one frame showing three encodings side by side, each labelled:\n  - the SlotMeter (solid vs hatched + \"3 of 5 open\")\n  - the cells-map bucket labels from PublicPointMap (\"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\", \"16+\")\n  - the 00a · ProvenanceMark legend \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\".\n  Caption: \"Solid vs hatched means taken vs open. Filled vs hollow means provenance only.\"\n- 00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n  - V1 at iOS AX5: the segments keep their size, the numeral label moves below the segments, the date pill grows and wraps, and the RankBadge grows vertically, with \"BLOCK / FOUNDER\" on two lines.\n  - The same at Android 200%.\n  - V1 and V2 desaturated, captioned \"Taken vs open by texture plus numeral.\"\n- 00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light:\n  (a) f9-founding-meter-preview on web-390: V1 on the PLACE B preview.\n  (b) f9-block-founders-panel on iOS 393: V2.\n  (c) f9-nearby-cells-map on Android 412: V3 as the wall line. Beside it, show f9-verification-promise-copy and f9-invite-rewards-card, each as one line that names the tier (\"Founding Neighbor · 3 of 5 open · Closes Tue 27 Oct\") and never the rank in the same sentence.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Summary and spoken label: the meter is one element that reads \"Founding Neighbor slots: 3 of 5 open, closes Tuesday 27 October.\"\n- Taken vs open is carried by solid vs hatched, plus the numeral.\n- The meter is not a target. Any card action is 44pt/48dp/44px.\n- The RankBadge reads \"Block Founder number 3\".\n\nCOPY RULES:\n- Never write \"permanent\" unless the data model guarantees it.\n- Rank (\"Block Founder #3\") and tier (\"Founding Neighbor\") never share a sentence.\n- Closing dates are written as dates, never as \"closes in 6 days\" or hh:mm.\n\nPLATFORMS: identical on iOS, Android and web; only the target minimums differ.\n\nINSTEAD OF (SlotMeter):\n- Instead of hollow segments for open slots, draw hatched segments with an ink edge, because hollow means \"on record, not confirmed\".\n- Instead of a warning-tinted pill, draw a neutral surface.sunken pill, because a deadline for a badge is not an alarm.\n- Instead of an hh:mm or \"closes in 6 days\" countdown, print \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", because live countdowns manufacture urgency.\n- Instead of a border-token fill for the remaining time, draw a text.secondary outline, because border tokens are never the only edge of a segment.\n- Instead of an empty meter at 0 open, or a meter shown after a failed lookup, render nothing, because the meter must never promise a slot the system cannot honour.\n\n======================================================================\n6 · PublicPointMap\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: Shows exactly where neighbours see a post, drawn at true scale from the server's stable public point.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy with callouts. The address is HOME A, and the viewer is Maya Chen):\n- Map thumb, 16:9: 326×183pt inside the card, radius md 8, with a 1px text.secondary edge.\n  - The base map uses neutral tokens: land is surface.sunken, and streets are 4pt surface.base lines with 1px text.secondary casing.\n  - Street labels are in caption 12/16 text.strong with a 2px surface.base halo: \"NE 18th St\", \"NE 138th Ave\", \"NE 23rd St\".\n  - No ramp and no brand tint.\n- The frame is centred on the public pin, never on the home.\n- A single public pin: a 24pt teardrop in text.primary with a 2px surface.base halo and a 6pt surface.base centre.\n- Above the pin, a label chip: a pill in surface.base with a 1px text.secondary edge and shadow md, in label 13/18 text.primary, reading \"What neighbors see\".\n- No home marker anywhere.\n- Scale bar at the bottom left, on an 80% surface.base plate: a 1.5px text.primary line with end ticks, in tenths of a mile (\"0\", \"0.1\", \"0.2 mi\"). At this zoom the thumb spans about 0.8 mi, so 0.2 mi = 81pt.\n- Caption under the map, in bodySmall text.primary: \"Neighbors see your posts at this spot, the same spot every time, about 0.3 mi from your address.\" This caption is the map's one-sentence summary.\n- A row under the caption, owned by f9-privacy-mirror (draw it only in context): \"Hidden from neighbors: your street address, your home on the map\".\n- Controls, 8pt below the map (8pt below the caption when a caption is present, as in V1). Every button is 44×44pt on iOS and web and 48×48dp on Android, with radius md, a surface.base fill, a 1px text.secondary edge and a 20pt text.primary glyph. The accessible names are the words shown here. The same two-row layout is used at every size:\n  - Left, a zoom column with \"Zoom in\" (+) above \"Zoom out\" (−), 8pt apart.\n  - Right-aligned, a 3×2 arrow pad with 8pt gaps: the top row holds \"Move map up\" (↑) in the middle slot, and the bottom row holds \"Move map left\" (←), \"Move map down\" (↓) and \"Move map right\" (→).\n  - Cluster width: 208pt on iOS and web (44 + 16 + 3×44 + 2×8), 224dp on Android. Height: 96pt on iOS and web, 104dp on Android. Both fit the 326pt content width.\n  - Focus order: Zoom in, Zoom out, Move map up, Move map left, Move map down, Move map right, then List cells when present.\n- Cells-map extension:\n  - Cells are rectangles with a 1px text.secondary outline and a 70% surface.base fill.\n  - Each cell prints its bucket label centred, in label 13/18 text.primary: \"0\", \"1–5\", \"6–15\" or \"16+\".\n  - The user's cell gets a 2px primary.600 inner ring (#38BDF8 in dark mode) and the caption \"Your cell\" inside it.\n  - A \"List cells\" text button (primary.700; dark #38BDF8) sits on its own third row, 8pt below the controls, left-aligned, 44pt tall (48dp on Android). The V3 controls block is therefore 148pt tall on iOS and web and 160dp on Android. The loading skeleton reserves these heights.\n\nPENDING DECISION — range box R (not a published variant):\n- The ±0.005° box is centred on the home by definition, so drawing it may reveal the home. Until the founder answers open question (1), draw R only on 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light, inside a dashed 1px text.secondary annotation frame labelled \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\". Do not draw it on any other artboard, and do not publish it.\n- How to draw it: the real ±0.005° box, about 1.11 km tall × 0.78 km wide (about 0.69 × 0.49 mi, or about 141 × 99pt at this zoom), as a 1.5px dashed text.secondary rectangle with no fill. Use a zoom where the 326pt thumb spans about 1.6 mi, so the whole box fits inside the 183pt-tall thumb with a margin. The scale bar reads \"0\", \"0.25\", \"0.5 mi\" (0.25 mi = 51pt). The box sits off-centre in the frame.\n\nVARIANTS:\n- V1 privacy mirror (described above).\n- V2 composer one-liner: a row at least 44pt tall with a 16pt pin glyph in text.secondary, the bodySmall text.primary line \"Neighbors see this post at the same spot as your other posts, about 0.3 mi from your address.\", and a trailing text button \"See the spot\" (primary.700, 44pt; dark #38BDF8) that opens V1. No map is drawn.\n- V3 cells map:\n  - A 326×326pt map with 9 cell rectangles in a 3×3 grid, with the user's cell in the centre. Names and buckets:\n    - top row: North-west 0 · North 1–5 · North-east 1–5\n    - middle row: West 6–15 · Your cell 6–15 · East 16+\n    - bottom row: South-west 0 · South 0 · South-east 1–5\n  - The summary line \"14 neighbor posts in your cell in 30 days. 3 Pantopus posts not counted.\"\n  - The 00a · FreshnessLine \"Updated 12m ago\".\n\nSTATES:\n- ready.\n- loading: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton panel. A surface.sunken 16:9 block (square for V3), with the controls drawn as outlines at their reserved height. It is static under Reduce Motion. V2 shows its text immediately.\n- vector fallback: when tiles fail, draw land in surface.base and streets as 1px text.secondary lines, and keep the labels, pin, scale bar and caption. Add the caption \"Simplified map\" above the thumb.\n- offline:\n  - With a cache: the cached map under the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\". The pan and zoom buttons are disabled, with the reason caption \"Moving the map needs a connection.\"\n  - With no cache: the reserved 16:9 slot (square for V3) is a surface.sunken block holding the centred line \"You're offline. The map needs a connection.\" in body text.strong. The caption stays, and the buttons are disabled.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light: V1 on iOS 393 with every callout, including the controls cluster geometry. Beside it, the pending-decision frame holding R.\n- 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: privacy mirror · composer one-liner · cells map.\n  - Grid columns: ready · loading · vector fallback · offline.\n  - Privacy mirror × offline and cells map × offline: draw both the cached form and the no-cache form, stacked in the cell.\n  - Composer one-liner:\n    - × loading: the line as in ready, because it shows its text immediately.\n    - × vector fallback: \"n/a — no map drawn\".\n    - × offline: the line unchanged, because the composer owns the offline notice.\n  - Dark base map: land is dark surface.raised, streets are dark surface.base with dark text.secondary casing, the pin core is #E5E7EB with a #0F172A halo, and the user's cell ring is #38BDF8.\n- 00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light: V3 on Android 412 with its controls. Beside it, the \"List cells\" view: nine 48dp rows, each with a cell name, bucket and lock state.\n  - \"Your cell · 6–15 · Detail open\"\n  - \"North-west of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"North of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"North-east of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"West of your cell · 6–15 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"East of your cell · 16+ · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"South-west of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"South of your cell · 0 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  - \"South-east of your cell · 1–5 · Detail after 3 friends join\"\n  The locked tier only states its requirement. Nothing is blurred or fogged.\n- 00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n  - V1 at iOS AX5. The map keeps its width, and the caption, chip and street labels grow. If the chip would be wider than the map, it moves under the map as a text line: \"What neighbors see: the pin on this map\".\n  - The glyph buttons keep their size and the two-row cluster. On V3, \"List cells\" wraps and grows.\n  - V1 at Android 200%.\n  - V1 and V3 desaturated, captioned \"Pin by shape and label; buckets by printed numbers; your cell by ring width and words.\"\n- 00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light:\n  (a) f9-privacy-mirror on iOS 393: V1 with the hidden-from-neighbors row and the neighbour feed-card header.\n  (b) f9-nearby-cells-map on Android 412: V3 with the summary line.\n  (c) the f9-privacy-mirror composer entry on web-390: V2 above a post field.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- The map content has a text equivalent.\n  - V1 reads: \"Map. One pin marks where neighbors see your posts, about 0.3 miles from your address. Your home is not shown. Scale bar 0.2 miles.\"\n  - V3 reads: \"Cells map. Your cell: 6 to 15 posts in 30 days.\" It is followed by the List cells view.\n- Pan and zoom work through buttons, never only by drag or pinch. On web, the focused map also accepts +, − and the arrow keys.\n- Buttons are 44pt/48dp/44px with 8pt/8dp gaps.\n- Controls never auto-hide while assistive tech is on.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n- Use the caption exactly as given.\n- Never write \"re-rolled every time you post\".\n- The pin label is exactly \"What neighbors see\".\n- Cells-map counts say \"Pantopus posts\", never \"curator\".\n\nPLATFORMS: identical geometry on all three. Only the button minimums differ (44pt iOS · 48dp Android · 44px web), and web adds the keyboard keys.\n\nINSTEAD OF (PublicPointMap):\n- Instead of a 150 m ring around the home, draw the single public pin where neighbours see it, because the real offset area is about 12 times larger, and a ring centred on the home reveals the home.\n- Instead of publishing the ±0.005° box now, keep it in a pending-decision frame, because a box centred on the home can reveal the home.\n- Instead of a blurred, fogged or locked map, draw the full map and state the requirement in words, because a hidden map is a carrot, not information.\n- Instead of a lightness-only ramp for post density, print the bucket label in every cell, because adjacent ramp steps are only 1.16 to 1.66:1 apart.\n- Instead of a home marker \"for orientation\", show street labels only, because a screenshot must never locate the home.\n- Instead of one long controls row, draw the zoom column and the arrow pad, because six 48dp buttons do not fit in 326pt.\n\n======================================================================\n7 · FactCount\n======================================================================\nPURPOSE: States how much is on file for the address without implying that anything is missing.\n\nANATOMY (draw it on 00b · FactCount · 01-anatomy with callouts):\n- A vertical block, at most 160pt wide.\n- Line 1: the integer in h3 20/28/600 (label weight) text.primary, then a 4pt gap, then \"on file\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary, baseline-aligned.\n- Line 2, 6pt below: category pips. The contract places them beside the integer; here they sit below it so the block fits in 160pt (see Notes). There is one labelled pip for each category that has anything known, in this fixed order: Place · Dates · Money · People · Proof.\n  - Pip: 20pt tall, radius pill, surface.sunken fill, captionMedium 12/16/500 text.strong, 8pt horizontal padding, 4pt gaps.\n  - Pips wrap to a second line.\n  - A pip is always a word, never a bare dot.\n- Unknown categories draw nothing: no outline, no placeholder, no \"0\". The host screen (x-place-file) owns any \"You can also add\" list; this component never draws one.\n- The whole block is one target of at least 44pt (48dp on Android), extended beyond the visible block if needed. Tapping it opens the place file; inside x-place-file it scrolls to the list.\n- The place file header and the keeper strip use the same geometry.\n- Fixture: HOME A shows \"14 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates · Money · People. The same home at the same moment shows the same number on every surface.\n\nVARIANTS:\n- V1 place file header: \"14 on file\" with Place · Dates · Money · People.\n- V2 keeper strip: \"14 on file\" with Place · Dates · Money · People, right-aligned within 160pt.\n- V3 T1 (PLACE B, \"Saved place · Only you\"): \"7 on file\" with Place · Dates only. Only Place and Dates can appear at T1.\n- The contract specimen number \"11 on file\" appears only in the f1-claim-receipt crop, as the count at claim time. The facts carried into a claim come from T1, so that receipt shows the pips Place · Dates only.\n\nSTATES:\n- default.\n- loading: a 00d · WarmingSkeleton with a surface.sunken 24×20pt bar for the integer and two 48×20pt pill shapes. No ring outline and no count-up. It is static under Reduce Motion.\n- offline: the count stays, with the 00a · FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 7:04 AM\" under the block.\n\nARTBOARD CONTENTS\n- 00b · FactCount · 01-anatomy · light: V1 with every callout, plus one pip magnified 4×.\n- 00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · light and · dark:\n  - Grid rows: place file header · keeper strip · T1.\n  - Grid columns: default · loading · offline.\n- 00b · FactCount · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light:\n  - V1 and V2 at iOS AX5: the integer and \"on file\" stack, the pips wrap one per line if needed, the maximum width is lifted to the full row, and in the keeper strip the block moves below the name and mood line.\n  - The same at Android 200%.\n  - All three variants desaturated, captioned \"Categories by printed words, not colour.\"\n- 00b · FactCount · 04-in-context · light:\n  (a) x-place-file on iOS 393: the header \"Your place file\" with V1 \"14 on file\" and the ScopeChip \"Your household\".\n  (b) f11-keeper-strip on Android 412: Ollie (otter) with the mood word \"On it\", the mood line \"Recycling and garbage go out tomorrow by 6:30 AM\", and V2 \"14 on file\".\n  (c) f1-claim-receipt on web-390: \"11 on file\" with the pips Place · Dates in the claim receipt, at claim time.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n- Summary and spoken label: the block is one element, and its spoken label starts with the visible text (label in name).\n  - V1 and V2 read \"14 on file: place, dates, money, people.\"\n  - T1 reads \"7 on file: place, dates.\"\n  - The claim-receipt crop reads \"11 on file: place, dates.\"\n- Categories are carried by words. The target is 44pt/48dp/44px.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n- Never \"X of Y\", never \"knows\" (no \"Ollie knows\"), never a percentage.\n- Use \"on file\" as written.\n\nPLATFORMS: identical on all three.\n\nINSTEAD OF (FactCount):\n- Instead of a closed five-segment ring with outlined empty segments, draw the integer and word pips for known categories only, because an empty slot reads as a task left undone.\n- Instead of a progress bar, level or XP, draw the plain count \"14 on file\", because the count states what is held, not how far someone has come.\n- Instead of a count-up animation, show the final number at once, because motion here implies an achievement.\n- Instead of \"3 of 6 things on file\", write \"14 on file\", because fractions imply incompleteness.\n- Instead of different counts for the same home on different surfaces, show \"14 on file\" everywhere at the same moment, because drift between surfaces reads as an error.\n- Instead of the spoken \"14 things on file\", say \"14 on file\", because the spoken name must contain the visible text.\n\n======================================================================\nARTBOARDS (exact names per C0; the BATCH PLAN sets the priority order)\n======================================================================\n00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light — Wildfire row with callouts; the 4-row instrument with its summary on iOS and on web-1440\n00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · dark — dark twin\n00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light — the four layers × loading, ready, no data, not studied/non-burnable, stale and frozen, plus Wildfire very low for contrast\n00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light — Dana vs You compare with its spoken label, the collapsed line, and the two-column layout\n00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · dark — dark twin\n00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light — the full instrument in five states, with the row spoken labels\n00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · dark — dark twin\n00b · ScaleStrip · 05-og-column · light — the OG column recipe and its height budget\n00b · ScaleStrip · 06-ax5-200 · light — iOS AX5, Android 200%, web at 200% zoom, and an Increase Contrast row\n00b · ScaleStrip · 07-greyscale · light — 02 and 03 desaturated\n00b · ScaleStrip · 08-in-context · light — three host crops plus the also-used-in line\n00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light — detail card with callouts and the swatch row\n00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · dark — dark twin\n00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light — the variant × state grid, plus threshold 151, the clamp, and the capsule on every hue\n00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · light — the widget block in iOS colour, iOS tinted, and Android\n00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · dark — dark twin\n00b · AqiBand · 04-ax5-200 · light — AX5 legend list, Android 200%, and the widget text fallback\n00b · AqiBand · 05-greyscale · light — 01 and 02 desaturated\n00b · AqiBand · 06-in-context · light — three host crops plus the also-used-in line\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light — the HOME A strip with callouts, the overflow cell, and the holiday-move pair\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light — Today card and widget medium × eight states\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light — the widget block with its legend, and the year-band window\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · dark — dark twin\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light — iOS, Android, web-390, and web-1440 per-cell buttons\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light — iOS AX5, Android 200%, and the widget text fallback\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light — 02 desaturated\n00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light — three host crops plus the also-used-in line\n00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light — the HOME A band with callouts\n00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light — five variant rows × five states\n00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light — exact-day placement with the collision rule, plus the PLACE B inset\n00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light — widget large with its legend, gallery previews, and tinted rendering\n00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · dark — dark twin\n00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light — iOS AX5, Android 200%, and the widget text fallback\n00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light — 02 desaturated\n00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light — three host crops plus the also-used-in line\n00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light — the preview card with callouts, the RankBadge below it, and the magnified segments\n00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light — three variants × three states, plus the 0-open absence specimen\n00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light — three encodings compared\n00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, and desaturated\n00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light — three host crops plus the two tier lines\n00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light — the privacy mirror with callouts, and R in the do-not-publish frame\n00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light — three variants × four states\n00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light — the 9-cell map and the 9-row list\n00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, and desaturated\n00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light — three host crops\n00b · FactCount · 01-anatomy · light — the header block with callouts\n00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · light — three variants × three states\n00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · dark — dark twin\n00b · FactCount · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — AX5, 200%, and desaturated\n00b · FactCount · 04-in-context · light — three host crops\n00b · Notes — assumptions, invented strings, deviations, open questions, and omitted states\n\nThe manifest has 57 artboards, including Notes.\n\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn; after each batch, stop and wait for \"continue\")\nBatch 1:\n  1. 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · light\n  2. 00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · light\n  3. 00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · light\n  4. 00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · light\n  5. 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · light\n  6. 00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · light\nBatch 2:\n  1. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 01-anatomy · light\n  2. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · light\n  3. 00b · YearBand · 01-anatomy-phone · light\n  4. 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · light\n  5. 00b · SlotMeter · 01-anatomy · light\n  6. 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · light\nBatch 3:\n  1. 00b · PublicPointMap · 01-anatomy · light\n  2. 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · light\n  3. 00b · FactCount · 01-anatomy · light\n  4. 00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · light\n  5. 00b · ScaleStrip · 05-og-column · light\n  6. 00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · light\nBatch 4:\n  1. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · light\n  2. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 04-platforms-and-voiceover · light\n  3. 00b · YearBand · 03-desktop-exact-day · light\n  4. 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · light\n  5. 00b · PublicPointMap · 03-cells-map-and-list · light\n  6. 00b · SlotMeter · 03-not-provenance · light\nBatch 5:\n  1. 00b · ScaleStrip · 06-ax5-200 · light\n  2. 00b · ScaleStrip · 07-greyscale · light\n  3. 00b · AqiBand · 04-ax5-200 · light\n  4. 00b · AqiBand · 05-greyscale · light\n  5. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 05-ax5-200 · light\n  6. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 06-greyscale · light\nBatch 6:\n  1. 00b · YearBand · 05-ax5-200 · light\n  2. 00b · YearBand · 06-greyscale · light\n  3. 00b · SlotMeter · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n  4. 00b · PublicPointMap · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n  5. 00b · FactCount · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light\n  6. 00b · ScaleStrip · 08-in-context · light\nBatch 7:\n  1. 00b · AqiBand · 06-in-context · light\n  2. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 07-in-context · light\n  3. 00b · YearBand · 07-in-context · light\n  4. 00b · SlotMeter · 05-in-context · light\n  5. 00b · PublicPointMap · 05-in-context · light\n  6. 00b · FactCount · 04-in-context · light\nBatch 8:\n  1. 00b · ScaleStrip · 01-anatomy · dark\n  2. 00b · ScaleStrip · 02-layers-by-state · dark\n  3. 00b · ScaleStrip · 03-compare · dark\n  4. 00b · ScaleStrip · 04-instrument-states · dark\n  5. 00b · AqiBand · 01-anatomy · dark\n  6. 00b · AqiBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark\nBatch 9:\n  1. 00b · AqiBand · 03-widget-micro · dark\n  2. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n  3. 00b · FourteenDayStrip · 03-widget-and-window · dark\n  4. 00b · YearBand · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n  5. 00b · YearBand · 04-widget-large-and-gallery · dark\n  6. 00b · SlotMeter · 02-variants-by-state · dark\nBatch 10:\n  1. 00b · PublicPointMap · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n  2. 00b · FactCount · 02-variants-by-state · dark\n  3. 00b · Notes\n\n======================================================================\n00b · Notes (the last artboard)\n======================================================================\nA. Invented strings. List every quoted string in this prompt that is not in the house-style fixtures or the component contract, grouped by component. This includes all row labels (\"Flood zone\", \"Radon zone\", \"Air quality index (AQI)\", \"Wildfire hazard potential\"), all control names (\"Zoom in\", \"Zoom out\", \"Move map left/up/down/right\", \"List cells\"), all spoken labels and readouts (including the YearBand October and November readouts and the stale and failed Air labels), all summaries (including both YearBand summaries and \"14 neighbor posts in your cell in 30 days. 3 Pantopus posts not counted.\"), all nine List cells rows, all widget and legend lines, all specimen item names, all offline and fallback lines (including \"You're offline. The map needs a connection.\"), \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\", the also-used-in lines, and the RankBadge numeral \"#3\".\n\nB. Assumptions:\n- Board conventions: the artboard naming override (C0); the off-scale micro-geometry (C13); the dark marker and pointer halos fixed at #0F172A, while AqiBand gaps follow the host surface (C6); phone specimen cards drawn 358 wide in every phone frame (C2); the web-1440 card widths (C2).\n- Specimen clocks (C10): ready and offline Air specimens are drawn at 7:10 AM, alert and still-above specimens at 4:10 PM, and stale specimens at TODAY 6:10 PM. So \"ready\" and \"stale\" differ by age, not only by caption.\n- ScaleStrip: \"You\" in compare is the recipient's own address with specimen values; You = Wildfire \"Low · 2 of 5\", and the other three layers are in the same band as Dana. The Air row inside the instrument leaves out the pollutant and prints the AqiBand range labels.\n- AqiBand: \"PM2.5\" is the pollutant for AQI 42.\n- FourteenDayStrip: the cell height is 76pt (6 + 44 + 4 + 16 + 6). The widget variant uses a 60pt cell with at most 2 marks before \"+N\", to fit its 100pt budget in the 158pt widget.\n- PLACE B pickup: the frequency is Not set, so only the next Thursday (Thu 22 Oct) is drawn, and there is no weekly rhythm. The Thanksgiving move is drawn because the City of Camas holiday notice applies to every Thursday route.\n- YearBand: the pickup rhythm lane is not counted in \"N dates\"; the strip does count pickups as items. County rules are drawn as bars, the same as in FourteenDayStrip. The desktop label column is 128px. The collision threshold is 14px.\n- PublicPointMap: the nine cell names and buckets; the two-row controls cluster; the no-cache offline line.\n- FactCount: the claim-time receipt shows Place · Dates only, because claimed facts come from T1. The \"You can also add\" list from the research brief belongs to the host x-place-file, not to this component.\n- SlotMeter: the elapsed bar is 4pt tall, outlined for the remaining part, and decorative. The RankBadge is 120×64pt.\n\nC. Normalisations:\n- The contract example \"as of Sep 12, 2026\" became \"as of Sat 12 Sep 2026\", following the house date rule.\n- The contract example \"Closes Tue, Sep 22\" became \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\", because Tue 22 Sep is before TODAY (Mon 19 Oct) and the window would already be closed. The fixture window opens Mon 5 Oct.\n- The contract example \"Crossed 151 at 4:00 PM\" is drawn as \"Crossed 101 at 4:00 PM\", because AQI 118 does not cross 151, and 101 is the default.\n- The contract example \"Next 14 days: 9 items\" was replaced by the fixture count \"Next 14 days: 6 items\".\n- The contract example \"Next 12 months: 9 dates. Next: Furnace warranty ends Nov 14.\" was replaced by fixture data.\n- The contract's widget lane names used Camas, which is PLACE B's city. HOME A uses \"You · Vancouver · Clark County · Washington\".\n- The outbound action \"Free test kits · Washington Dept of Health ↗\" became \"Get a free test kit · Washington Dept of Health ↗\", so it starts with a verb.\n- The research brief's radon wording \"Zone 1 — highest potential of EPA's 3 zones\" is not used. The board uses the contract's approved string \"Radon Zone 1 — highest potential (county)\".\n- The empty-strip line follows QuietDayReceipt (\"next two weeks\"). The brief's alternative is \"next 14 days\".\n- The widget text fallback was reworded as \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Voter registration must arrive by\", and relative counts were added to the summaries and widget lines.\n\nD. Deviations from the contract (each one needs sign-off):\n- The stale ProvenanceMark keeps full ink instead of the contract's \"50% opacity\", and the holiday ghost keeps full ink instead of being dimmed. Reason: text.secondary at 50% is 1.98:1 on base and 1.91:1 on sunken, and at 40% it is 1.66:1, all below the house 3:1 rule. Staleness is carried by the age words, and the move by the strike.\n- Compare pointers are identical triangles, not the contract's \"same marker form\" (the capsule), so the two readings can be placed above and below one track.\n- FactCount pips sit below the integer, not beside it, so the block fits its 160pt maximum width.\n- The FactCount spoken label is \"14 on file: …\", not the contract's \"11 things on file: …\", so the spoken name contains the visible text (WCAG 2.5.3). The keeper strip shows \"14 on file\", matching the place file for the same home, and \"11 on file\" is used only as the claim-time count.\n- OG text: the contract says \"text is at least 40px cap\". This board reads that as a 40px font size, as the research brief's \"≥40 px type\" does; a 40px cap height would need about 56px type and would not fit the 630px frame. The single sources line is 28px, spanning the full 1168px width, because at 40px it would not fit on one line.\n- The dark highlighted DateRow uses a dark base wash with a #38BDF8 outline, because the light infoBg wash under dark text is 1.16:1.\n\nE. Open questions for the founder:\n(1) The optional ±0.005° range box has the home at its geometric centre, even when the frame is off-centre. Should it exist at all? Until this is answered, it is drawn only in the pending-decision frame on PublicPointMap 01 and is not published.\n(2) \"Closes Tue 27 Oct\" has no relative count, even though dates beyond tomorrow normally add one (\"in 8 days\"). This follows the no-countdown rule for the founding window. The native spoken month readouts on YearBand also give absolute dates only.\n(3) For 00a: should the stale mark style change from opacity to \"full ink + age words\" (or a dashed stroke) in the contract?\n(4) For 00d: QuietDayReceipt uses a bare stroked check, while the provenance grammar reserves the ticked disc for \"You added\" and legends print \"✓ You added this\". Keep the exemption (bare stroke, no disc, always followed by \"Checked\"), or switch CheckItems to a glyph that is not a check?\n(5) Confirm the PM2.5 sensitive-groups sentence against EPA TAD Table 4.\n\nF. Omitted states: none. List every cell printed \"n/a\" together with its reason.\n\nDONE WHEN\n- All 57 artboards in the manifest exist with exactly these names, each shown as a visible label.\n- Every component has all of the following:\n  - anatomy with callouts (sizes plus token names)\n  - every variant and every state from its section drawn on this board, with each variant × state grid complete (no blank cells, one reason per n/a) and the remaining variants and states on the artboards named in the PUBLISH checklist\n  - a light and a dark specimen\n  - an AX5 and a 200% specimen\n  - a greyscale specimen with cue captions\n  - its one-sentence summary and spoken label drawn as text\n  - two or three in-context crops that name their surface ids. ScaleStrip, AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip and YearBand also have a line naming the variant for every other usedIn surface.\n- No hex value appears except the six named AQI swatches and the dark values listed in C6.\n- No text sits on an AQI fill. text.muted is never used for readable text. No text.secondary text sits on a surface.sunken fill. No border token is the only edge or fill of a band, segment, bar, mark or input.\n- Every provenance mark is at full ink and at least 3:1 in every state, including stale marks and holiday ghosts.\n- Every widget block and the OG column print the provenance word next to each mark or in an in-block legend line.\n- Filled discs, rings and ticked discs appear only as provenance marks. The single exception is the bare stroked check in QuietDayReceipt lines, always followed by \"Checked\". Position markers are capsules, compare uses identical labelled triangle pointers, and SlotMeter uses solid vs hatched.\n- County and state rules are bars in both FourteenDayStrip and YearBand.\n- Every stated geometry adds up: the 76pt strip cell, the 60pt widget cell and its 100pt budget, the 612px OG budget, the 848px YearBand desktop grid, and the controls cluster within 326pt.\n- No mark, cell or segment is a target on iOS, Android or web-390. Only the desktop-web FourteenDayStrip cells are buttons, and they are 44px.\n- No grade, score, progress ring, completion ring, countdown, streak or confetti appears anywhere. No percentage is used as a score, confidence or completion. The FEMA annual-chance percentages (\"0.2% a year\", \"1% a year or more\", \"Zone AE — 1% chance each year\") are band names and are allowed.\n- \"N of M\" appears only as:\n  - the Wildfire reading \"<Word> · N of 5\" (for example \"Moderate · 3 of 5\" or \"Low · 2 of 5\") and its spoken forms\n  - the SlotMeter \"3 of 5 open\" and the annotation label \"0 of 5 open → treated as closed\"\n  - the AqiBand spoken \"category N of 6\".\n- Every fixture string matches the house style exactly, and every invented string, deviation and open question is on 00b · Notes.\n- Fail-closed states: SlotMeter closed and lookup failed render nothing and are drawn per C5. FourteenDayStrip and YearBand errors draw no strip or band; a 00c · InlineErrorRow with Retry takes the slot (not per C5).\n- The PublicPointMap range box R appears only inside the \"PENDING DECISION — do not publish\" frame on PublicPointMap 01.\n\nPUBLISH\nWhen I accept a component, add it to the Pantopus design system under this exact name: ScaleStrip, AqiBand, FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, SlotMeter, PublicPointMap or FactCount. Include its light and dark specimens, and include every variant (V1…Vn) and every state listed in the component's section, wherever it is drawn on this board. Name each one \"<Component> / <Vn name> / <state>\". Checklist:\n- ScaleStrip: V1–V10; loading, ready, partial (loading), partial (failed), differs tag, stale air row and AX5, plus the OG column recipe. From 01, 02, 03, 04, 05 and 06.\n- AqiBand: V1–V6; ready, stale, no reading (with and without the provider error), alert, still above threshold and offline, plus threshold 151 and the clamp. From 01, 02, 03 and 04.\n- FourteenDayStrip: V1–V4; loading, ready, empty, stale, permission-denied, T1, error and highlighted row, plus the overflow and holiday-move specimens. From 01, 02, 03 and 04 (including the web-1440 per-cell buttons).\n- YearBand: V1 (HOME A and PLACE B) and V2–V4; loading, ready, empty checked, error and offline, plus desktop exact-day placement with the collision rule. From 01, 02, 03 and 04.\n- SlotMeter: V1–V3; open, closed (absent) and lookup failed (absent), with the RankBadge. From 01 and 02.\n- PublicPointMap: V1–V3; ready, loading, vector fallback and offline (with and without a cache), plus the List cells view. From 01, 02 and 03. Do not publish the range box R.\n- FactCount: V1–V3; default, loading and offline. From 01 and 02.\nPublish the RankBadge only as part of SlotMeter, and the six AQI swatches only as part of AqiBand. Do not publish the stand-ins for 00a, 00c or 00d parts."
