      {
        "prompt": {
          "id": "00c",
          "name": "Foundations: Rows and lists",
          "componentsCovered": [
            "DateRow",
            "FactRow",
            "LockedActionRow",
            "InlineErrorRow",
            "GrantLimitList",
            "FirstWeekRow",
            "BillRow",
            "MemberRow",
            "InviteRow",
            "NotificationRow",
            "TextActionRow",
            "ThumbnailRail"
          ],
          "artboardCount": 61,
          "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is the Foundations board: Rows and lists.\n\nTYPE: NEW (a component specimen board). It has no screens, only component specimens. Twelve components are specified below, each under its exact name. Later projects will ask for these components, variants and states by the exact names and slugs on this board and will have no other reference, so every specimen must be complete, exact and labelled.\n\nATTACH: none. The component contract does not list any of these twelve rows as already shipped. Draw them from this prompt.\n\nCOMPONENTS ON THIS BOARD (exact names, in build order): DateRow · FactRow · LockedActionRow · InlineErrorRow · GrantLimitList · FirstWeekRow · BillRow · MemberRow · InviteRow · NotificationRow · TextActionRow · ThumbnailRail.\n\n==================================================================\nPART 1 — BOARD CONVENTIONS (these apply to every artboard on this board, all 61 of them)\n==================================================================\n\n1.1 Artboard names. Every artboard is named \"00c · <ComponentName> · <NN-what> · <light|dark>\", exactly as in the ARTBOARDS manifest at the end, and shows that name as a visible label above the frame, in caption 12/16 text.secondary. The last artboard is \"00c · Notes\".\n\n1.2 The five artboards per component. Each of the twelve components gets exactly these five artboards, in this order:\n  01-anatomy · light: one large specimen at 2x zoom with numbered callouts, then five labelled text panels: ACCESSIBILITY, COPY RULES, PLATFORMS, INSTEAD OF and USED IN.\n  02-grid · light: the variant × state grid at 1x, one cell per listed combination.\n  03-ax5-200-greyscale · light: two large-text columns side by side at the top: (a) iOS at AX5 Dynamic Type, where body is 53pt; (b) Android at 200% font scale with Android 14 nonlinear scaling. Underneath them, at full artboard width and at 1x, (c) a greyscale (0% saturation) copy of the full 02 grid.\n  04-in-context · light: two or three mini crops of the named consuming surfaces, plus any platform variants the component section asks for.\n  05-grid · dark: the same grid as 02, in the same layout, in dark tokens (per 1.6), plus the 1x anatomy specimen in dark, top left.\n\n1.3 Canvas and widths. Artboards are at least 1440 wide, on surface.app. Grow an artboard's width or height to fit its cells at 1x; never scale a cell down. Unless a cell says otherwise, draw each row at iOS width: a 393pt frame with 16pt side margins, so the row content is 361pt wide. Where a component section asks for Android, draw the row in a 412dp frame (380dp content). Web 390 uses a 390px frame, and web 1440 uses a 720px list column.\n\n1.4 Callouts. Callouts are drawn outside the component: a numbered circle (caption, text.secondary outline), a 1px text.secondary leader line, and a caption that gives the size in pt/dp/px and the token name, e.g. \"② title · body 16/24/400 · text.primary\". Callouts never overlap the component. Show spacing with 1px dimension lines and a number (\"16pt · spacing.4\"). Every 01-anatomy also carries a \"web menu\" callout that states how the component's custom actions appear on web (per 1.14).\n\n1.5 Grid layout and labels.\n  - Variants are rows, labelled at the left in label 13/18 text.strong. States are columns, labelled at the top in overline 11/16/600.\n  - Label every variant row exactly \"<code> · <slug>\" (e.g. \"V1a · pickup-both\") and every state column exactly \"<code> · <slug>\" (e.g. \"S2 · highlighted-arrival\"), using the codes and slugs given in each component section.\n  - Give every cell a caption under it, in caption 12/16 text.secondary, exactly \"<Component> · <variant slug> · <state slug>\" (e.g. \"DateRow · deadline-voter · done\").\n  - Each cell draws the component at 1x. Draw only the cells listed in the component's GRID CELLS. Any grid position that is not listed stays empty canvas: no frame, no label, no n/a text.\n  - An \"n/a\" cell appears only where this prompt writes \"n/a\"; there, write \"n/a — <reason>\" in caption text.secondary inside a plain cell, with the normal cell caption under it. Never draw a ghost component in an n/a cell.\n\n1.6 Tokens. Use token names only. Light: surface.base #FFFFFF, raised #F9FAFB, sunken #F3F4F6, app #F6F7F9; text.primary #111827, strong #374151, secondary #6B7280, muted #9CA3AF (placeholders only; nothing on this board uses it); border.default #E5E7EB, strong #D1D5DB, subtle #F3F4F6, focus #0284c7; primary.50 #f0f9ff, primary.700 #0369a1; success #059669; warning #D97706; error #DC2626 / errorBg #FEF2F2; info #0284c7 / infoBg #F0F9FF; identity.home #16A34A. Dark: surface.base #0F172A, raised #1E293B, sunken #0F172A, app #020617; text.primary #E5E7EB, strong #F1F5F9, secondary #94A3B8, muted #64748B; border.default #1F2937, strong #374151, subtle #1E293B, focus #38BDF8; dark links use dark border.focus (#38BDF8).\n  The dark token set has no infoBg, errorBg, primary.50, primary.700 or semantic entries, and dark sunken equals dark base, so every sunken shape would vanish on a base row. On every 05-grid · dark artboard, use exactly these substitutes, and list each one on Notes:\n  (D1) Highlight: a dark surface.raised wash plus the 4pt leading bar in dark border.focus (see 1.8). On a row that already sits on raised (D3), use the leading bar alone.\n  (D2) Write-failure fill: dark surface.raised plus a 1.5px error border.\n  (D3) Rows that sit on sunken in light sit on dark surface.raised in dark, with dark text.strong.\n  (D4) Any surface.sunken fill (skeleton bars, avatar circles, StatusChip, ScopeChip and \"Statewide — WA\" chip fills, thumbnail slots, the disabled CTA) becomes dark surface.raised when it sits on a dark base row, and dark border.strong when it sits on a dark raised row. Text inside keeps dark text.strong.\n  (D5) Selection fill (ThumbnailRail selected row, ChoiceChip selected): dark surface.raised plus a 1.5px dark border.focus edge plus a leading check in dark border.focus. Never primary.50 in dark.\n  (D6) Anything drawn in primary.700 that is not a link (the upload ring, the retry and minting spinners, the unread dot) uses dark border.focus in dark. The upload ring track is dark border.strong.\n  (D7) Semantic glyph hues (success tick, warning glyph, error glyph) and the identity.home rule keep their light values in dark, on glyphs and rules only, never on text. Check each at 3:1 or better against the dark surface it sits on, and write the ratio in a caption beside the first occurrence.\n  (D8) Card edges: any card in dark (the LockedActionRow V3 card, the InlineErrorRow V5 host card, any card in a dark cell) gets a 1px dark text.secondary keyline, because dark border.default on raised is 1.00:1. Write its ratio in a caption beside the first occurrence.\n  Increase Contrast: no separate artboard. Every 4.5:1 text and 3:1 graphic check on this board must also hold under Increase Contrast. Under Increase Contrast, cards in light get the same 1px text.secondary keyline as D8; nothing else changes. Write this once as a caption on each 05 artboard and list it on Notes.\n  Row separators are 1px border.default hairlines, inset 16pt from the leading edge. They are decoration only: no row depends on a hairline as its only edge.\n\n1.7 Type. Use only the scale: body 16/24/400 · bodyMedium 16/24/500 · bodySmall 14/20/400 · bodySmallMedium 14/20/500 · label 13/18/600 · caption 12/16/400 · captionMedium 12/16/500 · overline 11/16/600 caps +0.5. Use SF Pro on iOS, Roboto on Android and system-ui on web. Amounts use tabular figures.\n\n1.8 Targets, focus, highlight, selection and disabled actions (every component).\n  - Targets are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android with 8dp gaps between targets, and 44px on web. In each 01-anatomy, draw every target as a dashed 1px text.secondary rectangle labelled \"target 44pt / 48dp / 44px\".\n  - A ProvenanceMark, a glyph or a dot is never a target by itself. The enclosing row or button is.\n  - Focus is a 2px border.focus ring drawn 2px outside the whole row. When a row holds a separate target (link, overflow, Retry, Resend, Add, dismiss), focus on that target rings that target only.\n  - Highlight (arrival from a notification) is an infoBg wash across the full row plus a 4pt border.focus bar on the leading edge, full row height. It has no outline and never carries a check glyph. If the row carries a 2px identity.home rule, the bar sits directly inside that rule. In the \"on arrival\" frame, the focus ring is also present, drawn 2px outside the row, so bar (inside) and ring (outside) never touch.\n  - Selection, where it exists, is a primary.50 fill plus a leading check glyph (dark: D5).\n  - Focus, highlight and selection must each look different. Draw one focused cell beside each highlighted or selected cell the component section asks for.\n  - Disabled text actions look the same on every component: the label in text.secondary (never primary.700, never text.muted), kept focusable, with a reason caption directly under it in caption 12/16 text.secondary. Disabled filled controls (the LockedActionRow V1 CTA) use a surface.sunken fill with a text.strong label (dark: D4).\n\n1.9 AX5 / 200% rules (every 03 artboard).\n  - Text wraps and never truncates or ellipsises, except where a component names the one field that truncates first.\n  - Side-by-side pairs stack vertically.\n  - Trailing elements (amount, mark, chevron, text action) move below the text block, aligned to the text's leading edge.\n  - Leading glyphs and marks scale with the text, and ProvenanceMark keeps its shape.\n  - Row height grows, and the minimum heights below are minimums only.\n  - Label each column \"iOS · AX5 (body 53pt)\" and \"Android · 200%\".\n\n1.10 Greyscale (every 03 artboard). Draw the full 02 grid desaturated, with the same labels and cell captions. Beside it, write one caption per state or variant naming the non-colour cue that carries it, for example \"done = tick glyph + 'You marked this done'\" or \"highlighted = 4pt leading bar\". If a cell only reads through colour, that is a defect: fix the component, not the caption.\n\n1.11 Motion. Highlights fade out over 300ms or less. Under Reduce Motion they cross-fade. Under Reduce Motion, spinners are removed and the in-progress label (\"Sending…\", \"Reissuing…\", \"Retrying…\", \"Making a link…\") stays as static text. Idle loops stop within 5s.\n\n1.12 Components from other Foundations boards. These rows embed components designed on other boards: ProvenanceMark, SourceCaption, ScopeChip, KindGlyph, StatusChip, ChoiceChip, FreshnessLine, OfflineNotice, InlineUndo and WarmingSkeleton. If the published Pantopus design system already contains one of them, use it. Otherwise draw this stand-in exactly and label it \"stand-in\":\n  - ProvenanceMark: OFFICIAL = solid disc; ON RECORD, NOT CONFIRMED = ring with a stroke of at least 1.5px; YOU ADDED = solid disc with the tick knocked out as a cut-out, never a second colour. Ink is text.secondary, or dark text.secondary in dark mode. Size S = 16pt in rows; XS = 12pt minimum. The spoken names are \"official\", \"on record, not confirmed\" and \"you added this\". Filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else. Each surface prints the word once, as the legend line \"● Official · ○ On record, not confirmed · ✓ You added this\" in caption text.secondary, or as the word beside the first mark.\n  - SourceCaption: caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"Authority · scope · as-of\". It wraps and never ellipsises the authority. On sunken it is text.strong.\n  - ScopeChip: pill, height 24pt, surface.sunken fill, a 12pt glyph plus label 13/18 in text.strong. When the chip opens the scope control, its hit area is 44pt / 48dp; draw that target. The chip strings are \"Saved place · Only you\" (person glyph) and \"Your household\" (house glyph). They are spoken as \"Visible to only you\" and \"Visible to your household\". The approved sentence forms are \"Only you will see this.\" and \"Everyone in this household will see this.\" Where finance permissions differ between members, the sentence names the people instead (\"You and Sam can see these\"); never \"Everyone\" there.\n  - KindGlyph: 24pt line icon, 2pt stroke, text.strong, one distinct drawing per kind: garbage, recycling, garbage+recycling, notice deadline, warranty ends, HOA dues, property-tax (appeal / due), voter registration, bill. Never one generic calendar icon.\n  - StatusChip: pill, height 24pt, captionMedium, surface.sunken fill, text.strong. Any semantic hue goes only on a leading glyph. Exactly one per row.\n  - ChoiceChip: pill, radius pill, 32pt visual height inside a 44pt / 48dp target, label 13/18. Selected = primary.50 fill + primary.700 text + a leading check glyph (dark: D5). Unselected = a 1px text.secondary edge + text.strong label (see Notes 3). The focus ring is distinct from selection. At AX sizes the chips wrap to radio rows.\n  - InlineUndo: the row collapses in place to \"<what happened> · Undo\". It is announced with role=status, and Undo is focusable. The Undo target is 44pt and stays until the user leaves the screen. There is no countdown.\n  - WarmingSkeleton: surface.sunken bars (dark: D4) in the final geometry and at the final height. There is no text inside. The container is announced once as \"Loading\" (aria-busy on web), not shape by shape. It shimmers, or is static under Reduce Motion.\n  - FreshnessLine / OfflineNotice: caption text.secondary, e.g. \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" (invented). Each disabled control gets a reason caption under it (1.8). There is no banner colour.\n\n1.13 Fixtures. Use the house-style FIXTURES. TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026, 6:10 PM Pacific. Relative counts in this prompt are computed from that date. Any string this prompt marks \"(invented)\", and any string you add yourself, goes on the Notes artboard. Dates always show the weekday (\"Fri 23 Oct\"). They never use numeric formats like 10/23/2026, and never \"midnight\".\n\n1.14 Platforms default. Unless a component's PLATFORMS line says otherwise, the contract has no platform differences for it: write \"No platform differences\" in its PLATFORMS panel. On every component:\n  - Custom actions are VoiceOver custom actions on iOS and TalkBack custom actions on Android.\n  - On web, custom actions that are not already visible buttons get a visible row menu button: a 20px ellipsis in a 44px target at the row's trailing edge. Where a row already has an overflow button or visible buttons for those actions, that is the web menu; do not add a second one. Every web crop in 04 draws this button where it applies.\n  - Disabled controls stay in the iOS and Android accessibility tree with their reason as a hint.\n\n1.15 In-context crops (every 04 artboard). Every crop that shows a ProvenanceMark also shows the legend line from 1.12 (or the word beside the first mark) and the ScopeChip for that surface (\"Your household\" for Home A, \"Saved place · Only you\" for Place B). Label each crop \"<surface id> · <platform>\".\n\n==================================================================\nPART 2 — THE TWELVE COMPONENTS\n==================================================================\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nDateRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. One dated fact in a list. Its row grammar is shared by the 14-day strip list, the calendar agenda, the place file Dates section and reminder rows.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Row: minimum height 56pt, padding 16pt horizontal and 12pt vertical, on surface.base.\n② Leading KindGlyph, 24pt, text.strong, top-aligned with the title, with a 12pt gap after it.\n③ Title in body 16/24/400, text.primary. It wraps and is never truncated.\n④ Line 2 in caption 12/16 text.secondary: the relative date plus the absolute date, e.g. \"in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\". \"Tonight\", \"Today\" and \"Tomorrow\" stand alone, with no absolute date after them. An approximate date reads \"about Dec 2026\".\n⑤ SourceCaption short form (authority · scope), which follows on line 2 after a middot or wraps to line 3.\n⑥ Trailing ProvenanceMark S (16pt), vertically centred, with 8pt (spacing.2) between it and the text.\n⑦ An optional chip after the title reading \"Statewide — WA\", in ScopeChip geometry (24pt pill, surface.sunken, text.strong) with a 12pt state-outline glyph.\n⑧ Annual rows and self-entered rows get a 2px identity.home rule on the leading edge, full row height, plus a recurrence caption on the last line in caption text.secondary (\"Every year\", \"Every month\", \"Does not repeat\", all invented).\n⑨ Done tick: a 16pt stroke check, not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark.\n⑩ Web menu callout: on web, a row menu button (20px ellipsis, 44px target) sits after the mark and holds the four custom actions.\n\nVARIANTS (all drawn; code · slug):\n  V1 pickup (Home A, as of TODAY, before Maya confirmed her day). The title names the bins.\n    V1a · pickup-both: garbage+recycling glyph · \"Recycling and garbage\" · \"Tomorrow · Waste Connections · city schedule\" (\"city schedule\" invented) · hollow mark.\n    V1b · pickup-garbage: garbage glyph · \"Garbage only\" · \"in 8 days · Tue 27 Oct · Waste Connections · city schedule\" · hollow mark.\n  V2 · holiday-moved (Place B, Camas; the hollow mark is an assumption): garbage glyph · \"Thanksgiving — moved to Fri 27 Nov\" · \"in 39 days · Fri 27 Nov · City of Camas 2026 calendar\" · hollow mark.\n  V3 deadline. The weekday is always shown, and received-by deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n    V3a · deadline-voter: voter registration glyph · \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · chip \"Statewide — WA\" · \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct · Washington Secretary of State · statewide\" (authority string invented) · filled mark.\n    V3b · deadline-notice: notice deadline glyph · \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\" · \"in 133 days · Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Lease ends Wed 31 Mar 2027\" · last line \"Does not repeat · Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\" (\"Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\" invented) · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule.\n    V3c · deadline-tax: property-tax due glyph · \"Property tax, 2nd half\" · \"in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov · Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\" · filled mark · identity.home rule · \"Every year\".\n  V4 · conditional-rule: property-tax appeal glyph · \"Property-tax appeal window\" · \"Closes Thu 1 Jul 2027, or 60 days after your value notice was mailed\" · \"Clark County Board of Equalization · county-wide\" · filled mark · identity.home rule · \"Every year\".\n  V5 · reminder: warranty glyph · \"Reminder: Water-heater warranty ends Sat 12 Dec\" (the \"Reminder:\" prefix is invented) · \"in 54 days · Sat 12 Dec · You added this\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule · \"Does not repeat\".\n  V5x · reminder-approx (fixture delta: the warranty date was entered as approximate): \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"about Dec 2026\" · YOU ADDED mark.\n  V6 · money: HOA dues glyph · \"HOA dues\" · amount \"$285.00\" right-aligned in bodyMedium with tabular figures, placed before the mark · \"in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov · You added this\" · YOU ADDED mark · identity.home rule · \"Every month\".\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · highlighted (per 1.8: infoBg wash plus the 4pt border.focus leading bar, no outline; dark: D1), with accessibility focus moved onto the row. Draw two frames as two columns:\n    S2a · highlighted-arrival: wash, bar and the focus ring 2px outside the row.\n    S2b · highlighted-decayed: wash and bar gone; the focus ring remains.\n  S3 · done: title and line 2 in text.secondary, the ⑨ tick before the title, and line 2 prefixed \"You marked this done ·\". Done is personal: on every row, including the civic V3a row, it stays Only you and is never shown to the household. Add an outside annotation on the V3a S3 cell: \"done stays Only you\".\n  S4 · permission-hidden: the row is not rendered. The rows above and below close the gap, with no placeholder and no ghost row. An annotation arrow outside the list reads \"row absent: viewer lacks permission\".\n  SF · focused: the focus ring from 1.8 on the whole row.\n\nGRID CELLS (02 and 05):\n  - V1a, V1b, V2, V3a, V3b, V3c, V4, V5, V5x and V6, each in S1 and S3.\n  - V1a and V3a in S2a and S2b.\n  - One S4 cell: a three-row list of V1a, [absent V6] and V3a.\n  - V3a in SF, placed directly beside V3a S2a and V3a S2b.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03):\n  - Draw V3a and V6.\n  - The title wraps to as many lines as needed.\n  - The \"Statewide — WA\" chip drops below the title.\n  - Line 2 wraps at middots.\n  - The amount and mark move below the text block, amount first, then the mark scaled to about 28pt.\n  - The KindGlyph scales to 32pt and stays top-aligned.\n  - The identity.home rule stays full height.\n\nGREYSCALE (03): hollow vs filled vs knocked-out tick must still read. Done reads through the tick glyph and the words. Highlighted reads through the 4pt leading bar. The annual rule reads as a 2px rule, and \"Every year\" carries the meaning.\n\nACCESSIBILITY (panel):\n  - The whole row is one element and the target (min 56pt), read in visual order. The mark and glyph are not targets.\n  - Pattern: \"<title>, <line 2 as shown>, <authority, scope>, <mark name>\". The spoken label says only the dates the row shows; \"Tomorrow\" is spoken as \"tomorrow\" with no absolute date. Example: \"Recycling and garbage, tomorrow, Waste Connections city schedule, on record, not confirmed.\"\n  - Done rows start with \"You marked this done\". Done stays Only you.\n  - Custom actions: Edit · Remind me · Where this comes from · Mark done. On web they sit in the ⑩ row menu button.\n  - Non-colour encoding: the glyph shape carries the kind, the mark shape carries provenance, the leading bar carries highlight, and the words carry done.\n  - Contrast: text at least 4.5:1, mark at least 3:1.\n\nCOPY RULES (panel):\n  - For deadlines, the title names the action: \"Tell your landlord in writing by Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\n  - Received-by deadlines say \"must arrive by\".\n  - Dates are spelled out, never 10/11/2026.\n  - Beyond tomorrow, the relative count comes first: \"in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\". Conditional rules (V4) are exempt from the relative count.\n  - Source captions carry a scope word: \"Clark County Treasurer · county-wide\".\n  - Pickup titles use exactly \"Recycling and garbage\" or \"Garbage only\".\n  - Holiday moves read \"moved to Fri 27 Nov\", never \"delayed\" or \"cancelled\".\n  - \"I did this\" reads \"You marked this done\" and stays Only you.\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14). Web adds the ⑩ row menu button.\n\nINSTEAD OF (panel):\n  - Instead of red text or an overdue chip on an annual date that has passed, draw the next occurrence with its \"Every year\" caption. Annual dates never inherit overdue red.\n  - Instead of one generic calendar icon for every row, draw the specific KindGlyph. The glyph is what tells kinds apart without colour.\n  - Instead of a greyed placeholder row for a date the viewer may not see, draw nothing. A ghost row leaks that something exists.\n  - Instead of a numeric date like 10/26/2026, draw \"Mon 26 Oct\". The weekday is what people plan by.\n\nUSED IN: f5-today-calendar-strip, f3-household-calendar, x-place-file, x-date-sheet, f3-household-notifications, f7-today-widget.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops (each with the legend line and ScopeChip per 1.15):\n  (1) f5-today-calendar-strip, iOS, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\", a card with a 14-cell strip outline above rows V1a, V3a and V6, a foot row \"+ Add a date\", and the legend line. Annotate the strip: \"strip cells are not targets; the rows below are\".\n  (2) x-place-file, web 1440 list column, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\", section overline \"DATES\" with rows V3b, V4 and V5, each with its ⑩ row menu button, and the legend line.\n  (3) f3-household-calendar, Android 412, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\", an agenda with day header \"Tue 20 Oct\" and row V1a in S2a, and the legend line.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nFactRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. One row per fact in the place file and in settings. The fact is known, missing, or not available at this tier.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Row of 56pt minimum, padding 16pt horizontal, surface.base.\n② Label in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary, above\n③ the value in body 16/24 text.primary.\n④ ProvenanceMark S (16pt) after the value, with an 8pt gap.\n⑤ Trailing chevron (16pt, text.secondary) or a text action in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), e.g. \"Add\".\n⑥ Missing form: the label, then an ask sentence in body text.primary, then the text action \"Add\".\n⑦ Disclosure row \"More you can add (5)\" with a chevron. At most 3 promoted asks may show per screen, and the rest sit under this row.\n⑧ Target rule callout: on rows with a chevron, the whole row is the target. On rows with a text action (missing, declined, permission-disabled), the text action is a separate 44pt / 48dp / 44px button and the row itself is not a target. Rows with neither (V3, V8) are not targets.\n⑨ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (all drawn; code · slug; the home each cell belongs to is named):\n  V1 known:\n    V1a · known-flood (any address): label \"Flood zone\" · value \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\" · filled mark · chevron.\n    V1b · known-pickup-unconfirmed (Home A, as of TODAY): label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · hollow mark · chevron.\n    V1d · known-pickup-confirmed (Home A, fixture delta: after Maya confirmed Tuesday): label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Tuesday · Waste Connections\" · filled mark · chevron.\n    V1c · known-pickup-placeb (Place B): label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Thursday · City of Camas\" · hollow mark · chevron.\n  V2 missing, drawn as an invitation, never in red:\n    V2a · missing-dates: label \"Dates\" · ask \"Add one date that matters\" · action \"Add\".\n    V2b · missing-frequency (Place B): label \"Pickup frequency\" · value \"Not set\" in text.secondary · action \"Add\".\n  V3 · not-at-tier (Place B): label \"People who live here\" · value \"Claim this address first\" in text.secondary · no action, no chevron, no mark.\n  V4 · done-ask (Home A, same fixture delta as V1d), drawn quiet: a 16pt stroke check (not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark) · \"Pickup day set · Tuesday\" (invented), all in text.secondary · chevron.\n  V5 declined (Home A before Sam joined; fixture delta):\n    V5a · declined-undo: the moment after the decline, as the InlineUndo \"Just you, then. · Undo\".\n    V5b · declined-later: later, re-openable: label \"People who live here\" · value \"Just me\" · action \"Add the people you live with\".\n    V5c · declined-skip: label \"Pickup day\" · value \"Skipped\" (invented) · action \"Set your pickup day\".\n  V6 · permission-disabled: label \"Reminders\" · reason inline in bodySmall text.primary \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" (invented) · action \"Open Settings\".\n  V7 · receipt (Home A): label \"What moved when you claimed\" · value \"2 dates and your pickup day\" (invented) · chevron.\n  V8 \"Your reports\", three sub-cells, each with label \"Your reports\" and a StatusChip (all invented):\n    V8a · reports-checking: \"Pickup schedule\" · chip \"Checking\" · caption \"We'll check by Mon 26 Oct\"\n    V8b · reports-fixed: \"Pickup schedule\" · chip \"Fixed\" · caption \"Fixed Fri 16 Oct\"\n    V8c · reports-no-change: \"Pickup schedule\" · chip \"No change\" · caption \"City of Camas confirmed Thursday\"\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · loading: a WarmingSkeleton at exactly 56pt, with a 40%-width label bar above a 70%-width value bar and no text.\n  S3 · offline: the value stays readable. The text action is disabled per 1.8 (text.secondary, focusable), with the reason caption \"You're offline. You can add this when you're back.\" (invented) under it. On V7 (chevron, no text action) the row stays readable and opens cached content.\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS:\n  - V1a, V1b, V1d, V1c, V2a, V2b, V3, V4, V5a, V5b, V5c, V6, V7, V8a, V8b and V8c in S1.\n  - V1a, V2a, V3 and V8a in S2.\n  - V1a, V2a, V6 and V7 in S3.\n  - V2a in SF, with the ring on \"Add\" only (the row is not a target).\n  - V1b and V1d sit in adjacent rows so the hollow-to-filled change reads side by side.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03):\n  - Draw V1a and V2a.\n  - The label wraps, and the value wraps below it.\n  - The mark and chevron (or \"Add\") drop below the value.\n  - \"Add\" keeps a 44pt / 48dp target.\n\nGREYSCALE: missing reads through the ask sentence plus \"Add\", not through colour. Not-at-tier reads through its words. Unconfirmed vs confirmed reads through the ring vs disc.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - Targets follow ⑧: rows with a chevron are one target (44pt / 48dp / 44px, 56pt visual); text actions are separate buttons.\n  - Known rows merge their label: \"<label>, <value>, <mark name>\". Example: \"Flood zone, Zone X, minimal flood hazard, official.\"\n  - Asks are read as text, then a verb-first button: \"Pickup frequency, not set.\" then \"Add. Button.\"\n  - V5a is announced with role=status (\"Just you, then. Undo.\"), and Undo is focusable.\n  - The loading skeleton is announced once as \"Loading\".\n  - The disabled offline action reads its reason.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - The approved asks are \"Set your pickup day\" · \"Add one date that matters\" · \"Add the people you live with\".\n  - \"Not set\" is in text.secondary.\n  - Hazard values put the plain meaning first: \"Zone X — minimal flood hazard\".\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of a red X or red text for a missing fact, draw the ask sentence with \"Add\". Missing is an invitation, not an error.\n  - Instead of a score, percentage or \"3 of 6\" on the place file, draw plain rows and the \"More you can add (5)\" disclosure. Counts of completion create pressure.\n  - Instead of more than 3 promoted asks, draw 3 and fold the rest under \"More you can add (5)\".\n  - Instead of hiding a not-at-tier fact, draw it grey with \"Claim this address first\" and no button, so the path is named without a dead control.\n\nUSED IN: x-place-file, f6-home-basics-rows, f1-today-tab, f3-household-block, f9-verification-promise-copy, f4-notification-settings.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) x-place-file, iOS, Place B: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\", then V1a (flood zone), V1c (Thursday · City of Camas), V2b, V2a, V3, the disclosure \"More you can add (5)\", and the legend line. Do not use V1b or V1d here: the Tuesday cells are Home A's.\n  (2) f4-notification-settings, Android: V6 at the top of the group.\n  (3) f6-home-basics-rows, web 1440, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\", V7 and V8a.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nLockedActionRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. Replaces or accompanies an unavailable control. It states the reason and the path forward.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① One row, minimum 44pt, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt horizontal.\n② Leading lock glyph, 16pt, text.secondary.\n③ Reason in bodySmall 14/20: text.strong on surface.sunken, or text.secondary on surface.base.\n④ Trailing link \"Verify address\" in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), with a 44pt target.\n⑤ A 1px border.subtle hairline above the row (decoration only).\n⑥ The reason wraps to 2 lines before anything truncates.\n⑦ When the row sits under a disabled CTA, tapping the disabled CTA opens the same reason. Draw a callout arrow from the CTA to the row.\n⑧ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (all drawn; code · slug):\n  V1 · under-cta: a disabled button \"Message your neighbors\" (per 1.8: surface.sunken fill with text.strong label, kept focusable; dark: D4), with the row directly below: \"Address verification needed to message your neighbors · Verify address\".\n  V2 · list-row: \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter · Verify address\". Drawn in two rows: V2s · list-row-sunken and V2b · list-row-base.\n  V3 · card-header: a card titled \"Residency Pass\" (dark: D8 edge) with the row inside the header: \"Address verification needed to show your Residency Pass · Verify address\".\n  V4 · pending (viewer Sam, whose postcard is still in transit; Maya's address is already confirmed): \"We're checking your postcard code — expected Thu 22–Thu 29 Oct\" (invented), with no link.\n  V5 · server-refused, shown after a tap the server refused: \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter. We checked again. · Verify address\" (second sentence invented).\n  V6 · names-who-can-act (viewer Sam): \"Maya can add bills here\", with no link.\n  V7 · not-at-tier (Place B): \"Claim this address first\", grey text.secondary, no CTA.\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · locked.\n  S2 · pending (V4's form).\n  S3 · offline: the link is disabled per 1.8 (text.secondary, focusable), with the reason caption \"You're offline. You can verify when you're back.\" (invented) under it.\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS:\n  - V1, V2s, V2b, V3, V5, V6 and V7 in S1.\n  - V4 in S2.\n  - V1, V2b, V3 and V5 in S3.\n  - V4 in S1: \"n/a — pending is its own variant\".\n  - V4, V6 and V7 in S3: \"n/a — this variant has no link to disable\".\n  - V2b in SF, with the focus ring on the \"Verify address\" link only (per 1.8).\n\nAX5 / 200% (03):\n  - Draw V1 and V2b.\n  - The reason wraps fully.\n  - \"Verify address\" drops to its own line below the reason, left-aligned, keeping its target.\n  - The lock glyph scales to 24pt and stays top-aligned.\n\nGREYSCALE: the lock glyph plus the words carry the meaning. Nothing is coloured except the link, which still reads as a link because of its position and its verb. The offline link reads as disabled through its reason caption.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - The reason is at 4.5:1 or better.\n  - The link names its destination: \"Verify address, opens Verify this address\".\n  - The disabled control is exposed with its reason as a hint: \"Message your neighbors, dimmed. Address verification needed to message your neighbors.\"\n  - The offline link is exposed as dimmed with its reason as a hint.\n  - Row and link targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - The pattern is \"Address verification needed to <specific action>\". Any extra context (V5) follows it as a second sentence.\n  - Never write a generic \"Verification required\".\n  - When someone else can act, name them (\"Maya can add bills here\").\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of red or amber colouring, draw the neutral lock glyph in text.secondary. Nothing is wrong; something is not yet available.\n  - Instead of text.muted for the reason or the disabled link, draw text.strong on sunken or text.secondary on base, because both must be read.\n  - Instead of a present but inert control with no explanation, draw the control with this row under it.\n  - Instead of showing a T1 (saved place) user a verification lock on a home-only feature, draw V7 \"Claim this address first\". Verification means nothing before a claim.\n\nUSED IN: f3b-locked-action-row, f3-members-roster, f3-member-home-dashboard, f3b-invitation-decision, f3-bills-list, f3-bill-detail-web, f3-household-calendar, f10-bill-provenance, f10-extraction-confirm, x-place-file, x-date-sheet, f6-home-basics-rows, f9-block-founders-panel, f11-keeper-strip.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) f3-member-home-dashboard, iOS, viewer Sam: V1.\n  (2) f3-bills-list, Android, viewer Sam before Maya shared bills: V6 under the list header \"Bills\" (no count, total or scope sentence).\n  (3) f9-block-founders-panel, web 1440: V3's card-header form on a card titled \"Block Founders\", with the row \"Address verification needed to earn a Block Founder rank · Verify address\" (invented).\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nInlineErrorRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. Shows a partial failure in one component. It names what failed and keeps everything else live.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① The row sits in the failed component's own slot and height, and it keeps its position in the list.\n② Leading glyph, 16pt, an exclamation in a circle, in error hue (glyph only; dark: D7).\n③ Message in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary.\n④ Trailing \"Retry\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), with a 44pt target.\n⑤ The surface is surface.base. It is errorBg only when a write failed (dark: D2).\n⑥ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (all drawn; code · slug):\n  V1 · provider-unreachable: \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now · Retry\".\n  V2 · carry-failed: \"We couldn't move your water-heater warranty · Retry\" (adapted to the fixture; see Notes 3).\n  V3 · upload-failed: \"Upload failed · Retry\".\n  V4 · save-failed, value preserved, on errorBg: the field above still shows \"Tuesday\". The row reads \"We couldn't save that. Your choice is still here. · Retry\" (second sentence invented).\n  V5 · fail-closed: draw an f9-block-founders-panel card (dark: D8 edge) with its title \"Block Founders\" and a LockedActionRow (V3 form) directly under the title. The founding meter, the invite banner and the Earn row are absent, with no gap and no error row. Outside the card, draw dashed annotation brackets where each would have been, labelled \"founding meter\", \"invite banner\" and \"Earn row\", and the annotation \"fail-closed: nothing rendered, no error row\".\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · failed.\n  S2 · retrying: \"Retry\" becomes \"Retrying…\" (invented) with a 12pt spinner (dark: D6), or the static text under Reduce Motion. The target stays in place and the message stays.\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1–V4 in S1 and S2 · V5 in S1 · V5 in S2: \"n/a — nothing to retry\" · V1 in SF, ring on Retry only.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V4. The message wraps. Retry drops below it on its own line and keeps its target.\n\nGREYSCALE: failure reads through the glyph shape (an exclamation in a circle) and the words. errorBg is not needed to understand V4.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - A polite live-region announcement on appearance.\n  - Retry names its target: V1 \"Retry air quality\"; V2 \"Retry moving your water-heater warranty\" (invented); V3 \"Retry upload\" (invented); V4 \"Retry saving pickup day\" (invented).\n  - Retry targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px.\n\nCOPY RULES: messages are specific and blameless, name the provider or the thing, and say what to do next. Typed input is kept.\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of \"Oops, something went wrong\", draw \"We couldn't reach AirNow just now · Retry\". The user needs to know what failed.\n  - Instead of hiding a failed row among successful ones or dropping it, draw it in its own slot and order, so nothing silently disappears.\n  - Instead of an error row for a fail-closed component, draw nothing. A broken meter must never promise a slot.\n  - Instead of clearing the field on a failed save, keep \"Tuesday\" in it.\n\nUSED IN: f1-today-tab, f1-claim-receipt, f10-mail-day-triage, f10-snap-capture-tray, f10-bill-trend, f4-briefing-optin-card, f4-notification-settings, f6-home-basics-rows, f11-keeper-naming, f11-keeper-strip.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) f1-today-tab, iOS, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\", the air section replaced by V1, with the pickup section above still live and showing its mark plus the legend line.\n  (2) f10-snap-capture-tray, Android: V3 on one tray item.\n  (3) f6-home-basics-rows, web 390: V4.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nGrantLimitList\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. Two scannable lists: what you get now (ticked) and what needs address verification (locked). One component serves invite, attestation and verify.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Grant list heading \"What you get now\" (invented; label 13/18 text.strong). The grant list always comes first.\n② Grant rows, 44pt each: a 16pt stroke check in success hue (a stroke check, not a disc, so it cannot be mistaken for the YOU ADDED mark; dark: D7), a 12pt gap, and a verb phrase in body 16/24 text.primary.\n③ Limit list heading \"What needs address verification\" (invented; label 13/18 text.strong).\n④ Limit rows, 44pt each: a 16pt lock glyph in text.secondary and a verb phrase in body text.primary.\n⑤ Both lists use identical type and row height.\n⑥ Two columns 24pt apart on web 1440. Stacked on mobile.\n⑦ Callout: \"one shared string set; every variant draws from it\".\n⑧ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\nDraw the 01 specimen twice: the stacked iOS form at 2x, and the two-column web 1440 form beside or below it at 1x (1.3 applies; do not shrink it).\n\nSTRING SET (exact):\n  Grants: \"Sees and edits the calendar\" · \"Sees bills and who paid\" · \"Sees who lives here\".\n  Limits: \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · \"Show your Residency Pass\" · \"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\" · \"Earn a Block Founder rank\".\n\nVARIANTS (all drawn; code · slug):\n  V1 · invitation-decision: two columns on web 1440 and stacked on iOS (the grid cell draws the stacked iOS form), with both headings, all 3 grants and all 5 limits.\n  V2 · role-offered: under a disclosure \"Role offered: Member\", the heading \"What you get now\" and the 3 grants only.\n  V3 · attestation: 3 grant rows (the choice of rows is an assumption for Notes): \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\" · \"Show your Residency Pass\", with stroke checks under heading \"What you get once Maya confirms you live here\" (invented).\n  V4 · verify-unlock: heading \"What needs address verification\", then \"Message your neighbors\" · \"Get a residency letter\", then a 44pt row \"and 3 more\" with a chevron that expands the remaining three.\n  V5 · role-caption-member: ChoiceChips \"Member\" (selected) and \"Guest\". Under them, a caption in text.secondary: \"Sees and edits the calendar · Sees bills and who paid · Sees who lives here\". The caption has no visible heading; it is exposed as a list with the accessible name \"What members can do\" (invented).\n  V5g · role-caption-guest: the same chips with \"Guest\" selected; the caption reads \"Sees and edits the calendar\", with the accessible name \"What guests can do\" (invented; the Guest capability is an assumption; list on Notes).\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · accepted: the limit list gains the caption \"Verify your address to unlock these\" in caption text.secondary under its heading.\n  SF · focused.\n  SX · selected.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1–V5 and V5g in S1 · V1 in S2 · V2, V3, V4, V5 and V5g in S2: \"n/a — accepted applies after an invitation is accepted\" · V4 in SF (ring on \"and 3 more\") beside V5 in SX (\"Member\" chip selected), per 1.8.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1. Columns stack, grants first. Phrases wrap, and glyphs stay top-aligned and scale to 24pt. In V5 the chips wrap to radio rows.\n\nGREYSCALE: check vs lock is a shape difference, and the headings carry the meaning. The selected chip reads through its check glyph.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - Each list has a heading, exposed as a heading; where there is no visible heading (V5, V5g), the list has an accessible name.\n  - The check and lock glyphs are decorative; the heading carries the meaning.\n  - Rows are read as list items: \"What you get now, list, 3 items. Sees and edits the calendar.\"\n  - \"and 3 more\" is a 44pt / 48dp button: \"Show 3 more\".\n\nCOPY RULES: every row is a verb phrase. Use the string set exactly. Never write a bare product name.\n\nPLATFORMS: stacked on mobile (iOS, Android, web 390) and two columns on web 1440. The V5 chips follow ChoiceChip's platform notes (iOS segmented control where native; M3 filter chips on Android).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of a warning box around the limits, draw the plain lock rows. Limits are information, not danger.\n  - Instead of bare product names (\"Real Rent\", \"Residency Pass\"), draw verb phrases (\"Share what you pay in rent (Real Rent)\"). People decide on what they can do.\n  - Instead of text.muted on sunken for locked rows, draw body text.primary with a text.secondary lock, because these rows must be read.\n\nUSED IN: f3b-invitation-decision, f3-invite-composer, f3b-owner-attestation, f3b-verify-address-sheet, f9-verification-promise-copy, f3-members-roster.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) f3b-invitation-decision, web 1440: V1, with \"Accept\" and \"Not now\" below.\n  (2) f3b-verify-address-sheet, iOS medium detent with a visible Close: V4.\n  (3) f3-invite-composer, Android: V5.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nFirstWeekRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. The single pointer on Today to the next first-week ask. It comes from a bounded set of steps that is already started.\n\nFIXTURE DELTA. FirstWeekRow specimens show Place B (Jordan Lee) on Tue 13 Oct 2026, 3 days after the Sat 10 Oct save. The 7-day activation window runs Sun 11 Oct through Sat 17 Oct and closes after Sat 17 Oct. The hidden variant shows Mon 19 Oct, when the window has closed. List this delta and this day count on Notes.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① One row, 48pt: padding 16pt horizontal and 12pt vertical (12 + 24 + 12 = 48), surface.base.\n② Text in bodyMedium 16/24 text.primary: \"Next: set your pickup day →\". The arrow is part of the link.\n③ Trailing dismiss button: a 16pt close glyph in text.secondary inside a 44pt / 48dp target, with 8dp between it and the row link.\n④ Callout listing the bounded set: Save (already done) · Pickup day · Reminder or widget · One date or person.\n⑤ Callout: \"Only steps reachable at the current tier are counted. Verify, profile and photo are never steps.\"\n⑥ Callout: \"Shown for 7 days (the activation window).\"\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"the visible dismiss button is the only extra action; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (code · slug):\n  V1a · next-pickup: \"Next: set your pickup day →\".\n  V1b · next-widget: \"Next: put today on your home screen →\" (invented).\n  V2 · hidden (complete or dismissed): draw the Today section stack with no row and no gap, plus the annotation \"hidden: set complete, dismissed, or 7 days passed\".\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · dismissed (stored server-side): the row collapses in place to the InlineUndo \"Hidden from Today · Undo\" (invented). Undo is 44pt and stays until the user leaves Today, with no countdown.\n  SFl · focused-link.\n  SFd · focused-dismiss.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1a and V1b in S1 and S2 · V2 as one cell (column S1) · V1a in SFl beside V1a in SFd, each ringing only its own target.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1a in S1 and S2. The text wraps to two or more lines, and the arrow stays at the end of the text. The dismiss button stays top-aligned at the trailing edge. The row grows beyond 48pt.\n\nGREYSCALE: reads fully through text; no colour is used.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - The whole row is one link: \"Next: set your pickup day. Link.\"\n  - Dismiss is a separate button, \"Dismiss next step\", and is also offered as a custom action on the link.\n  - Undo is announced with role=status.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - Name only the next step, in sentence case, verb first. Never show a count or fraction of steps.\n  - The window matches the activation window: 7 days.\n  - Step strings come from the set: \"set your pickup day\", \"put today on your home screen\", \"add one date that matters\".\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of \"3 of 6\" or any denominator, draw \"Next: <step> →\". Naming the next step moves people without pressure.\n  - Instead of counting verify, profile or photo, draw only the four set steps reachable at the viewer's tier. A step you cannot do is not a step.\n  - Instead of a checklist card, draw this single 48pt row. The full list lives in the place file.\n\nUSED IN: f1-today-tab, x-place-file, f4-briefing-optin-card.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), two crops:\n  (1) f1-today-tab, iOS, Place B: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\", then V1a, then the pickup section (hollow mark, with the legend line).\n  (2) x-place-file, web 390, Place B: ScopeChip \"Saved place · Only you\", the same step as a FactRow ask (\"Set your pickup day\"), with an annotation \"same set, same storage\".\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nBillRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. A household bill with payer attribution, so two people don't pay the same bill.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Row of 64pt minimum, padding 12pt vertical and 16pt horizontal. The whole row opens bill detail.\n② Line 1 left: the provider in bodyMedium 16/24 text.primary. This is the ONLY field that truncates, and it truncates first.\n③ Line 1: one StatusChip after the provider.\n④ Line 1 right: the amount in bodyMedium with tabular figures, right-aligned in the same optical column on every row.\n⑤ Line 2 left: the due date in bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary, \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n⑥ Line 2 right: the attribution in bodySmall text.secondary, \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\". It is never truncated.\n⑦ Overflow button: a 20pt ellipsis in a 44pt / 48dp target. Its menu holds Mark paid · I paid this · Paid a different amount · Skip this month. On web this is the row menu button (1.14).\n⑧ List header (bodySmall text.strong), viewer Maya: \"4 upcoming · $591.17 through Mon 2 Nov · You and Sam can see these\". Viewer Sam: \"… · You and Maya can see these\". Finance access differs between members, so the header names the people instead of \"Everyone\".\n\nFIXTURE ROWS (Home A, viewer Maya unless stated):\n  - Clark Public Utilities · Upcoming · $142.18 · \"Due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct\".\n  - City of Vancouver water · Upcoming · $84.00 · \"Due in 9 days · Wed 28 Oct\".\n  - HOA dues · Upcoming · $285.00 · \"Due in 13 days · Sun 1 Nov\". (HOA dues also appears as DateRow V6; see Notes 2.)\n  - Comcast · Upcoming · $79.99 · \"Due in 14 days · Mon 2 Nov\".\n  - Paid example (invented): Comcast · Paid · $79.99 · \"Due Fri 2 Oct\" · \"Paid by Sam · Thu 1 Oct\".\n  - Overdue example (invented): Waste Connections · Overdue, with an error glyph in the chip · $38.75 · \"Due Thu 15 Oct\".\n  - Due-today example (invented; fixture delta Fri 23 Oct): Clark Public Utilities · Due today · $142.18.\n\nVARIANTS (code · slug):\n  V1 · manage (viewer Maya): the overflow menu is open, showing its four items.\n  V2a · member-overflow (viewer Sam): the overflow holds \"I paid this\" only.\n  V2b · member-no-overflow (viewer Sam): no overflow; the caption \"Maya can mark this paid\" (invented) replaces the right side of line 2.\n  V3 · only-me: line 2 adds a 12pt person glyph and ScopeChip's approved sentence \"Only you will see this.\" after the due date, wrapping to line 3.\n  V4 · former-member: \"Paid by Sam (no longer here) · Thu 1 Oct\".\n  Chip strip rows: C1 · chip-upcoming, C2 · chip-due-today, C3 · chip-overdue, C4 · chip-paid (the fixture example rows above).\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · highlighted from a notification (per 1.8: infoBg wash plus the 4pt border.focus leading bar, no outline; dark: D1), with focus moved to the row. Two columns:\n    S2a · highlighted-arrival: wash, bar and the focus ring 2px outside the row.\n    S2b · highlighted-decayed: wash and bar gone; the focus ring remains.\n  S3 · marked-paid: the row collapses in place to the InlineUndo \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\", announced with role=status. After the user leaves the screen, the row reads \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\" (invented). The household notification is held until the user leaves the screen without undoing; add a callout saying so.\n  S4 · permission-denied (viewer Sam before Maya shared bills; fixture delta): the header shows only the list title \"Bills\", with no count, total or scope sentence, and the list body is replaced by a LockedActionRow in names-who-can-act form, \"Maya can give you access to bills\" (invented).\n  S5 · offline: the FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" (invented) sits above the rows. Rows stay readable. Overflow items are disabled per 1.8, with the reason \"You're offline. You can mark bills paid when you're back.\" (invented).\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS:\n  - V1 in S1, S2a, S2b, S3 and S5.\n  - V2a and V2b in S1; V2a in S4.\n  - V3 in S1.\n  - V4 in S1.\n  - C1, C2, C3 and C4 in S1.\n  - V1 in SF, placed directly beside V1 S2a and V1 S2b.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw the Clark Public Utilities (C1) and paid-Comcast (C4) rows.\n  - The provider wraps; it no longer truncates at AX sizes.\n  - The chip drops below the provider, then the amount below the chip.\n  - The due date and attribution stack, attribution last.\n  - The overflow button stays top-trailing.\n\nGREYSCALE: status reads through the chip words. Overdue has a glyph plus the word. The payer reads through the name. Highlighted reads through the leading bar.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - The label is merged: \"Clark Public Utilities, 142 dollars 18 cents, due Friday 23 October, upcoming.\"\n  - Paid: \"Comcast, 79 dollars 99 cents, paid by Sam, Thursday 1 October.\"\n  - S3 is a live region: \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid. Undo.\" Undo is focusable.\n  - Overflow items are also custom actions.\n  - The row target is the full row; the overflow is a separate 44pt / 48dp target, 8dp away.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - Notifications say \"marked paid\", not \"paid\".\n  - The attribution form is \"Paid by <first name> · <weekday day month>\".\n  - A former member reads \"Sam (no longer here)\".\n  - The list header names who can see the bills; never \"Everyone\" when finance access differs.\n  - Never write monitoring language such as \"still hasn't paid\".\n\nPLATFORMS (added by this board, not in the contract): the overflow uses the native menu: an iOS pull-down menu, an Android M3 DropdownMenu, and a web menu button with keyboard support. Draw all three in 04.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of a one-tap \"Mark paid\" on the row face or the dashboard, draw it inside the overflow menu. A mis-tap must not notify the whole household.\n  - Instead of an avatar without a name, draw \"Paid by Sam\". The name is the point.\n  - Instead of a budget meter or spend bar, draw the header sentence with the total.\n  - Instead of truncating the attribution, truncate the provider.\n\nUSED IN: f3-bills-list, f3-member-home-dashboard, f3-bill-detail-web, f10-mail-piece-photo.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops plus the platform strip:\n  (1) f3-bills-list, iOS, viewer Maya: the header ⑧ (\"… You and Sam can see these\") plus the four upcoming rows.\n  (2) f3-member-home-dashboard, Android, viewer Sam: a Bills card with the header \"… You and Maya can see these\" and two V2a rows.\n  (3) f3-bill-detail-web, web 1440: the row as the page header summary, reached from a notification, with its web menu button.\n  Platform strip: the V1 overflow menu drawn on iOS, Android and web.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nMemberRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. A person in the household. It carries no trust badge and no status badge.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Row of 56pt minimum, padding 16pt.\n② A 40pt initials avatar: a surface.sunken circle (dark: D4) with initials in label 13/18 text.strong. Neutral, with no identity hue (an assumption; list on Notes).\n③ Name in body 16/24 text.primary.\n④ Caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"joined Mon 12 Oct 2026\" or \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" (both dates invented).\n⑤ Overflow button (44pt / 48dp) with Change role · Confirm lives here · Remove. On the viewer's own row the only item is \"Leave Larkspur Loop\". On web this is the row menu button (1.14).\n⑥ Group heading in overline 11/16 text.secondary: OWNER · ADMINS · MEMBERS · GUESTS.\n⑦ Group disclosures, each a 44pt row under its heading: MEMBERS \"What can members do?\", ADMINS \"What can admins do?\", GUESTS \"What can guests do?\". OWNER has no disclosure.\n⑧ Optional second caption with method and date: \"Address confirmed by postcard · Thu 15 Oct 2026\" (date invented), in text.secondary with no badge shape. It appears only on the viewer's own row, never on another person's row, so household members never look different from one another. List this narrowing on Notes.\n\nVARIANTS (Home A, viewer Maya. Role variants reuse Sam Ortega so no new people are invented; code · slug):\n  V1 · owner: \"Maya Chen (you)\" (\"(you)\" suffix invented) · \"joined Mon 12 Oct 2026\" · ⑧ caption (Maya's own row).\n  V2 · admin: \"Sam Ortega\" under ADMINS (no ⑧).\n  V3 · member: \"Sam Ortega\" under MEMBERS · \"joined Tue 13 Oct 2026\" (invented) (no ⑧).\n  V4 · guest: \"Sam Ortega\" under GUESTS · \"access until Sun 1 Nov 2026\" (no ⑧).\n  V5 · you: Maya's own row, with the overflow open showing only \"Leave Larkspur Loop\".\n  V6a · roster-line (44pt): \"Maya and Sam live here · View\".\n  V6b · roster-count (Priya's view before acceptance, count only): \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\".\n  V7 · empty (44pt; Home A before Sam joined, fixture delta): \"Just you at Larkspur Loop · Invite someone\". \"Invite someone\" is a text button in primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus).\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · loading: a WarmingSkeleton with a 40pt circle and two bars at 56pt, no text, announced once as \"Loading\".\n  S3 · offline: the overflow is disabled per 1.8, with the reason \"You're offline. You can change roles when you're back.\" (invented).\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6a, V6b and V7 in S1 · V3 and V6a in S2 · V3 and V5 in S3 · V3 in SF.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V3 and V6a.\n  - The avatar stays 40pt, or scales to 48pt at most, top-aligned.\n  - Name and caption wrap.\n  - V6a splits \"View\" onto its own line.\n  - The overflow button stays top-trailing.\n\nGREYSCALE: role reads through the group heading words, never through colour.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - The avatar is decorative; the name is read.\n  - Pattern: \"Sam Ortega, member, joined Tuesday 13 October 2026. Actions available.\"\n  - The loading state is announced once as \"Loading\".\n  - The overflow items are also custom actions.\n  - Row and overflow targets are 44pt / 48dp.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - Verification is shown on actions, through LockedActionRow, and never on names.\n  - The only exception is ⑧ on the viewer's own row, which names the method and the date.\n  - Roles are Owner, Admin, Member, Guest. Never \"resident\".\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of a \"Verified\" or \"Household member\" chip, draw the plain ⑧ caption on the viewer's own row only. A badge on a person reads as a trust score.\n  - Instead of a check-badge shape on the avatar, draw the plain initials circle.\n  - Instead of listing names to someone who has not accepted, draw the count line \"Maya Chen and 1 other live here\".\n\nUSED IN: f3-members-roster, f3-member-home-dashboard, f3-household-block, f3b-owner-attestation, x-place-file, f3b-invitation-decision.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) f3-members-roster, iOS: OWNER (V1, no disclosure) and MEMBERS (V3, with its disclosure), then the PENDING group (InviteRow).\n  (2) f3-household-block, Android: V7 (Home A before Sam joined).\n  (3) f3b-invitation-decision, web 1440: V6b.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nInviteRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. A pending invitation or invite link, with its expiry and a one-tap fix.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Row of 56pt minimum, in a \"PENDING\" group (overline) that only managers see. It is drawn quieter than people: no avatar.\n② Leading mail glyph, 16pt, text.secondary.\n③ Recipient in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary: \"priya@example.com\", or a username in the form \"@priya\" (invented).\n④ Caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires Mon 26 Oct\" (sent date invented).\n⑤ Inline \"Resend\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus), with a 44pt target.\n⑥ Overflow button (44pt / 48dp) with Cancel · Extend. On web this is the row menu button (1.14).\n\nVARIANTS (code · slug):\n  V1 · pending-email: as in the anatomy.\n  V1u · pending-username: the same row with recipient \"@priya\" (invented).\n  V2 · expiring (fixture delta Sun 25 Oct): caption \"Member · sent Mon 12 Oct · Expires tomorrow\". The expiry is words in text.secondary, not tinted.\n  V3 · needs-reissue: a warning glyph (hue on the glyph only; dark: D7) and, in text.primary, \"Needs reissue — your household's invite rules changed · Reissue\".\n  V4 · declined (fixture delta: Priya declined): StatusChip \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\" (date invented). The overflow holds only \"Remove\". There is no Resend.\n  V5 · link-active: a link glyph, then \"Invite link · Works once · Expires Mon 26 Oct · Turn off link\" (expiry added; see Notes). \"Turn off link\" is a text button.\n  V6 · awaiting-approval (joined by link, so the link is used and no expiry applies): \"priya@example.com · Waiting for your OK\", with two equal-weight text buttons, \"Approve\" and \"Remove\", 8dp apart.\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default (the variants above).\n  S2 · sending: \"Resend\" becomes \"Sending…\" (invented) and \"Reissue\" becomes \"Reissuing…\" (invented), with a 12pt spinner (dark: D6; static text under Reduce Motion), then \"Sent\" (invented) as a role=status caption.\n  S3 · offline: each action is disabled per 1.8, with its own reason caption (all invented):\n    - Resend (V1): \"You're offline. You can resend when you're back.\"\n    - Reissue (V3): \"You're offline. You can reissue when you're back.\"\n    - Turn off link (V5): \"You're offline. You can turn off the link when you're back.\"\n    - Approve (V6): \"You're offline. You can approve when you're back.\"\n    - Remove (V4, V6): \"You're offline. You can remove this when you're back.\"\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1, V1u, V2, V3, V4, V5 and V6 in S1 · V1 and V3 in S2 · V1, V5 and V6 in S3 · V4 in S2: \"n/a — declined invites cannot be resent\" · V1 in SF, ring on Resend only.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V6. The recipient wraps at the \"@\". The caption wraps at middots. Resend drops below the caption. Approve and Remove stack, each at full width.\n\nGREYSCALE: expiry, reissue and declined each read through words and a glyph shape.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - Pattern: \"Invitation to priya@example.com, member, expires Monday 26 October. Resend. Button.\"\n  - Resend is announced as \"Invitation resent\".\n  - Expiry is always in words.\n  - Targets are 44pt / 48dp with 8dp gaps.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - The expiry is shown on every pending invite (email or username) and every active link. An awaiting-approval row shows none, because its link has already been used.\n  - The link warning (\"Works once\") appears at the point of choice.\n  - Every email uses @example.com.\n  - Each offline reason names the action it blocks.\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of a \"Remind them\" action on a declined invite, draw only \"Remove\". A decline is an answer.\n  - Instead of a real email domain, draw @example.com.\n  - Instead of a warning-tinted expiring row, draw \"Expires tomorrow\" in text.secondary words. Urgency comes from the date, not from colour.\n\nUSED IN: f3-members-roster, x-place-file, f3-invite-composer, f3-invite-banner.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) f3-members-roster, iOS: the PENDING group with V1 and V5.\n  (2) f3-invite-banner, Android: V3 as the banner's single slot.\n  (3) f3-invite-composer, web 1440: V5 under the link choice.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nNotificationRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. The in-app twin of every push. Tapping it lands on the exact object.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Row of 64pt minimum, padding 12pt vertical, 16pt trailing.\n② A fixed 12pt leading column holding a 6pt unread dot in primary.700 (dark: D6), with the accessibility label \"Unread\". Read rows keep the empty column, so the text never shifts. The dot is not a provenance mark and not a target.\n③ A 28pt initials avatar (surface.sunken, text.strong; dark: D4). System rows have no avatar and keep the text aligned.\n④ Line 1 in body 16/24 text.primary: a sentence with the actor first.\n⑤ Line 2 in caption text.secondary, joined by middots: the date and time · the home label (only for readers with more than one home) · for reminders, a trailing ProvenanceMark S.\n⑥ Grouped row: a chevron disclosure that expands to the individual rows.\n⑦ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (Home A, viewer Maya; times invented except 7:00 AM, the morning briefing time; code · slug). Each variant is an independent specimen; V1 shows Clark Public Utilities marked paid although BillRow shows it upcoming (fixture delta).\n  V1 · bill-paid: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked Clark Public Utilities paid · $142.18\" · \"Today · 5:40 PM\".\n  V2 · task-completed: Sam avatar · \"Sam marked \"Carts out\" done\" (task invented) · \"Today · 5:55 PM\".\n  V3 · event-created: Sam avatar · \"Sam added a date: HOA dues, Sun 1 Nov\" · \"Yesterday · 8:12 PM\".\n  V4 · date-reminder (system): \"Online or mail voter registration must arrive by Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Today · 7:00 AM\" · filled mark.\n  V5 · bill-reminder (system): \"Clark Public Utilities is due in 4 days · Fri 23 Oct · $142.18\" · \"Today · 7:00 AM\" · YOU ADDED mark (assumption: household bills are entered by the household; list on Notes).\n  V6j · member-joined (fixture delta: Priya has accepted, a future state): Priya avatar · \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills\" (invented).\n  V6l · member-left: Sam avatar · \"Sam left Larkspur Loop\" (invented).\n  V7 · grouped: \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\", with a chevron, expanded below into 3 V1-style rows.\n  V8 · gone-target: the landing after tapping a removed bill, a plain body line \"That bill was removed.\" in the bill's slot, with the notifications list still reachable through Back.\n  V9 · multi-home (fixture delta: Maya with a second home): V1 with line 2 \"Today · 5:40 PM · Larkspur Loop\".\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · unread (dot present).\n  S2 · read (no dot; identical weight and fill).\n  S3 · push-off: a 44pt banner row at the top of the list: \"Push is off. You'll still see these here. · Turn on\" in bodySmall text.strong on surface.sunken (dark: D3).\n  S4 · offline: FreshnessLine \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\" above the list. Rows stay readable. Tapping a row whose object is not cached shows the reason \"You're offline. This opens when you're back.\" (invented).\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1, V2, V3, V4, V5, V6j, V6l and V7 in S1 and S2 · V9 in S1 · V8 as one cell (column S1) · S3 above a V1 row (one cell) · S4 above V1 and V4 (one cell) · V1 in SF.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V7. The sentence wraps fully. Line 2 wraps at middots. The dot column stays 12pt, top-aligned with line 1. The avatar stays 28pt.\n\nGREYSCALE: unread reads through the dot's presence. Draw one extra greyscale cell showing that unread and read rows differ only by the dot, and add the caption \"unread is also spoken first\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - The label is merged, with \"Unread\" first: \"Unread. Sam marked Clark Public Utilities paid, 142 dollars 18 cents. Today, 5:40 PM.\"\n  - Reminder rows end with the mark name: \"…Today, 7:00 AM, official.\"\n  - The row is the target and lands on the exact object.\n  - The grouped row reads \"Sam marked 3 bills paid, collapsed, button\".\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - Amounts appear in-app only, never in pushes.\n  - Use \"marked paid\", not \"paid\"; the grouped row reads \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" (see Notes 3).\n  - The actor comes first.\n  - A landing whose object no longer exists says \"That bill was removed.\"\n\nPLATFORMS: default (1.14).\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of bold text or a tinted background for unread rows, draw the 6pt dot plus the spoken \"Unread\". Weight and tint changes make read rows look disabled.\n  - Instead of landing on a generic list when the object exists, land on the object: the bill row highlighted (BillRow S2a).\n  - Instead of an avatar on system rows, leave the avatar slot empty and keep the text aligned.\n\nUSED IN: f3-household-notifications, f4-notification-settings.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), two crops:\n  (1) f3-household-notifications, iOS, Home A: ScopeChip \"Your household\", the S3 banner, then V1 (unread), V4 (unread) and V3 (read), and the legend line.\n  (2) f4-notification-settings, web 1440: the \"Household activity\" group with a sample V1 row.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nTextActionRow\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. Tertiary actions that spread the product (share, compare, outbound links). They never outrank the primary action.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Two text buttons side by side: \"Share this address\" and \"Compare with a friend\". Each is in bodySmallMedium primary.700 (dark: dark border.focus) with a 44pt / 48dp target, 8dp apart, with no fill and no border.\n② Caption under the buttons in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"The card shows your city and your readings — never your address, and no name.\" (invented).\n③ Outbound variant: a bordered row, 48pt minimum, radius md 8, with a 1px text.secondary edge (at least 3:1). It holds the destination name in bodySmall text.primary and a trailing 16pt external-link glyph \"↗\".\n④ Web menu callout: \"no custom actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (code · slug):\n  V1 · share-compare (① + ②).\n  V2a · outbound-test-kits: \"Free test kits · Washington Dept of Health ↗\"\n  V2b · outbound-votewa: \"Check or update at VoteWA ↗\"\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · idle.\n  S2 · minting: on \"Compare with a friend\", a 12pt spinner (dark: D6) replaces the start of the label, and the label reads \"Making a link…\" (invented). The button is not re-tappable. Under Reduce Motion the spinner is removed and \"Making a link…\" stays.\n  S3 · copied: a caption \"Link copied\" (invented) with role=status appears under the pair and stays until the user leaves.\n  S4 · cancelled: nothing changes. Draw the idle row again with the annotation \"share sheet dismissed: neutral, no message\".\n  S5 · offline: \"Compare with a friend\" is disabled per 1.8, with the reason \"You're offline. Compare needs a connection.\" Outbound rows are disabled (text.secondary name and glyph), with the reason \"You're offline. You can open this when you're back.\" (invented).\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1 in S1–S5 · V2a and V2b in S1 and S5 · V2a and V2b in S2, S3 and S4: \"n/a — outbound links open the browser\" · V2b in SF.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 and V2b. The two buttons stack vertically, each full width with its own target. The caption wraps. The outbound row wraps the destination name, and the glyph stays trailing, top-aligned.\n\nGREYSCALE: the buttons read as actions through their verbs and position. The outbound row reads through its text.secondary edge, the destination name, the verb and the ↗ glyph.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - Links name their destination: \"Check or update at VoteWA, opens in browser\".\n  - \"Link copied\" is a status message.\n  - Targets are 44pt / 48dp / 44px, with 8dp between the two buttons.\n\nCOPY RULES:\n  - Buttons start with a verb.\n  - The caption states what the card reveals.\n  - Use \"Compare with a friend\", never \"challenge\" or \"vs\".\n  - Offline reasons open with \"You're offline\".\n\nPLATFORMS:\n  - Only the system share sheet is used. iOS supplies LPLinkMetadata; Android supplies EXTRA_TITLE to the system chooser; web uses the browser's share, falling back to copying the link (S3).\n  - In 04, draw the iOS share sheet header and the Android system chooser header as plain grey frames labelled \"system UI\", not redrawn by us.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of placing these actions inside the sticky WallBar, draw them on the page surface under the content card. The wall's single primary action must stay single.\n  - Instead of an app-drawn Android chooser, draw the system chooser frame.\n  - Instead of filled or bordered buttons for share and compare, draw text buttons, so they never outrank the primary.\n\nUSED IN: f8-native-share-compare, f8-compare-sheet, f8-seasonal-aha, f6-place-section-details, f8-compare-reveal.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops plus the platform strip:\n  (1) f8-native-share-compare, iOS: V1 under a seasonal card outline.\n  (2) f6-place-section-details, Android: V2a under a radon row (if the radon row shows a mark, add the legend line and ScopeChip per 1.15).\n  (3) f8-seasonal-aha, web 390: V2b.\n  Platform strip: the iOS and Android system share frames.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nThumbnailRail\n------------------------------------------------------------------\nPURPOSE. The optional leading photo slot on mail rows and in the capture queue.\n\nANATOMY (01-anatomy callouts):\n① Thumbnail sizes, all radius md 8:\n  - triage: 56×56pt;\n  - drawer: 40×52pt;\n  - privacy list: 32×32pt.\n② Photo content is a neutral envelope on a grey table, with no legible name, address or amount.\n③ When there is no photo, the rail collapses: the text moves to the leading margin, with no empty square.\n④ Upload: a determinate ring inside the thumbnail, 2pt stroke, primary.700 on a border.strong track (dark: D6), plus a text value beside the row, \"Uploading 2 of 3\" (invented). This is transfer progress, not a score, and it never carries a percentage.\n⑤ Failed: a 16pt retry glyph centred on a surface.sunken thumbnail (dark: D4), plus the row caption \"Upload failed · Retry\" (this is InlineErrorRow V3).\n⑥ Deleted: a quiet 16pt document glyph on surface.sunken (dark: D4), plus the words \"photo deleted Mon 12 Oct\" (date invented) in caption text.secondary.\n⑦ Selected thumbnail: a primary.50 fill behind the row plus a check glyph (dark: D5). Below it appears a visible action row of three 44pt text buttons, 8dp apart: \"Retake\" · \"Delete\" · \"Same letter as previous\".\n⑧ Web menu callout: \"the visible action row holds the actions; no row menu button\".\n\nVARIANTS (mail fixtures: Clark Public Utilities, Comcast; code · slug):\n  V1 · triage (56pt): thumbnail · \"Clark Public Utilities\" · \"Bill · $142.18\".\n  V2 · drawer (40×52): thumbnail · \"Comcast\".\n  V3 · privacy (32pt): thumbnail · \"Photo of your mail · Mon 19 Oct\" (invented).\n  V4 · queue: two joined pieces drawn as a stacked thumbnail (two offset 56pt rectangles) plus the label \"2 pages\".\n  V5 · no-photo: V1 with the rail collapsed.\n\nSTATES (code · slug):\n  S1 · default.\n  S2 · uploading: the ring plus \"Uploading 2 of 3\".\n  S3 · failed.\n  S4 · deleted.\n  S5 · offline: the thumbnail is a surface.sunken slot (dark: D4) with a cloud-off glyph, and the caption \"You're offline. This photo isn't saved on this device.\" (invented).\n  SX · selected (⑦).\n  SF · focused.\n\nGRID CELLS: V1 in S1–S5 · V2 in S1, S2 and S4 · V3 in S1 and S4 · V4 in S1 and S2 · V5 in S1 · V1 in SX (with the action row) beside V1 in SF.\n\nAX5 / 200% (03): draw V1 in S2 and V1 in SX.\n  - The thumbnail stays 56pt, top-aligned.\n  - The progress text wraps below the title.\n  - The action row stacks: three full-width 44pt / 48dp buttons.\n\nGREYSCALE: upload reads through the ring plus the words. Failed reads through the retry glyph plus the words. Selected reads through the check glyph plus the visible action row.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - The thumbnail is part of the row element: \"Clark Public Utilities, bill, photo, uploading 2 of 3\".\n  - Retake, Delete and Same letter as previous are visible buttons and also custom actions.\n  - No action is long-press-only or hover-only.\n  - Upload progress is a polite status (live region).\n\nCOPY RULES: the contract lists none. Use \"Photo of your mail\", never \"scan\" or \"document\", for the stored image. Upload progress reads \"Uploading 2 of 3\", with no percentage.\n\nPLATFORMS: web converts HEIC to JPEG before rendering; add a callout on the web crop. iOS and Android render natively.\n\nINSTEAD OF:\n  - Instead of a broken-image icon, draw the ⑥ deleted glyph with words, or the ⑤ retry glyph.\n  - Instead of placing the progress ring under or near the Delete target, keep the ring inside the thumbnail and the action row separate, so a tap meant for Delete never lands on progress.\n  - Instead of an empty square when there is no photo, collapse the rail.\n  - Instead of a percentage beside the ring, draw \"Uploading 2 of 3\". Percentages are banned by house invariant 6.\n\nUSED IN: f10-mail-day-triage, f10-snap-capture-tray, f10-mail-piece-photo, f10-mail-snap-privacy, f10-bill-provenance.\n\nIN CONTEXT (04), three crops:\n  (1) f10-mail-day-triage, iOS: V1, V5, then V1 selected with the action row.\n  (2) f10-snap-capture-tray, Android: V4 and V1 in S2.\n  (3) f10-mail-snap-privacy, web 1440: V3 rows, including one deleted, with the HEIC callout.\n\n==================================================================\nPART 3 — NOTES ARTBOARD (\"00c · Notes\")\n==================================================================\nList these, plus anything else you assumed. Keep items 2 and 3 to one line each.\n  1. Every string marked \"(invented)\" in this prompt, and any string you added. These include: \"What you get now\", \"What needs address verification\", \"What you get once Maya confirms you live here\", \"What members can do\", \"What guests can do\", \"Next: put today on your home screen →\", \"Hidden from Today · Undo\", the TextActionRow caption, \"Making a link…\", \"Link copied\", the FactRow V6 reason, \"Pickup day set · Tuesday\", \"Skipped\", \"2 dates and your pickup day\", the three V8 report strings, the ThumbnailRail S5 caption, \"Uploading 2 of 3\", \"Photo of your mail · Mon 19 Oct\", \"photo deleted Mon 12 Oct\", \"Retrying…\", \"Retry moving your water-heater warranty\", \"Retry upload\", \"Retry saving pickup day\", \"Your choice is still here.\", \"Sending…\", \"Reissuing…\", \"Sent\", \"@priya\", \"Declined · Thu 15 Oct\", \"Expires Mon 26 Oct\" on the link row, the five InviteRow offline reasons, \"Address verification needed to earn a Block Founder rank\", \"We checked again.\", \"We're checking your postcard code — expected Thu 22–Thu 29 Oct\", \"Maya can mark this paid\", \"Maya can give you access to bills\", \"Next due Mon 23 Nov\", \"You're offline · as of 5:52 PM\", every other offline reason, \"Reminder:\" (DateRow V5 prefix), \"city schedule\", \"Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027\", \"Every year\" / \"Every month\" / \"Does not repeat\", \"Washington Secretary of State · statewide\", \"Maya Chen (you)\", \"Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills\", \"Sam left Larkspur Loop\", \"Carts out\", and the NotificationRow offline reason.\n  2. Fixture deltas:\n     - FirstWeekRow on Tue 13 Oct, 3 days after the Sat 10 Oct save; the window runs Sun 11 Oct through Sat 17 Oct.\n     - Home A pickup: as of TODAY it is on record, not confirmed (DateRow V1a, V1b; FactRow V1b, hollow). FactRow V1d and V4 show the later state after Maya confirmed Tuesday (filled).\n     - FactRow V1c belongs to Place B (Thursday · City of Camas).\n     - DateRow V5x: the water-heater warranty date entered as approximate (\"about Dec 2026\") instead of the fixture's Sat 12 Dec 2026.\n     - InviteRow V2 on Sun 25 Oct; InviteRow V4 shows Priya's invite declined.\n     - BillRow \"Due today\" on Fri 23 Oct.\n     - BillRow S4 and LockedActionRow crop (2): Sam before Maya shared bills.\n     - LockedActionRow V4: Sam's postcard still pending; Maya's address is already confirmed (MemberRow ⑧).\n     - HOA dues appears both as a household bill (BillRow) and as a self-added monthly date (DateRow V6).\n     - FactRow V5 and MemberRow V7 show Home A before Sam joined.\n     - NotificationRow V1 shows Clark Public Utilities marked paid, while BillRow shows it upcoming.\n     - NotificationRow V6j shows Priya joined, although the fixture has her pending.\n     - NotificationRow V9 shows Maya with a second home.\n  3. Contract conflicts (one line each, \"drawn as X instead of contract Y\"):\n     (a) FirstWeekRow: contract lists a \"fraction\" variant (\"1 of 4 done — next: …\"); not drawn, because house invariant 6 and the research brief rejected it.\n     (b) DateRow: \"Statewide — WA\" drawn in ScopeChip geometry as a coverage chip, instead of one of ScopeChip's two exact strings.\n     (c) NotificationRow: grouped row drawn as \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" instead of contract \"Sam paid 3 bills\".\n     (d) NotificationRow: \"Push is off…\" drawn as specified, although the glossary limits \"push\" to technical settings copy.\n     (e) LockedActionRow: \"Verify address\" / \"Verify your address\" drawn instead of the glossary's \"Verify this address\".\n     (f) InlineErrorRow: \"water-heater warranty\" drawn instead of contract \"furnace warranty\", to match the fixture.\n     (g) GrantLimitList: the Guest capability caption and the attestation grant rows are assumed; the contract does not give them.\n     (h) DateRow V2: hollow mark on an official city holiday move, assumed because Place B's schedule is unconfirmed.\n     (i) ThumbnailRail: contract lists \"2 of 3 uploaded, 40%\"; not drawn, because house invariant 6 and the research brief rejected percentages. Drawn as \"Uploading 2 of 3\" with a determinate ring.\n     (j) MemberRow ⑧: verification caption drawn on the viewer's own row only, instead of never (contract \"never on names\").\n     (k) ChoiceChip unselected: drawn with a text.secondary edge instead of contract border.strong (house style forbids a border token as an input's only edge).\n     (l) TextActionRow outbound row: drawn with a text.secondary edge instead of a border token, for the same reason.\n     (m) BillRow V3: drawn with ScopeChip's approved sentence \"Only you will see this.\", one of several scope wordings the contract lists.\n     (n) NotificationRow V5: drawn with a YOU ADDED mark (assumed: household bills are entered by the household); the contract requires a mark but does not say which.\n     (o) BillRow header: drawn as \"… You and Sam can see these\" instead of contract \"… Everyone at Maple St can see these\", because finance access differs and ScopeChip's doNot requires naming the people.\n     (p) BillRow platform notes (native overflow menus): added by this board; the contract has none.\n     (q) InviteRow V6: \"Approve\" drawn as specified, although the glossary lists \"approve member\" under Not for confirming a person.\n     (r) ThumbnailRail / InlineErrorRow V3: \"Upload failed\" and \"Uploading 2 of 3\" drawn as specified, although the glossary lists \"upload\" under Not for mail photos.\n     (s) FactRow V3 and LockedActionRow V7: \"Claim this address first\" (a contract string) drawn on Place B rows, although ScopeChip's copy rule says a saved place never uses the word \"claim\".\n     (t) LockedActionRow V5: drawn as \"Address verification needed to get a residency letter. We checked again.\" instead of a generic server-refusal notice, to keep the contract pattern.\n     (u) InviteRow: expiry drawn on pending invites and the active link, and omitted on the awaiting-approval row, narrowing \"the expiry is always shown\".\n  4. Dark-mode substitutes D1–D8 from 1.6, each with where it was used, the 3:1 checks for D7 and D8, and the Increase Contrast note.\n  5. The neutral avatar colour.\n  6. Any state you could not draw, and why.\n\n==================================================================\nDONE WHEN\n==================================================================\n- All 61 artboards in the manifest exist, named exactly, each with its visible label.\n- Every grid row and column is labelled \"<code> · <slug>\" and every cell carries the caption \"<Component> · <variant slug> · <state slug>\" (1.5).\n- Every component shows every variant and state listed above; n/a cells appear only where this prompt writes them, each with its reason (1.5).\n- Every 01-anatomy meets 1.2 and 1.4: callouts with size and token for each part, the web menu callout, plus the five panels.\n- Every 03 artboard meets 1.2, 1.9 and 1.10 (the BillRow provider truncates at default sizes only).\n- Every 04 artboard meets 1.15: crops that show marks carry the legend line and the ScopeChip; web crops show the row menu button where 1.14 requires it.\n- Every 05 artboard uses only the dark tokens and substitutes D1–D8 in 1.6, and no sunken shape or card edge disappears.\n- Colour, targets, focus, highlight, selection and disabled actions follow 1.6 and 1.8: no hex on a component, no text.muted anywhere on this board, disabled text actions in text.secondary with a reason caption, no semantic hue on text, no border token as a meaningful edge, and highlight (leading bar), focus (outer ring) and selection (fill plus check) each look different.\n- Marks follow 1.12: 12pt or larger, stroke 1.5px or more, never a target by itself.\n- Copy follows 1.13: every string comes from this prompt or is listed on Notes; every email uses @example.com; no percentage or completion fraction appears anywhere on the board.\n- Undo follows 1.12: role=status, no countdown anywhere.\n\n==================================================================\nARTBOARDS (exact names, in delivery order)\n==================================================================\n00c · DateRow · 01-anatomy · light — 2x specimen with callouts (including the web row menu button), a11y, copy, platforms, INSTEAD OF, used-in panels.\n00c · DateRow · 02-grid · light — pickup-both … money × default/highlighted-arrival/highlighted-decayed/done/permission-hidden/focused.\n00c · DateRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V3a and V6 at iOS AX5 and Android 200%, greyscale grid below.\n00c · DateRow · 04-in-context · light — f5-today-calendar-strip, x-place-file and f3-household-calendar crops, each with legend and scope chip.\n00c · DateRow · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · FactRow · 01-anatomy · light — specimen with callouts, including the target rule and the \"More you can add (5)\" disclosure, and panels.\n00c · FactRow · 02-grid · light — known (flood, pickup unconfirmed/confirmed, Place B)/missing/not-at-tier/done/declined/permission-disabled/receipt/reports × default/loading/offline/focused.\n00c · FactRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1a and V2a at large text, greyscale grid below.\n00c · FactRow · 04-in-context · light — x-place-file (Place B), f4-notification-settings and f6-home-basics-rows crops.\n00c · FactRow · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · LockedActionRow · 01-anatomy · light — specimen under a disabled CTA, with callouts and panels.\n00c · LockedActionRow · 02-grid · light — under-cta/list-row (sunken, base)/card-header/pending/server-refused/names-who-can-act/not-at-tier × locked/pending/offline/focused, with n/a reasons.\n00c · LockedActionRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1 and V2b at large text, greyscale grid below.\n00c · LockedActionRow · 04-in-context · light — f3-member-home-dashboard, f3-bills-list and f9-block-founders-panel crops.\n00c · LockedActionRow · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · InlineErrorRow · 01-anatomy · light — specimen with callouts and panels.\n00c · InlineErrorRow · 02-grid · light — provider-unreachable/carry-failed/upload-failed/save-failed/fail-closed × failed/retrying/focused.\n00c · InlineErrorRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1 and V4 at large text, greyscale grid below.\n00c · InlineErrorRow · 04-in-context · light — f1-today-tab, f10-snap-capture-tray and f6-home-basics-rows crops.\n00c · InlineErrorRow · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · GrantLimitList · 01-anatomy · light — stacked iOS specimen at 2x and two-column web specimen at 1x, string set, callouts and panels.\n00c · GrantLimitList · 02-grid · light — invitation-decision/role-offered/attestation/verify-unlock/role-caption (member, guest) × default/accepted, focused and selected cells.\n00c · GrantLimitList · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1 stacked at large text, greyscale grid below.\n00c · GrantLimitList · 04-in-context · light — f3b-invitation-decision, f3b-verify-address-sheet and f3-invite-composer crops.\n00c · GrantLimitList · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · FirstWeekRow · 01-anatomy · light — the 48pt row with dismiss, the bounded-set callouts and panels.\n00c · FirstWeekRow · 02-grid · light — next-pickup/next-widget/hidden × default/dismissed, plus focused-link and focused-dismiss cells.\n00c · FirstWeekRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1a and the dismissed state at lar