ight — unread column, avatar and two-line callouts, panels.\n00c · NotificationRow · 02-grid · light — bill-paid … gone-target and multi-home × unread/read, plus the push-off, offline and focused cells.\n00c · NotificationRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1 and V7 at large text, greyscale grid below with the unread-dot cell.\n00c · NotificationRow · 04-in-context · light — f3-household-notifications and f4-notification-settings crops.\n00c · NotificationRow · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · TextActionRow · 01-anatomy · light — text-button pair, caption and outbound row callouts, panels.\n00c · TextActionRow · 02-grid · light — share-compare/outbound-test-kits/outbound-votewa × idle/minting/copied/cancelled/offline/focused.\n00c · TextActionRow · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — stacked pair and outbound row at large text, greyscale grid below.\n00c · TextActionRow · 04-in-context · light — f8-native-share-compare, f6-place-section-details and f8-seasonal-aha crops, plus the system share frames.\n00c · TextActionRow · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · ThumbnailRail · 01-anatomy · light — three thumbnail sizes, collapse, ring with \"Uploading 2 of 3\", failed, deleted and selected-action-row callouts, panels.\n00c · ThumbnailRail · 02-grid · light — triage/drawer/privacy/queue/no-photo × default/uploading/failed/deleted/offline, plus selected and focused.\n00c · ThumbnailRail · 03-ax5-200-greyscale · light — V1 uploading and selected at large text, greyscale grid below.\n00c · ThumbnailRail · 04-in-context · light — f10-mail-day-triage, f10-snap-capture-tray and f10-mail-snap-privacy crops.\n00c · ThumbnailRail · 05-grid · dark — the same grid and the 1x anatomy in dark tokens.\n00c · Notes — invented strings, fixture deltas, contract conflicts, dark substitutes D1–D8, omissions.\n\n==================================================================\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn; wait for \"continue\" after each turn)\n==================================================================\nTurn 1: DateRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 2: FactRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 3: LockedActionRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 4: InlineErrorRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 5: GrantLimitList 01–05 (5).\nTurn 6: FirstWeekRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 7: BillRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 8: MemberRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 9: InviteRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 10: NotificationRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 11: TextActionRow 01–05 (5).\nTurn 12: ThumbnailRail 01–05 and 00c · Notes (6).\nKeep the Notes list as you go and deliver it in Turn 12. Ask a question only if two readings would produce materially different components.\n\n==================================================================\nPUBLISH\n==================================================================\nWhen I accept a component, add it to the Pantopus design system under this exact name. Use the names DateRow, FactRow, FirstWeekRow, BillRow, MemberRow, InviteRow, NotificationRow, TextActionRow, LockedActionRow, GrantLimitList, InlineErrorRow and ThumbnailRail. Name each variant and state with the slugs used in the grid labels on this board (e.g. DateRow variant \"deadline-voter\", state \"highlighted-arrival\"). Do not publish the \"stand-in\" drawings from 1.12 under their names. Those components are published from their own Foundations boards."
