                  "issue": "Some invented strings are not marked '(invented)', so they may never reach the Notes list.",
                  "evidence": "'Sending…', 'Reissuing…', 'Retrying…', 'Sent', 'Making a link…' (marked in one place only), the 'Reminder:' prefix, 'city schedule', 'Reminder Mon 15 Feb 2027', and 'Priya joined Larkspur Loop — can see the calendar and bills'.",
                  "fix": "Mark each one '(invented)', or add them by name to Notes item 1."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "Asides about where material came from add length and point to documents Claude Design cannot see. The Notes list also repeats reasons already given in the body, which gives the model a second copy to reconcile.",
                  "evidence": "Examples: '(invented; taken from the v1 f4-notification-settings prompt)', 'the research brief (P5, section 2.5)', 'which the contract's inconsistency list names as one of five scope wordings', and Notes 3(k): 'so the rule holds without narrowing'.",
                  "fix": "Drop the 'taken from v1 …' and brief or contract citations from the body. Keep Notes item 3 as a one-line-per-item list in the form 'drawn as X instead of contract Y'. Drop 3(k), because it is not a conflict."
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "BillRow's PLATFORMS line adds platform notes the contract does not have, while 1.14 describes the default as what the contract says.",
                  "evidence": "The contract's BillRow platformNotes is '—'. The prompt's PLATFORMS line says 'the overflow uses the native menu … Draw all three in 05'.",
                  "fix": "Keep the platform notes, and add a Notes 3 item: 'BillRow platform notes added (native overflow menus); the contract has none.'"
                },
                {
                  "severity": "minor",
                  "issue": "The delivery order puts dark (03) before AX5/greyscale (04), which reverses the house style's priority. A fallback rule has to paper over the difference.",
                  "evidence": "The house style's ARTBOARDS priority: '… then AX5/200% and greyscale, then the dark twins'. The prompt's 'Order note' fallback: 'finish in this priority: 01, 02, 04, 05, then 03'.",
                  "fix": "Renumber so the order matches the priority: 03-ax5-200-greyscale, 04-in-context, 05-grid · dark. Update 1.2, the manifest and DONE WHEN, and delete the order note."
                }
