      {
        "prompt": {
          "id": "00d",
          "name": "Foundations: States, feedback and asks",
          "componentsCovered": [
            "QuietDayReceipt",
            "WarmingSkeleton",
            "InlineUndo",
            "DestructiveConfirm",
            "LandingBannerSlot",
            "NotificationAsk",
            "PushCopy",
            "ReminderLeadControl"
          ],
          "artboardCount": 44,
          "promptText": "Use the Pantopus house style pasted above. This project is the Foundations board: States, feedback and asks.\n\nTYPE: NEW (a component specimen board). This project draws no screens. It draws eight components as specimens: QuietDayReceipt, WarmingSkeleton, InlineUndo, DestructiveConfirm, LandingBannerSlot, NotificationAsk, PushCopy and ReminderLeadControl. Later projects (59 surfaces, each in a separate project with no shared memory) will use these components by exact name. When the founder accepts a component, it is published into the Pantopus design system. What you draw here is exactly what every later screen will get, so every size, token, string and state below is literal.\n\nATTACH:\n1. A screenshot of the shipped mailbox-arrival pill at the top of the Place tab (iOS, Android and web-390). LandingBannerSlot copies its geometry exactly. If this screenshot is missing, use the fallback geometry given under LandingBannerSlot and list \"mailbox-arrival pill screenshot missing; fallback geometry used\" on 00d · Notes.\n2. Optional, reference only: docs/screenshots/hub-v2-skeleton-ios.png, hub-v2-skeleton-android.png and hub-v2-skeleton-web.png (the existing shimmer tone). Treat these three as tone references and nothing more. Their layout is not a spec.\nNo other component on this board exists in the shipped app, so nothing else is attached.\n\nWHY THIS BOARD EXISTS. These eight components cover the moments when the product has to be honest about time and consent: nothing is wrong (QuietDayReceipt), something is still loading (WarmingSkeleton), something can be taken back (InlineUndo), something can't be taken back (DestructiveConfirm), something is waiting for you (LandingBannerSlot), the product wants to interrupt you (NotificationAsk, PushCopy), and the product will interrupt you on dates you chose (ReminderLeadControl). Each has a quiet default and none of them nags.\n\n====================================================================\nBOARD CONVENTIONS (these apply to all 44 artboards in this project)\n====================================================================\nC1. Canvas and names. Each artboard is a 1600px-wide spec board on surface.app (dark twins: dark app), with height as needed. Above each frame, print the artboard name exactly as the ARTBOARDS manifest gives it, in label 13/18 text.strong. Name format: \"00d · <ComponentName> · <NN-what> · <light|dark>\". This board's name format replaces the house-style artboard format (\"<surface-id> · <platform> · <NN-state> · <light|dark>\"); the platform goes in each specimen's C13 name instead. The Notes artboard is named exactly \"00d · Notes\", with no light/dark suffix.\nC2. Specimens are drawn at 1x at their real platform width: iOS 393pt, Android 412dp, web-390 390px, web-1440 1440px (crop web-1440 to the relevant column and label the crop \"web-1440 crop\"). Print the platform tag (ios / android / web-390 / web-1440) under each specimen in caption 12/16 text.secondary.\nC3. Callouts. Draw callouts as numbered markers: 16pt squares with radius xs, a text.strong 1px outline and a caption numeral. Connect each marker to its part with a 1px text.secondary leader line. The key sits beside the specimen: \"1 · 16pt tick glyph · text.secondary\". Callout markers are always squares, never circles, so they can't be mistaken for provenance marks. Dimension rulers are 1px text.secondary with caption numbers (for example \"44pt\").\nC4. Grids. Each \"variants × states\" artboard is a table. Rows are variants and columns are states. Headers are label 13/18/600 text.strong in sentence case, written as C13 gives them. Each cell holds one specimen. If a combination doesn't apply, the cell shows the caption \"Not applicable: <reason in one clause>\" on surface.sunken in text.strong. Every \"Not applicable\" on this board carries its reason; never leave a cell blank and never print a bare \"Not applicable\".\nC5. Dark tokens and the contrast table. Dark twins redraw their grid with the house-style dark tokens, plus these dark tokens the house style doesn't list: dark text.strong #F1F5F9, dark text.muted #64748B (disabled controls only), dark text.inverse #111827, dark border.strong #374151. Dark surface.sunken equals dark base, so it can't separate anything. In dark mode a card's edge comes from the fill step (dark raised on dark app), not from border.default. Dark cards have no shadow. Each dark grid below names its container surface.\nThis is the only contrast table on the board. Every section refers to it as \"(C5)\"; print the matching figure beside the part on the board.\n  Light, on surface.base: text.secondary 4.83:1 · semantic.error 4.83:1 (glyphs and borders only) · primary.700 5.93:1, and text.inverse on a primary.700 fill 5.93:1 · semantic.warning 3.19:1 (glyphs only) · text.muted 2.54:1 (disabled labels only, never readable text).\n  Dark, on dark raised #1E293B: dark text.secondary #94A3B8 5.71:1 · link #38BDF8 6.83:1 · semantic.error #DC2626 3.03:1 (glyphs only) · semantic.warning #D97706 4.59:1 (glyphs only) · dark border.default 1.00:1 (never an edge).\n  Dark, on dark base #0F172A: #94A3B8 6.96:1 · semantic.error #DC2626 3.70:1 (glyphs and borders only) · dark text.inverse #111827 on a #38BDF8 fill 8.28:1.\nC6. Every \"ax5-200-greyscale\" artboard has three required columns: (a) iOS at AX5 (body 53pt), (b) Android at 200% font scale with Android 14 non-linear scaling (body 16sp renders at about 28sp; caption 12sp renders at 24sp), (c) a greyscale copy (100% desaturated) of the light default and of the most state-heavy light cell, captioned with what still tells the states apart (a word, a glyph shape, a weight). Any extra frames a section lists for this artboard go in a labelled row below the three columns. At AX5 and 200%, pairs stack, text wraps instead of truncating, sheets may scroll, and no string ever ends in an ellipsis unless this prompt says it does (only PushCopy's collapsed tray does).\nC7. Every \"in-context-and-rules\" artboard has five panels in this order: IN CONTEXT (two or three mini crops, each 393pt wide for iOS or 390px wide for web-390, cropped to about 300pt tall, each labelled with its consuming surface id and captioned \"host illustrative, not a spec\" in caption text.secondary; under the crops, one line \"Also consumed by: <ids>\" listing the rest of the component's consumers), ACCESSIBILITY (spoken label pattern, non-colour encoding, target rule), COPY (the rule plus real strings), PLATFORMS (iOS vs Android vs web), INSTEAD OF (each line reads \"Instead of X, draw Y — because Z\", with a tiny struck-through thumbnail of X beside a thumbnail of Y). Label the struck-through X thumbnails \"Not this\" in caption text.strong, so they are never read as a spec.\nC8. Targets on every specimen. Draw the hit area of every control as a dashed 1px text.secondary rectangle with its size: 44×44pt on iOS, 48×48dp on Android with 8dp gaps, 44×44px on web. A small glyph is never a target by itself; its row or button is.\nC9. Focus vs selection. Wherever a focus state is drawn, focus is a 2px border.focus ring (dark #38BDF8) with a 2px offset. Selection is always the same treatment on this board: primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, a 16pt check glyph in primary.700 and a 600-weight label in text.primary (dark: dark raised fill, 1.5px #38BDF8 border, #38BDF8 check, dark text primary label). Never draw focus and selection with the same treatment. The only other fill-and-border treatment on this board is ReminderLeadControl's chosen-then-passed segment, defined in its PASSED-LEAD RULE; it has no check.\nC10. Glyphs. Use the existing Pantopus icon set only, at 16pt unless stated otherwise, with a 1.5px stroke. The tick used in receipts and chips is a plain check stroke, never a filled or hollow circle, because filled vs hollow means provenance and nothing else. No control on this board uses a radio circle.\nC11. Every string on this board comes from this prompt. Any string you have to add goes on 00d · Notes.\nC12. Contrast values printed on the board are the ones in the C5 table. Don't invent new ratios.\nC13. Specimen names. Print under every specimen, in caption text.strong, its published name: \"<Component> / <variant name in lower case> / <state name in lower case> / <platform>\", for example \"InlineUndo / removed row / pending undo / ios\". Grid row headers read \"V1 · Removed row\" and column headers read \"S1 · Pending undo\". The same rule applies to specimens outside grids. Where a section lists exact names, use those. Where a specimen has no state column, use its drawn state name (for example \"NotificationAsk / primer ios / never asked / ios\").\nC14. Components from other Foundations boards. Use FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, KindGlyph, AqiBand, ScaleStrip, PickupCard and MemberRow from the published Pantopus design system. If one is not published yet, draw a labelled box at the size below in surface.sunken with the component name in caption text.strong, and list it on 00d · Notes. Fallback sizes: FourteenDayStrip 361×40pt · YearBand 361×120pt with four 24pt lanes · AqiBand 361×48pt · ScaleStrip row 361×48pt · PickupCard 361×196pt · MemberRow 361×56pt · KindGlyph a 16pt or 42pt square as stated. The same fallback applies to the Pantopus app icon (a 20pt box labelled \"Pantopus app icon\"). Host screens in IN CONTEXT crops that haven't been drawn yet are drawn only as far as the crop needs, and captioned per C7.\nC15. Disabled controls. Every disabled control on this board stays focusable and reads its reason aloud (\"<label>, unavailable, <reason>\"). There are no silent dead buttons. Disabled labels use text.muted (dark #64748B) and are never the only place the reason is written: the reason also appears in readable text (text.primary, or text.secondary on base/raised, or text.strong on sunken).\n\n====================================================================\n1. QuietDayReceipt\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. Makes silence readable: a finished \"nothing needs you\" state that lists the checks that were run.\n\nANATOMY (draw on 00d · QuietDayReceipt · 01-anatomy · light, iOS 393, with callouts)\n1. Card: surface.base, radius lg 12, padding 16, shadow sm, full content width (361pt on iOS, 380dp on Android, 358px on web-390, 560px max in the web-1440 Today column).\n2. Heading: h3 20/28/600 text.primary, \"Nothing needs your attention today\". Shown only in the all-ticked state.\n3. Receipt line: 8pt below the heading, caption 12/16 text.secondary, \"Checked 6:00 PM\".\n4. CheckItem row: 12pt below the receipt line, one row of four CheckItems separated by 16pt gaps, wrapping to a second row if the width runs out. The items are \"weather\", \"air\", \"alerts\" and \"your calendar\".\n5. CheckItem: a 16pt tick glyph in text.secondary (C5), 4pt gap, caption 12/16 text.secondary label. An optional source time follows in the same style after \" · \", for example \"air · 6:00 PM\".\n6. No illustration, no keeper, no colour fill, no semantic tint.\nCallout on the card: \"The whole receipt reads as one line: Checked 6:00 PM · weather · air · alerts · your calendar\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows of the grid)\nV1 Today full: the card above (f1-today-tab).\nV2 Widget one-liner: a single caption line with no card, \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\", drawn inside a 338×158pt medium widget at 11pt minimum text size (f7-today-widget).\nV3 Briefing settings row: a settings row under the Briefings group, bodySmall 14/20 text.secondary, \"Skipped tonight — nothing needed you\" (f4-notification-settings, f4-briefing-optin-card).\nV4 Strip empty: a FourteenDayStrip (C14) with 14 empty day cells in one ink colour, then the caption \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" (f5-today-calendar-strip).\nV5 Year band empty: a YearBand (C14) with 12 month columns and the four lanes You / City / County / State left empty, then the caption \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" (x-place-file).\nV4 and V5 are fixture-free specimens: no address, place label or scope is drawn on them. The provider named in their failed state is the City of Vancouver calendar.\n\nSTATES (columns of the grid)\nS1 All ticked: the only state that shows the heading (V1) or the all-clear phrase (V2 to V5).\nS2 One pending: the heading is absent. The \"air\" CheckItem shows a spinner-free pending mark instead of a tick. Draw the mark as three 3pt dots in a row inside the 16pt glyph box, in text.secondary; it is never a single dot or a circle, so it can't be read as a filled provenance mark. The label reads \"air · not back yet\". The receipt line still reads \"Checked 6:00 PM\". Nothing animates.\nS3 One failed: the heading is absent. The \"air\" CheckItem becomes a line: a 16pt error glyph (semantic.error on the glyph only, C5), then \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, then a \"Retry\" text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 with a 44×44pt hit area. The other three items keep their ticks.\n\nPer-variant rules for S2 and S3 (fill every cell of the 5×3 grid):\n- V2 widget. S2: \"Checked 6:00 PM · air not back yet\". S3: \"Couldn't reach AirNow · 6:00 PM\", with no Retry inside the widget, because a widget tap opens Today, where Retry lives.\n- V3 settings row. S2: \"Not applicable: the row appears only after tonight's check has finished\". S3: \"Tonight's check couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\".\n- V4 strip. S2: \"Not applicable: the strip shows WarmingSkeleton until the calendar returns\". S3: no strip is drawn. The slot shows \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\", with the error glyph on the glyph only.\n- V5 year band. S2: \"Not applicable: the year band shows WarmingSkeleton until the calendar returns\". S3: no band is drawn. The slot shows \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\".\n\nGRID. 00d · QuietDayReceipt · 02-variants-by-states · light is the 5×3 grid above, with iOS specimens. 00d · QuietDayReceipt · 03-variants-by-states · dark is the same full grid in dark tokens. Container: the V1 card is dark raised on dark app. Tick in dark text.secondary, error glyph in #DC2626, Retry in #38BDF8; print their \"on dark raised\" figures from C5.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · QuietDayReceipt · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: the heading wraps to three lines. The CheckItems become a vertical list, one item per line (tick plus word). Retry drops under \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" on its own line and stays 44pt tall.\n- (b) 200% Android: the same vertical list, with 48dp rows.\n- (c) Greyscale of S1, S2 and S3: they still differ by glyph shape (check / three dots / error glyph) and by words (\"not back yet\", \"Couldn't reach\").\n- Extra row below: the V2 widget at AX sizes, text only, with no glyphs. The line wraps to at most three lines inside the medium widget.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken as a list. S1: \"Nothing needs your attention today. Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\" S2: \"Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, alerts, your calendar. Air: not back yet.\" S3: \"Couldn't reach AirNow.\" followed by the button \"Retry air quality\". (The S1 label adds the heading and the time to the contract's \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\"; see Notes 26.)\n- Non-colour encoding: every tick is paired with a word, and state is carried by the glyph shape plus words.\n- Targets: Retry is 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web. The CheckItems are not targets.\n- The S2 → S1 change is announced politely, once, without moving focus.\n\nCOPY. Show the heading only when every check succeeded. Strings: \"Nothing needs your attention today\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM\" · \"weather\" · \"air\" · \"alerts\" · \"your calendar\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM · nothing needs you tonight\" · \"Skipped tonight — nothing needed you\" · \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\" · \"Checked — nothing on file for the next year\" · \"Couldn't reach AirNow\" · \"Retry\".\n\nPLATFORMS. The same on iOS, Android and web. The only differences are target size (44pt / 48dp / 44px) and the widget text-only fallback at AX sizes.\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · QuietDayReceipt · 05-in-context-and-rules · light). All three crops are for PLACE B, viewer Jordan Lee, on Mon 19 Oct 2026 at 6:10 PM. Pickup there is Thursday, so nothing is due tonight and the quiet state is true.\n- f1-today-tab: the Today tab for PLACE B with the scope string \"Saved place · Only you\", the air band (AqiBand, C14) and the V1 card under it.\n- f7-today-widget: the medium widget labelled \"Birchfield Ct\" with the V2 line.\n- f4-notification-settings: Jordan's Briefings group, showing the line \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" (the reminder before last Thursday's pickup) with the V3 row under it.\nAlso consumed by: f5-today-calendar-strip, x-place-file, f4-briefing-optin-card, f11-keeper-strip.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"All caught up\", \"Inbox zero\" or \"You're all set\", draw \"Nothing needs your attention today\" with the four checks, because the person needs to see what was checked, not a mood.\n- Instead of showing the heading while one provider is still loading, draw S2 with no heading, because an early all-clear teaches people to stop trusting the product.\n- Instead of a cheerful illustration or keeper pose, draw the plain card, because silence is a fact here, not a celebration.\n- Instead of ticks in filled or hollow circles, draw bare check strokes, because filled vs hollow is reserved for provenance.\n- Instead of a generic \"Something went wrong\", draw \"Couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\", because a failed check names its provider.\n\n====================================================================\n2. WarmingSkeleton\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. Content-shaped placeholders sitting in their final slots during cold loads of 1–10 s, so nothing jumps when the data arrives.\n\nANATOMY (00d · WarmingSkeleton · 01-anatomy · light, iOS 393, with callouts)\n1. Shapes are filled surface.sunken (#F3F4F6) on surface.base cards. They match the final geometry: strip cells, track shapes, row bars, avatar circles, and for a facts count a number bar plus pill-shaped chip bars (the count is an integer plus chips; there is no ring, so there is no ring skeleton). Each shape uses the same radius as the part it stands in for. Shapes are filled, not outlined, because an outline-only skeleton reads as an empty state.\n2. The skeleton reserves the exact final height. Draw a height ruler beside each skeleton and a second ruler beside the loaded version, and caption both \"same height\".\n3. No text, no glyphs and no \"checking…\" anywhere inside a skeleton.\n4. Shimmer: a soft band 30% of the shape's width, surface.base at 60% opacity, sweeping left to right over the shapes. One pass takes 1.2 s. The shimmer stops after 4 passes (under 5 s) and holds static.\n5. Container: one accessibility element labelled \"Loading\" (callout).\n6. Dark: shapes are dark raised #1E293B on dark base. On a dark raised card, shapes are dark border.strong #374151. Skeleton shapes are decorative and have no contrast requirement; print that on the board.\n\nVARIANTS (rows)\nV1 Section skeleton (f1-today-tab), drawn at iOS 393. Air band: a 48pt-tall row with a 12pt-tall filled track shape (radius pill) and a 96×12pt label bar. Pickup card: a card with a 42×42pt square (radius md) in the KindGlyph slot, two bars (200×20pt and 240×14pt, radius xs) and two 44pt-tall button shapes of equal width (radius md). Fourteen-day strip: 14 cells, each 22×40pt with radius xs and 4pt gaps.\nV2 Row skeleton (lists), drawn at iOS 393. A row whose height equals the final row's height (draw it at 56pt, the MemberRow height, and caption it \"height = the consuming row's final height\"): 16pt padding, a 40pt avatar circle, and two bars (60% width × 14pt and 40% width × 12pt). Draw three rows.\nV3 Instrument skeleton. Four sub-specimens:\n  a. 14-day strip: 14 cells, 361×40pt overall.\n  b. Year band: 361×120pt, 12 month columns × 4 lanes of 24pt, with lane-label bars.\n  c. Scale strip: 4 rows, each 48pt tall, with a 12pt filled track shape and a 72×14pt reading bar beside it.\n  d. Bill trend: 12 columns, 16pt wide with 8pt gaps and radius xs, bottom-aligned, at heights of 40, 56, 48, 64, 52, 44, 60, 72, 56, 48, 64 and 52pt (varied, never equal), plus a 160×14pt summary bar above them.\nV4 Panel skeleton (f9-nearby-cells-map): a 361×240pt panel with radius lg in surface.sunken, a 6×4 grid of 1px border.default lines (decoration), and a 120×14pt caption bar below.\nExact C13 names for V3: \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument skeleton · 14-day strip / <state> / ios\" · \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument skeleton · year band / <state> / ios\" · \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument skeleton · scale strip / <state> / ios\" · \"WarmingSkeleton / instrument skeleton · bill trend / <state> / ios\", where <state> is shimmer, static or replaced progressively.\n\nSTATES (columns)\nS1 Shimmer (default): draw the band mid-sweep.\nS2 Static (Reduce Motion): the same shapes with no band. Loaded content replaces the skeleton with a 200 ms cross-fade.\nS3 Replaced progressively. Each replacement is a 200 ms cross-fade in place, and the height ruler shows no change. Loaded content per variant:\n  - V1: the air band is loaded (AqiBand, C14: AQI 42 Good, AirNow, observed 7:00 AM); the pickup card and the strip are still skeletons.\n  - V2: row 1 is loaded as MemberRow (C14, owner variant) \"Maya Chen\" with the caption \"Owner\"; rows 2 and 3 are still skeletons.\n  - V3: sub-specimen a is loaded as FourteenDayStrip (C14) for HOME A starting Mon 19 Oct 2026, with pickup marks on Tue 20 Oct and Tue 27 Oct and date marks on Fri 23 Oct (Clark Public Utilities), Mon 26 Oct (voter registration must arrive by), Wed 28 Oct (City of Vancouver water) and Sun 1 Nov (HOA dues). Sub-specimens b, c and d are still skeletons.\n  - V4: \"Not applicable: the panel lands as one piece\".\n\nGRID. 00d · WarmingSkeleton · 02-variants-by-states · light has 4 rows × 3 columns. 00d · WarmingSkeleton · 03-variants-by-states · dark is the same full grid in dark tokens. Container: V1–V3 cards are dark raised on dark app, so their shapes are dark border.strong #374151; the V4 panel sits on dark base, so its shapes are dark raised #1E293B.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE / REDUCE MOTION (00d · WarmingSkeleton · 04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: bar heights follow the line heights of the text they stand in for at AX5, so V1 grows to its AX5 final height and the two pickup button shapes stack. V2 rows grow to their AX5 heights.\n- (b) 200% Android: the same, with 48dp minimum rows.\n- (c) Greyscale: the skeleton still reads as a placeholder, because there is no text and the shapes are content-shaped.\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Reduce Motion\": V1 and V3 drawn static, with the caption \"no shimmer; replacements cross-fade\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Loading\", once, on the container. VoiceOver reads the container label. Android sets contentDescription \"Loading\" on the container. Web sets aria-busy=\"true\" on the section plus a visually hidden \"Loading\". Individual shapes are hidden from assistive tech.\n- Non-colour encoding: none is needed, because skeletons carry no data.\n- Targets: skeletons are not interactive, and controls are not tappable until their content lands.\n\nCOPY. No text inside skeletons, and no \"checking…\" claims.\n\nPLATFORMS\n- All platforms skip skeletons for loads under about 1 s. Draw a callout: \"under 1 s: show nothing new; keep the old content\".\n- Warm screens (the widget path, f7-widget-tap-landing) never show a skeleton. They refresh in place with no hairline.\n- Android uses the app's existing shimmer component with these shapes and the shimmer spec in anatomy item 4. iOS and web match it.\n- Fail-closed components never get a skeleton: the founding meter (f9-founding-meter-preview), the Earn row (f9-earn-removal) and LandingBannerSlot render nothing until their data is confirmed.\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · WarmingSkeleton · 05-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- f1-today-tab: a cold load showing V1 under the header \"Larkspur Loop\" with the scope string \"Your household\".\n- f3-members-roster: V2 with three rows.\n- f10-bill-trend: V3d inside the bill trend card.\nAlso consumed by: x-place-file, f5-today-calendar-strip, f1-your-places, f3-household-block, f3-member-home-dashboard, f8-compare-reveal, f8-compare-arrival-header, f9-privacy-mirror, f9-nearby-cells-map, f11-keeper-strip, f7-widget-tap-landing (as the no-skeleton warm path).\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a full-page spinner, draw content-shaped skeletons in their final slots, because a spinner hides how long the wait is and makes the page jump when data lands.\n- Instead of an empty card frame with nothing inside, draw the filled shapes of the final content, because a frame-only skeleton looks like an empty state.\n- Instead of skeleton text such as \"Checking air…\", draw text-free shapes, because a skeleton must not claim a check is under way.\n- Instead of a ring-shaped placeholder for a facts count, draw a number bar and chip bars, because the count is an integer plus chips and never a ring.\n- Instead of a skeleton for the founding meter or the invite banner, draw nothing, because those fail closed and must never suggest something is coming.\n- Instead of a shimmer that loops forever, stop it after 4 passes, because idle loops stop within 5 s.\n\n====================================================================\n3. InlineUndo\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. Reversible removals and declines with no timers and no dialogs.\n\nANATOMY (00d · InlineUndo · 01-anatomy · light, iOS 393, with callouts)\n1. The removed row collapses in place (height animates to 56pt over 200 ms) into a line on surface.base: bodySmall 14/20 text.primary 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\"', then \" · \", then an \"Undo\" text button (bodySmallMedium primary.700, C5) with a 44×44pt hit area.\n2. The line persists until the person leaves the screen. There is no countdown, no progress bar and no auto-dismiss. Callout: \"stays until you leave this screen\".\n3. Optional echo, Android only: draw it as a separate Android 412 inset beside the iOS anatomy, labelled \"android only\". It is a snackbar with the same text and Undo. It stays for as long as a screen reader is running (indefinite duration). It is never the only record: the in-row line is always present. The web toast appears only in the Platforms row on 04. iOS never draws an echo.\n4. Fan-out hold: a household-notifying write (Mark paid) holds its household notification until the undo line closes. Draw a callout with the caption line \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" in caption 12/16 text.secondary under the undo line.\n\nVARIANTS (rows)\nV1 Removed row: 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\" · Undo' (f1-your-places).\nV2 Declined ask: \"Just you, then. · Undo\" in the household block slot (f3-household-block). This is the contract string; see Notes 16.\nV3 Triage decision: \"Comcast · Recycled · Undo\", kept until the person taps \"Finish day\" (f10-mail-day-triage). Draw the \"Finish day\" button beneath it.\nV4 Undo all: a line at the top of the triage list, \"6 pieces sorted · Undo all 6\" (f10-mail-day-triage).\nV5 Bill + photo deleted: \"Bill and photo deleted · Undo\" (f10-bill-provenance, f3-bills-list).\nV6 Fan-out hold: \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid · Undo\", with the caption \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" (f3-bills-list). This variant is added from the contract's fan-out rule; see Notes 25.\n\nSTATES (columns)\nS1 Pending undo: the collapsed line with Undo.\nS2 Undone: the original row returns at full height with a primary.50 fill that fades to surface.base over 300 ms (Reduce Motion: shown static, no fade). Announced as \"Restored\". For V2 the household block ask returns. For V4 all six rows return. For V6 no household notification is sent.\nS3 Committed: the person has left and come back. The row is gone, the list has closed the gap, and there is no trace or banner. For V6 the household notification has been sent (draw a mini PushCopy thumbnail \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" beside it for reference).\n\nGRID. 00d · InlineUndo · 02-variants-by-states · light has 6 rows × 3 columns, iOS. 00d · InlineUndo · 03-variants-by-states · dark is the same full grid in dark tokens. Container: the rows sit in a dark raised card on dark app; the Undo link is #38BDF8 (C5, on dark raised).\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · InlineUndo · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: the message wraps, and \"Undo\" moves to its own line below, left-aligned, still 44pt tall.\n- (b) 200% Android: the same, with a 48dp Undo.\n- (c) Greyscale: Undo is still recognisable by its word and its weight (500 vs 400).\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Platforms\": see PLATFORMS.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: when a line appears, role=status announces 'Removed The Blairmont rental. Undo, button.' Undo is focusable. Focus stays where it was and is not moved to Undo. After Undo, the status is \"Restored The Blairmont rental.\"\n- Non-colour encoding: Undo is a word with a weight change, not only a link colour.\n- Targets: Undo is 44×44pt on iOS, 48×48dp on Android and 44×44px on web.\n\nCOPY. No \"(4s)\" countdowns and no \"Undo in 5…\". The pattern is \"<what happened> · Undo\". Strings: 'Removed \"The Blairmont rental\"' · \"Just you, then.\" · \"Comcast · Recycled\" · \"6 pieces sorted\" · \"Undo all 6\" · \"Bill and photo deleted\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid\" · \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" · \"Restored\" · \"Finish day\".\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: in-row line only. There is no native snackbar, so the echo is not drawn.\n- Android: in-row line, plus an optional Material 3 snackbar echo with indefinite duration, 48dp action, drawn above the bottom tab bar with scroll padding reserved.\n- Web: in-row line, plus an optional toast in a polite live region at the bottom left (web-1440) or above the tab bar (web-390). The toast has no auto-hide while focus is inside it.\nDraw one specimen per platform for V1 S1 in the \"Platforms\" row below the three columns on 04, named \"InlineUndo / removed row / pending undo / ios\", \"… / android\" and \"… / web-390\".\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · InlineUndo · 05-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- f1-your-places: the list with V1 in place of the removed row.\n- f10-mail-day-triage: V3 and V4 together, with \"Finish day\" at the bottom.\n- f3-household-block: V2 in the block's slot.\nAlso consumed by: x-date-sheet, f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming, f6-home-basics-rows, x-place-file, f3-bills-list, f10-snap-capture-tray.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a \"Remove this place?\" dialog for a cheap delete, draw the in-row V1 line, because routine actions are reversible and dialogs teach people to click through.\n- Instead of \"Undo (4s)\" with a countdown, draw \"Undo\" with no timer, because undo stays until the person leaves the screen.\n- Instead of a toast as the only trace, draw the in-row line (and the toast only as an echo), because toasts vanish before some people can reach them.\n- Instead of sending \"marked paid\" to the household at once, hold it until the undo line closes, because a notification can't be taken back.\n\n====================================================================\n4. DestructiveConfirm\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. The confirm for real losses. It names what goes and what stays.\n\nANATOMY (00d · DestructiveConfirm · 01-anatomy · light, iOS 393 plus web-1440 crop, with callouts)\n1. Container. A dialog (V1, V2, V3): surface.base, radius xl 16, padding 24, width 320pt on iOS, 312dp on Android (Material 3 basic dialog), 400px on web, over the platform's standard scrim, shadow lg. A sheet (V4): a surface.base sheet with radius xl 16 on the top corners, a large detent, and a visible \"Close\" in the top bar.\n2. Title: h3 20/28/600 text.primary, a question that names the object (\"Delete this photo?\").\n3. Body: one sentence, body 16/24 text.primary, naming what survives.\n4. Buttons: two equal-size buttons 44pt tall (48dp on Android), radius md 8, whose labels describe outcomes.\n   - Destructive button: surface.base fill, 1.5px semantic.error border (C5), a leading 16pt trash glyph in semantic.error, and the label in body 16/24 at weight 600 in text.primary. The red goes on the border and glyph only, as the house style requires. Callouts: \"no red fill\" and \"no red text\".\n   - Keep button: surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border, label bodyMedium 16/24/500 text.primary, no glyph.\n   - Order: Keep leads and Delete trails when side by side. When stacked (iOS at every size, and all platforms at AX5/200%), Delete is on top and Keep below.\n5. Initial focus: the title for screen readers. Keyboard focus lands on the Keep button, never on the destructive one. Draw the focus ring (C9) on Keep in one specimen.\n6. Dark: dialogs and sheets are dark base (never dark raised). The destructive border and trash glyph stay semantic.error #DC2626 (C5, on dark base, which passes for a non-text edge and glyph); the label is dark text primary at 600. Print this on the dark grid. The contract's red label is an alternative for the founder (Notes 14), not drawn here.\n\nVARIANTS (rows; viewer for V1–V3 is Maya Chen, for V4 Sam Ortega)\nV1 One photo. Title \"Delete this photo?\" Body \"The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed.\" Buttons \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\". (f10-mail-piece-photo, f10-bill-provenance)\nV2 All photos. Title \"Delete all 17 photos?\" Body \"The bills and their amounts stay; only the photos are removed.\" Buttons \"Delete 17 photos\" / \"Keep them\". (f10-mail-snap-privacy)\nV3 Keeper. Title \"Remove Ollie?\" Body \"Today goes back to no keeper. You can add one again any time.\" Buttons \"Remove Ollie\" / \"Keep Ollie\". (f11-keeper-naming)\nV4 Leave home sheet. Title \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" Two labelled lists, each item a 16pt glyph plus words:\n  \"What goes\" (glyph: minus stroke): \"The household calendar and bills\" · \"Household activity notifications\" · \"Your access to this home's place file\".\n  \"What stays\" (glyph: check stroke): \"Dates you added that are Only you\" · \"Your saved places\" · \"Bills you marked paid still show 'Sam (no longer here)'\".\n  Buttons \"Leave this home\" (destructive) / \"Stay in this home\". (f3-members-roster)\n\nSTATES (columns)\nS1 Open: as above.\nS2 Deleting: the title stays. The body is replaced by a progress line in body 16/24 text.primary with a 4pt linear bar (primary.700 on surface.sunken) under it. V1 \"Deleting the photo…\" · V2 \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" · V3 \"Removing Ollie…\" · V4 \"Leaving Larkspur Loop…\". Both outcome buttons are hidden until the action finishes. Escape (web), Back (Android) and swipe-to-dismiss do nothing during S2, and the live region keeps reading progress. On the V4 sheet, \"Close\" stays visible but disabled per C15: label in text.muted, still focusable, read as \"Close, unavailable, Close is available when this finishes.\", and the progress line above it is the readable reason. Dialogs (V1–V3) have no Close, so nothing else is drawn on them.\nS3 Done: the dialog or sheet is closed. Draw the host screen's status line that replaces it, in bodySmall text.primary with a 16pt check glyph: V1 \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · V2 \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" · V3 \"Ollie removed.\" · V4 lands on the Place tab with the line \"You left Larkspur Loop.\" There is no Undo on these, because the loss is real.\n\nGRID. 00d · DestructiveConfirm · 02-variants-by-states · light has 4 × 3 cells on iOS. 00d · DestructiveConfirm · 04-variants-by-states · dark is the same full grid in dark tokens. Container: every dialog and sheet is dark base over the scrim, with the dark rule from anatomy item 6.\n\nPLATFORMS (00d · DestructiveConfirm · 03-platforms · light; light only, see Notes \"Omitted\"). V1 S1 drawn four ways:\n- iOS 393: the custom in-app dialog with stacked buttons, Delete on top. It is not the system alert, so the outlined destructive treatment can show.\n- Android 412: a Material 3 basic dialog with the same title, body and outlined buttons side by side, right-aligned (\"Keep it\" then \"Delete photo\"). Back cancels in S1.\n- web-390: a bottom-anchored dialog at full width minus 16px each side, buttons side by side.\n- web-1440 crop: a 400px centred modal, buttons right-aligned side by side. Escape cancels in S1. Focus is trapped inside the dialog and returns to the invoking control on close.\nAlso draw V4 on iOS (sheet with Close) and Android (bottom sheet with a drag handle and a visible \"Close\").\nNames: \"DestructiveConfirm / one photo / open / ios\" (and android, web-390, web-1440) · \"DestructiveConfirm / leave home sheet / open / ios\" (and android).\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · DestructiveConfirm · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: V1 and V4 as scrollable sheets. Buttons stacked full width and pinned at the bottom, with scroll padding reserved so the last body line is never hidden under them.\n- (b) 200% Android: V1 dialog content scrolls and the buttons stack.\n- (c) Greyscale: the destructive button is still distinct by its outcome label (\"Delete photo\"), its trash glyph and its heavier 1.5px border, and the lists in V4 differ by glyph shape and heading word.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Delete this photo?, dialog. The bill and its amount stay; only the photo is removed. Delete photo, button. Keep it, button.\" While deleting, a polite live region reads \"Deleting 5 of 17\", updated at most every 5 items (5, 10, 15, then done).\n- Each variant's title is unique. In S1, Escape (web), Back (Android) and the Close control (sheets) all cancel. In S2 they do nothing, as stated above.\n- Non-colour encoding: the destructive action is named by its label and marked by its glyph, never by red alone. The trash glyph is decorative for screen readers.\n- Targets: 44pt / 48dp / 44px buttons with 8pt gaps.\n\nCOPY. Titles are questions that name the object, bodies name the survivors, and buttons name outcomes. Never just \"Are you sure?\" or \"This can't be undone\". Strings are those listed under VARIANTS and STATES.\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · DestructiveConfirm · 06-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- f10-mail-piece-photo: the photo viewer with V1 open over it.\n- f10-mail-snap-privacy: the \"Mail snaps\" card with V2 open.\n- f3-members-roster: Sam's member view with the V4 sheet.\nAlso consumed by: f10-bill-provenance, f11-keeper-naming.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Are you sure?\" / \"OK\" / \"Cancel\", draw \"Delete this photo?\" / \"Delete photo\" / \"Keep it\", because people decide faster when the buttons say what happens.\n- Instead of \"This can't be undone\", draw the sentence naming what stays, because people fear losing more than they will.\n- Instead of a filled red button, a red slab above the content, or red label text, draw the outlined button with a semantic.error border and trash glyph and a text.primary label, because a red fill shouts, semantic hues go on glyphs and borders only, and red text drops below readable contrast in dark mode.\n- Instead of default focus on the destructive button, put keyboard focus on Keep, because Enter must never destroy something.\n- Instead of this dialog for a cheap removal, use InlineUndo, because dialogs are reserved for losses that can't be undone.\n\n====================================================================\n5. LandingBannerSlot\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. The single arrival slot at the top of Place and /start. It shows exactly one banner at a time.\n\nANATOMY (00d · LandingBannerSlot · 01-anatomy-and-precedence · light, iOS 393, with callouts)\n1. Geometry: copy the attached mailbox-arrival pill exactly (height, radius, padding, fill, edge). Fallback, if the screenshot isn't attached: minimum height 44pt, radius pill, horizontal padding 16, vertical padding 12, surface.base on surface.app, shadow sm, 1px border.default as decoration.\n2. Leading 16pt glyph in text.secondary: an envelope for invitations (V1, V2, V4, and the V3 7-days-out specimen), a link glyph for compare (V5), a sync glyph for sync merge (V6), a home glyph for the claim receipt (V7). The only exception is V3 \"Expires tomorrow\", which uses the warning glyph (see V3).\n3. One-line sentence in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, actor name first.\n4. One trailing action: a text button in bodySmallMedium primary.700 with a 44×44pt hit area.\n5. Placement: 16pt below the navigation title and 16pt above the first section, at full content width (361pt iOS, 380dp Android, 358px web-390, 640px max in the web-1440 Place column).\n6. Two-line content (the expiring variant, or any wrap at large text) switches the shape from pill to radius 2xl 20, so the corners never clip text.\n7. Precedence ladder. Draw it as a vertical list of eight labelled steps with \"wins over\" connectors: invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify. Beside it, draw a scenario: an invite and a compare arrival are both pending, and only the invite banner is shown. Caption: \"Never two banners.\" (The order of claim receipt and sync merge is this board's proposal; see Notes 30.)\n8. Fetch failure: the slot renders nothing and the layout doesn't shift. Draw two stacked frames of the Place top with identical section positions, captioned \"hidden = 0pt; the first section stays put\".\n\nVARIANTS (rows)\nV1 One invite (viewer: Priya): \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\". Degraded form when the name or address can't be shown: \"Someone invited you to a home in Vancouver · Review\".\nV2 Count: \"You have 3 invitations · Review\". Callout: \"→ Invitations list\".\nV3 Expiring (drawn as if viewed on Sun 25 Oct 2026, the day before the Mon 26 Oct expiry): line 1 \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop · Review\". Line 2 is the caption \"Expires tomorrow\" in caption 12/16 text.primary. The leading glyph is a warning glyph in semantic.warning (C5, glyph only). Viewed on Mon 19 Oct instead, the caption reads \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" with the envelope glyph and no warning glyph; draw that as a small secondary specimen in the same row, named \"LandingBannerSlot / expiring · 7 days out / <state> / ios\".\nV4 Sender reissue (viewer: Maya): \"2 invitations need to be sent again · Fix\".\nV5 Expired compare link: \"That comparison link has expired. Type an address to see your own place.\" with the trailing action \"Close\". The sentence wraps to two lines, so this uses the radius 2xl shape.\nV6 Sync merge: \"Synced 3 items from your other device · Review\".\nV7 One-time claim receipt (viewer: Maya): \"You claimed Larkspur Loop · See what moved\". Callout: \"→ the persistent receipt in the place file, 'What moved when you claimed'\".\n\nSTATES (columns)\nS1 Hidden: an empty 0pt slot with a dashed annotation outline (board chrome only).\nS2 Shown: as above.\nS3 Offline: the action is disabled per C15: its label is in text.muted, it stays focusable, and it reads its reason aloud. A caption line below the banner, in caption text.secondary, is the readable reason. V1, V2, V3 and V6: caption \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\", spoken \"Review, unavailable, You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" V4: caption \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\", spoken \"Fix, unavailable, You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\" V5 and V7 keep their action live, because Close and the local receipt work offline; their S3 cells show the S2 banner with the caption \"action works offline\" (board chrome).\n\nGRID. 00d · LandingBannerSlot · 02-variants-by-states · light has 7 × 3 cells on iOS, plus the V3 7-days-out specimens in the V3 row. 00d · LandingBannerSlot · 03-variants-by-states · dark is the same full grid in dark tokens. Container: the banner is dark raised on dark app; actions are #38BDF8 and the warning glyph is #D97706 (C5, on dark raised).\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · LandingBannerSlot · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: the radius 2xl shape. The sentence wraps across as many lines as it needs, and the action moves below it, left-aligned, 44pt tall.\n- (b) 200% Android: the same, with a 48dp action.\n- (c) Greyscale: V3 still reads as expiring because of the words \"Expires tomorrow\" and the warning glyph shape.\n- Extra row below, labelled \"Platforms\": V1 S2 on android and on a web-1440 crop, named \"LandingBannerSlot / one invite / shown / android\" and \"… / web-1440\".\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: role=status when the banner appears, once: \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop. Review, button.\" Expiry is spoken in words: \"Expires tomorrow, Monday 26 October.\"\n- Non-colour encoding: expiry is carried by words plus the warning glyph, never by a tinted pill.\n- Targets: the action is 44pt / 48dp / 44px. The glyph is not a target.\n\nCOPY. Actor name first. Degrade to \"Someone invited you…\" or \"…a home in <city>\" (for HOME A the city is Vancouver). Expiry in words. Offline captions start with \"You're offline.\" Strings are those listed under VARIANTS and STATES.\n\nPLATFORMS. The same geometry on all three. On web, /start (anonymous) can show only V5 and compare arrivals; Place shows all of them.\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · LandingBannerSlot · 05-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- f3-invite-banner: the Place tab for Priya with V1 at the top (iOS, 393pt crop).\n- f8-compare-arrival-header: /start on web-390 (390px crop) with V5 (expired link) above the address field.\n- f1-claim-receipt / x-place-file: Place for Maya with V7.\nAlso consumed by: f9-founding-meter-preview (shares the slot and fails closed the same way).\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of stacking an invite banner over a compare banner, draw only the winner of the precedence ladder, because two banners split attention and push content down.\n- Instead of a red \"Couldn't load invitations\" banner on a fetch failure, render nothing, because a failed optional fetch must not look like an alert.\n- Instead of an amber-tinted pill for expiry, draw \"Expires tomorrow\" in text.primary with the warning hue only on the glyph, because tinted text fails contrast and colour alone doesn't carry meaning.\n- Instead of \"You've been invited!\", draw \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\", because the actor comes first.\n- Instead of a dead action while offline, keep it focusable with its reason read out and written, because silent dead buttons leave people guessing.\n\n====================================================================\n6. NotificationAsk\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. The in-context notification permission ask and its denial states. It is never a second \"Yes\".\n\nANATOMY (00d · NotificationAsk · 01-anatomy · light, iOS 393, with callouts)\nA. Card row form (lives on f4-briefing-optin-card):\n  1. Question in body 16/24 text.primary: \"The night before pickup?\"\n  2. Two buttons of equal weight side by side, \"Yes\" and \"Not now\". Both are outlined (1px text.secondary border, surface.base fill, bodyMedium text.primary label, radius md 8, 44pt tall, equal widths, 8pt gap). Callout: \"Yes fires the OS prompt directly. The OS prompt is not drawn.\"\n  3. Granted collapse: the row becomes \"6:00 PM · Change\", where \"Change\" is a primary.700 text button with a 44pt hit area.\n  4. Time chips expansion (after Change): four chips, \"5:00 PM\", \"6:00 PM\", \"7:00 PM\" and \"8:00 PM\", each 44pt tall with radius pill and 8pt gaps. Unselected: surface.base with a 1px text.secondary border and the label in text.primary. Selected: the C9 selection treatment.\n  5. Status slot at the trailing edge of the row, caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"Saving…\" / \"Saved\" / \"Couldn't save · Retry\".\nB. Primer sheet form, used only for the two indirect entries named by the contract. Draw the anatomy with the pickup entry; the household entry differs only in items 2, 3 and 4.\n  1. iOS sheet at medium detent, with a visible \"Close\" at top right.\n  2. Unique title in h3. Pickup entry: \"Pickup reminders on this phone\". Household entry: \"Household updates on this phone\".\n  3. PushCopy tray preview, with the caption \"This is the whole thing.\" Pickup entry: PushCopy V2 (\"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" / \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\"). Household entry: PushCopy V5 (\"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" / \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\").\n  4. Body in body text.primary. Pickup entry: \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Nothing else unless you turn it on.\" Household entry: \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\"\n  5. Silence contract in bodySmall text.secondary: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\"\n  6. iOS only: one forward button, \"Continue\" (or \"Open Settings\" on V4): primary.700 fill, text.inverse label (C5), full width, 44pt tall, radius md.\n  7. Caption under it in caption text.secondary: \"Your phone will ask next.\"\n  8. Android only: two buttons, \"Continue\" (or \"Open Settings\" on V6) and \"Not now\", both outlined: surface.base fill, 1px text.secondary border, bodyMedium text.primary label, 48dp tall, equal widths, 8dp gap, radius md. Neither is filled, so neither dominates. The filled button is iOS-only.\n\nVARIANTS (C13 row names in brackets)\nV1 Card row [card row] (Yes fires the OS prompt directly).\nV2 Primer iOS [primer ios] (filled Continue only, plus Close).\nV3 Primer Android [primer android] (outlined Continue + Not now, bottom sheet with a drag handle and a visible Close).\nV4 iOS denied [ios denied]: the primer body is replaced by \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" in body text.primary and an \"Open Settings\" button (the iOS filled style from B6). Caption: \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\"\nV5 Android denied once [android denied once]: the V3 primer again, with outlined \"Continue\" re-asking and the caption \"Your phone will ask next.\"\nV6 Android blocked [android blocked]: \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" with \"Open Settings\" and \"Not now\" as equal outlined buttons (B8).\nV7 Time chips expansion [time chips]: the four chips with 6:00 PM selected.\nThe household entry is not a separate variant: it is V2 and V3 with the household title, tray and body, named [primer ios household] and [primer android household].\n\nSTATES\nS1 Never asked: V1 as drawn.\nS2 Granted: the row collapses to \"6:00 PM · Change\".\nS3 Declined: the card slot collapses (200 ms; static under Reduce Motion). It is replaced once by a row \"Put Today on your home screen\" with an \"Add the widget\" text button, and that row is never shown again after this visit.\nS4 Switch on but OS blocked (drawn in the f4-notification-settings Briefings group): the switch shows on. Beneath it: a 16pt warning glyph (semantic.warning, glyph only), then \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" in bodySmall text.primary, then an \"Open Settings\" text button (44pt).\nS5 Saving / Saved / Couldn't save: three small specimens of the V7 row with the status slot showing each word. \"Couldn't save\" keeps the chip the person picked selected and offers \"Retry\".\n\nLAYOUT OF THE GRID (not every variant has every state; fill the cells as listed)\n00d · NotificationAsk · 02-card-row-states · light: rows V1 and V7 × columns S1–S5, iOS.\n- V1: S1 as drawn · S2 collapsed row · S3 collapsed slot plus the widget row · S4 \"Not applicable: shown in settings, not on the card\" · S5 \"Not applicable: the card row saves only through the chips\".\n- V7: S1 \"Not applicable: chips appear only after granted\" · S2 chips with 6:00 PM selected · S3 \"Not applicable: chips are hidden after a decline\" · S4 the settings group row described above · S5 the three status specimens.\n00d · NotificationAsk · 03-primer-and-denial-by-platform · light: seven full sheets at their platform widths, each with its exact name and, under it, a caption naming its entry:\n- \"NotificationAsk / primer ios / never asked / ios\" — caption \"after the first confirmed pickup\"\n- \"NotificationAsk / primer android / never asked / android\" — caption \"after the first confirmed pickup\"\n- \"NotificationAsk / primer ios household / never asked / ios\" — caption \"after household activity from Mail\"\n- \"NotificationAsk / primer android household / never asked / android\" — caption \"after household activity from Mail\"\n- \"NotificationAsk / ios denied / denied / ios\" — caption \"after the iOS prompt was declined\"\n- \"NotificationAsk / android denied once / denied once / android\" — caption \"after the Android prompt was declined once\"\n- \"NotificationAsk / android blocked / blocked / android\" — caption \"after the Android prompt was declined twice\"\n00d · NotificationAsk · 04-card-row-and-primer · dark, in dark tokens: V1 at S1 and S2; V7 at S2; V7 at S4 (the settings group blocked row); the pickup-entry V2 and V3 sheets. Container: the card row and settings group are dark raised on dark app; sheets are dark base. The selected chip uses the C9 dark selection. On the iOS primer (V2), Continue uses a #38BDF8 fill with the dark text.inverse label (C5, on dark base). On the Android primer (V3), both buttons are outlined: dark base fill, 1px #94A3B8 border, dark text primary label. Everything else on this component is light only (see PUBLISH and Notes \"Omitted\").\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · NotificationAsk · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: \"Yes\" and \"Not now\" stack full width in that order, both 44pt tall. The chips wrap to one per line. The primer sheet scrolls, and Continue stays pinned with scroll padding.\n- (b) 200% Android: the same, with 48dp buttons and chips and 8dp gaps.\n- (c) Greyscale: the selected chip is still clear from its check glyph and weight. S4 still reads as a problem from its words.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken, card row: \"The night before pickup? Yes, button. Not now, button.\" Chips: \"6:00 PM, selected, 2 of 4.\" Status is announced in a polite live region (\"Saved\") without moving focus. Each primer's title is unique (\"Pickup reminders on this phone\", \"Household updates on this phone\") and read first when the sheet opens.\n- Non-colour encoding: selected chips have fill + check + weight. The blocked state has glyph + words.\n- Targets: buttons and chips are 44pt on iOS, 48dp with 8dp gaps on Android and 44px on web.\n\nCOPY. The body lists the real defaults (anatomy B4). Silence contract: \"Only when something needs you. No news means nothing's up.\" Other strings: \"The night before pickup?\" · \"Yes\" · \"Not now\" · \"6:00 PM · Change\" · \"5:00 PM\" · \"6:00 PM\" · \"7:00 PM\" · \"8:00 PM\" · \"Pickup reminders on this phone\" · \"Household updates on this phone\" · \"Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\" · \"Continue\" · \"Your phone will ask next.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" · \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\" · \"Open Settings\" · \"Put Today on your home screen\" · \"Add the widget\" · \"Saving…\" · \"Saved\" · \"Couldn't save · Retry\" · \"Close\".\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: primer has a filled Continue only (plus Close). When denied, \"Open Settings\" goes to the app's Notifications page.\n- Android: primer has outlined Continue + Not now. Denied once → Continue re-asks. Blocked → outlined \"Open Settings\" + \"Not now\".\n- Web: not drawn on this board (no web push in scope). This is listed as a question on 00d · Notes.\n- All platforms: never at cold launch, sign-up or save. Draw a callout on 01: \"Appears only after an action that shows the purpose\".\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · NotificationAsk · 06-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- f4-briefing-optin-card: the card on Today for HOME A with V1.\n- f4-notification-primer: V2 (pickup entry) over f4-today-pickup-card (PickupCard, C14) after \"Yes, Tuesday is right\".\n- f4-notification-settings: the Briefings group in S4.\nAlso consumed by: f4-today-pickup-card, f3-household-notifications (the household-entry primer, drawn on 03).\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a primer button labelled \"Yes\" or \"Allow\", draw \"Continue\" with \"Your phone will ask next.\", because the decision already happened on the card and a second Yes is a trick.\n- Instead of imitating the iOS or Android system dialog, draw the in-app sheet with the PushCopy tray illustration, because a fake system dialog is deceptive and App Review rejects it.\n- Instead of a permanent amber banner for someone who tapped Not now, close the slot and offer the widget row once, because \"Not now\" never asks again on its own.\n- Instead of a filled \"Yes\" beside a grey \"Not now\", draw two equal outlined buttons, because declines are equal weight.\n- Instead of a filled Continue beside an outlined Not now on Android, draw both outlined, because Android keeps Not now as an equal choice.\n- Instead of the ask at launch or sign-up, draw it only after the first confirmed pickup, household activity from Mail, or a card tap, because people grant a request whose purpose they can see.\n\n====================================================================\n7. PushCopy\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. The canonical push strings and tray-preview artwork, so every surface draws the same notification.\n\nANATOMY (00d · PushCopy · 01-anatomy-and-levels · light, with callouts)\n1. Tray preview drawn as an in-app illustration: a surface.raised inset card (radius lg 12, padding 12) sitting on a surface.sunken panel (radius lg, padding 16). It is never drawn as a system alert, over a wallpaper, or with system chrome.\n2. Inside the inset: the Pantopus app icon from the design system at 20pt (if the design system has none, use the C14 fallback box and log it under missing dependencies), then \"Pantopus\" in caption 12/16 text.strong, then \"now\" in caption text.strong, right-aligned. (Text on the sunken-framed raised inset uses text.strong for secondary words.)\n3. Title: bodySmallMedium 14/20/500 text.primary, 30 characters or fewer, caveat first. Draw a character ruler under it with a tick at 30.\n4. Body: bodySmall 14/20 text.primary, 40 characters or fewer on its first line, carrying the source. Draw a ruler with a tick at 40.\n5. Place label: the street name only (\"Larkspur Loop\"), and only when the person has more than one place. Callout: \"drop ' · Larkspur Loop' for someone with one place\".\n6. Caption under the panel: \"This is the whole thing.\" in caption text.strong (it sits on the sunken panel).\n7. Actions (expanded only): title-case text buttons inside the inset, separated by a 1px border.default rule.\n8. Levels table on the same artboard, four rows, each named as given:\n   - \"PushCopy / levels / pickup briefings dates bills / ios android\": iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\n   - \"PushCopy / levels / household / ios android\": iOS Passive / Android LOW, one thread per home.\n   - \"PushCopy / levels / air 151 and above and noaa / ios android\": iOS Time Sensitive / Android HIGH.\n   - \"PushCopy / levels / air below 151 / ios android\": iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\n   Below the table: \"Never Time Sensitive for pickup.\" and \"Android: the air group holds two channels, one HIGH (AQI 151 or above, and NOAA warnings) and one DEFAULT (below 151).\"\n\nVARIANTS (rows; the viewer is Maya, HOME A, who also has a saved place, so street labels show)\nV1 Unconfirmed pickup. Title \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\" (28). Body \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\" (35). Action \"That's My Day\". Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV2 Confirmed pickup. Title \"Recycling + garbage tomorrow\" (28). Body \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\" (32). No action. Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV3 Air, Time Sensitive. Title \"Unhealthy air: AQI 176\" (22). Body \"AirNow, 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (31). Level: iOS Time Sensitive / Android HIGH (176 ≥ 151). On this row only, draw the words \"Time Sensitive\" as a caption word inside the inset beside \"now\" (caption text.strong), not as copied system chrome.\nV4 Air, below 151 (the fixture alert). Title \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" (25). Body \"AirNow, 4:00 PM · Larkspur Loop\" (31). Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT (the air group's below-threshold channel).\nV5 Bill marked paid (viewer: Maya, the actor is Sam). Title \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\" (25). Body \"Due Fri 23 Oct · Larkspur Loop\" (30). No amount. Level: iOS Passive / Android LOW.\nV6 Household roll-up. Title \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\" (23). Body \"Larkspur Loop\". One notification that updates in place. Level: iOS Passive / Android LOW.\nV7 Date reminder. Title \"Lease notice due in 14 days\" (27). Body \"Tell your landlord by Mon 1 Mar\" (31). Action \"Done\". Level: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT.\nV8 Hidden-preview placeholders: \"Pickup reminder\" · \"Air quality alert\" · \"Household update\" · \"Date reminder\". Android public version: \"Pantopus · Pickup reminder\" (and \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\" for the others).\nPrint each string's character count beside it, as above.\n\nSTATES (columns)\nS1 Collapsed tray at true truncation. On iOS, drawn at 393pt device width (inset 361pt). On Android, at 412dp (inset 380dp): title on one line, body on one line truncated with an ellipsis at the real width. This is the only place on this board where an ellipsis is allowed. Mark the visible part with the ruler. For V8, S1 shows the four placeholders as collapsed trays with previews hidden (\"Pantopus\" plus the placeholder).\nS2 Expanded: the full body. V1 and V7 add their action row (\"That's My Day\", \"Done\"). V2–V6 are drawn expanded with the full body and the board caption \"No action\" under the inset. V8: \"Not applicable: a hidden preview does not expand until the device is unlocked\".\nS3 Lock screen public version. iOS with previews hidden shows \"Pantopus\" plus the V8 placeholder for its group (V1, V2 → \"Pickup reminder\"; V3, V4 → \"Air quality alert\"; V5, V6 → \"Household update\"; V7 → \"Date reminder\"). Android shows \"Pantopus · Pickup reminder\" (and the matching placeholder for each). For V8, S3 shows the iOS and Android public forms side by side. Addresses, names and amounts never appear here.\n\nGRIDS\n00d · PushCopy · 02-ios-variants-by-states · light: 8 × 3, iOS.\n00d · PushCopy · 03-android-variants-by-states · light: 8 × 3, Android. Draw the Android small icon and app name row in the same illustrated style, with no system chrome.\n00d · PushCopy · 04-ios-and-android · dark: V1, V2, V3, V5 and V7 at S1 and S2, on both platforms, in dark tokens. Container: the inset is dark raised on a dark base panel; secondary words in the inset use dark text.secondary #94A3B8 (C5, on dark raised). Everything else on this component is light only (see PUBLISH and Notes \"Omitted\").\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · PushCopy · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) AX5 iOS: in the in-app illustration, the title and body wrap fully. The caption \"This is the whole thing.\" wraps. The illustration grows taller and never scales down.\n- (b) 200% Android: the same.\n- (c) Greyscale: the Time Sensitive marker on V3 still reads by its words, and the level is never carried by colour alone.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken, for the in-app illustration: read as one element, \"Example notification. Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow. Recycling + garbage · city schedule. This is the whole thing.\"\n- No house numbers and no full addresses in any string. Actions are in title case (\"That's My Day\", \"Done\").\n- Non-colour encoding: levels are labelled in words on the board.\n- Targets: the illustration is not interactive. Real tray actions are the system's.\n\nCOPY. Titles are 30 characters or fewer with the caveat first, bodies 40 or fewer with no house number and no amounts. Never \"Open Pantopus to…\". No keeper name or voice. No marketing, Founding or referral pushes. No pickup reminder duplicated alongside the briefing.\n\nPLATFORMS\n- iOS: Active / Passive / Time Sensitive as in the levels table. Hidden previews show the placeholder. Provisional authorization is never used for pickup.\n- Android: DEFAULT / LOW / HIGH channels, one channel per group, except the air group, which holds a HIGH and a DEFAULT channel (levels table). The public version is \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\".\n- Web: no push on this board.\n- Actions: no tray \"Mark paid\" action on any platform, because it fans out to the household and can't show an Undo.\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · PushCopy · 06-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- f4-notification-primer: V2's tray illustration inside the primer.\n- f4-notification-settings: the Air & weather alerts group row with V3 as its example and the level spelled out.\n- f3-household-notifications: the notification list row that V5 lands on.\nAlso consumed by: f4-today-pickup-card (landing for V1/V2), f1-today-air-band (landing for V3/V4).\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of \"Recycling and garbage tomorrow — not yet confirmed\", draw \"Unconfirmed: pickup tomorrow\", because at 30 characters a caveat at the end is the part that gets cut.\n- Instead of \"Bins out tonight. 2418 NE Larkspur Loop.\", draw \"Bins out tonight · Larkspur Loop\", because a house number doesn't belong on a lock screen.\n- Instead of \"Sam paid Clark PUD $142.18\", draw \"Sam marked Clark PUD paid\", because amounts stay inside the app and \"marked paid\" is the product's word.\n- Instead of drawing the notification over a phone wallpaper, as a system alert, or with a copied Time Sensitive badge, draw the inset illustration captioned \"This is the whole thing.\", because an imitation of system UI misleads.\n- Instead of \"Open Pantopus to see today's pickup\", draw the fact itself, because the notification is the whole message.\n\n====================================================================\n8. ReminderLeadControl\n====================================================================\nPURPOSE. Shows every reminder that will actually fire, on a small timeline running back from the date the person must act.\n\nPASSED-LEAD RULE (one rule for every variant). TODAY is Mon 19 Oct 2026. A lead whose date is before TODAY has passed. A passed lead has exactly one of two treatments:\n- Passed (never chosen): drawn disabled per C15: label in text.muted, no check, still focusable, read as \"<N> days, unavailable, <N> days before was <date>, which has passed.\" Activating it does not select it; it shows the explanation line and the suggestion under the control.\n- Chosen-then-passed (the lead was selected, then the date was edited so it has now passed): primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, NO check, label in bodySmall 400 text.primary, with the word \"passed\" under the label in caption text.primary (both lines fit in the 44pt segment). Dark: dark raised fill, 1.5px #38BDF8 border, no check, dark text primary label and word. Read as \"<N> days, selected, passed. <N> days before was <date>, which has passed.\" It keeps this treatment until the person picks another lead, and the explanation line and suggestion always show under the control.\nThe suggestion is always the longest lead that is still ahead. Nothing is saved until the person taps the suggestion or picks a live segment. The timeline never draws a passed lead's tick.\n\nANATOMY (00d · ReminderLeadControl · 01-anatomy · light, iOS 393, with callouts; the example date is the water-heater warranty ending Sat 12 Dec 2026)\nLead dates for this example: 60 days = Tue 13 Oct 2026 (passed) · 30 days = Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 7 days = Sat 5 Dec 2026 · 1 day = Fri 11 Dec 2026.\n1. Label above the control: label 13/18/600 text.primary, \"Remind me\".\n2. Segmented control, 361pt wide × 44pt tall (Android 380 × 48dp), four equal segments: \"60 days\", \"30 days\", \"7 days\", \"1 day\". The container has a 1px text.secondary outline, radius md 8 and 1px text.secondary dividers.\n   - Unselected segment: surface.base, label bodySmall text.primary.\n   - Selected segment: the C9 selection treatment. Selection = fill + check + weight. This matches the NotificationAsk chips.\n   - Passed segment: \"60 days\" is drawn disabled per the PASSED-LEAD RULE (callout: \"passed: Tue 13 Oct; focusable, reason read out\").\n   - Chosen-then-passed segment: drawn once as a small inset beside the control, per the PASSED-LEAD RULE (callout: \"chosen before a date edit; no check; 'passed' written\").\n   - Focus: the C9 ring, drawn separately on an unselected live segment.\n3. Mini timeline, 12pt below. A 2px text.secondary horizontal line with three 12pt-tall, 2px ticks, evenly spaced and not to scale. A two-slash break mark sits between the first and second ticks, captioned \"not to scale\". Each tick carries two labels:\n   - Date in bodySmall 14/20 text.primary: \"Thu 12 Nov 2026\" · \"Fri 11 Dec 2026\" · \"Sat 12 Dec 2026\".\n   - Role in caption 12/16 text.secondary: \"30 days before\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\".\n   A leader line runs from the \"Day of\" tick to an event label at the right end: KindGlyph (16pt, C14) plus \"Water-heater warranty ends\" in caption text.primary.\n4. Caption, 8pt below: \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\" in caption text.secondary.\n5. When \"1 day\" is selected, the lead and the day before are the same day, so draw two ticks (\"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\"). The caption then reads \"We'll also remind you on the day.\"\n\nVARIANTS (rows)\nV1 Date sheet (x-date-sheet): the warranty example, with 30 days selected and 60 days disabled (passed).\nV2 Extraction confirm (f10-extraction-confirm): 7 days is the default. The date is the City of Vancouver water bill, due Wed 28 Oct 2026. Passed leads: 60 days (Sat 29 Aug 2026) and 30 days (Mon 28 Sep 2026), both drawn disabled. Ticks: \"Wed 21 Oct 2026 · 7 days before\", \"Tue 27 Oct 2026 · Day before\", \"Wed 28 Oct 2026 · Day of\". Event label: \"Water bill due\".\nV3 Lease, anchored to the notice deadline (x-date-sheet, lease kind). The event is \"Notice deadline · Mon 1 Mar 2027\", never the lease end date. Draw the lease end \"Wed 31 Mar 2027\" as a label past the event in caption text.secondary (C5, readable, never text.muted), with the caption \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\". 30 days is selected. No lead has passed (60 days = Thu 31 Dec 2026). Ticks: \"Sat 30 Jan 2027 · 30 days before\", \"Sun 28 Feb 2027 · Day before\", \"Mon 1 Mar 2027 · Day of\".\n\nSTATES (columns)\nS1 Default: as drawn per variant, with passed segments disabled (V1: 60 days; V2: 30 and 60 days; V3: none).\nS2 Lead already passed (suggested alternative), per the PASSED-LEAD RULE:\n  - V1, labelled \"date first entered as Sat 16 Jan 2027 with 60 days chosen (Tue 17 Nov 2026), then edited to Sat 12 Dec 2026\": \"60 days\" uses the chosen-then-passed treatment. Under the control, a 16pt info glyph (primary.700) and \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" in bodySmall text.primary, then a suggestion button \"Use 30 days instead\" (outlined: surface.base, 1px text.secondary border, bodySmallMedium text.primary, 44pt). The timeline shows the suggested series \"Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 30 days before\", \"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\", captioned \"Suggested\".\n  - V2, labelled \"the extraction first read Sun 22 Nov 2026 and 30 days was chosen (Fri 23 Oct 2026); the date was then corrected to Wed 28 Oct 2026\": the event label stays \"Water bill due\". \"30 days\" uses the chosen-then-passed treatment and \"60 days\" is disabled (passed). The explanation line reads \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\", then \"Use 7 days instead\". The timeline shows \"Wed 21 Oct 2026 · 7 days before\", \"Tue 27 Oct 2026 · Day before\", \"Wed 28 Oct 2026 · Day of\", captioned \"Suggested\".\n  - V3: \"Not applicable: no lead has passed for Mon 1 Mar 2027\".\nS3 Disabled (date field empty): the segment container is on surface.sunken, all segment labels are text.muted, and no timeline is drawn. The segments stay focusable and read \"<N> days, unavailable, Add the date first to set reminders.\" The line \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" sits under it in bodySmall text.strong (on sunken). This state applies to all three variants.\n\nGRID. 00d · ReminderLeadControl · 02-variants-by-states · light has 3 × 3 cells on iOS, plus the \"1 day selected\" specimen for V1 beside the grid (named \"ReminderLeadControl / date sheet / default one day / ios\"). 00d · ReminderLeadControl · 03-variants-by-states · dark is the same full grid, including the one-day specimen, in dark tokens. Container: the control sits in a dark base sheet. The selected segment uses the C9 dark selection, and the chosen-then-passed segment uses the dark form from the PASSED-LEAD RULE. The container outline and ticks are #94A3B8 (C5, on dark base). Disabled labels are dark text.muted #64748B.\n\nAX5 / 200% / GREYSCALE (00d · ReminderLeadControl · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light)\n- (a) iOS AX5: the segments become four selectable rows, each at least 44pt. The selected row has the C9 selection treatment (primary.50 fill, 16pt check glyph, 600-weight label); unselected rows have no glyph; there are no circles. Line one is the role, line two is the date. For a passed row, only line one is text.muted; line two carries the date and the word \"passed\" in text.secondary, so the reason is always readable:\n  \"60 days before\" (text.muted) / \"Tue 13 Oct 2026 · passed\" (text.secondary) · \"30 days before\" / \"Thu 12 Nov 2026\" (selected) · \"7 days before\" / \"Sat 5 Dec 2026\" · \"1 day before\" / \"Fri 11 Dec 2026\".\n  The timeline becomes a vertical list of three rows: \"Thu 12 Nov 2026 · 30 days before\", \"Fri 11 Dec 2026 · Day before\", \"Sat 12 Dec 2026 · Day of\".\n- (b) Android 200%: the selectable rows as above, at 48dp.\n- (c) Greyscale: the selected segment is still identifiable by its check glyph and weight. Passed leads are identifiable by their lighter disabled label and missing check, and by the word \"passed\" in the AX rows. The chosen-then-passed segment is identifiable by the word \"passed\" under its label and its missing check, and S2 by the explanation line.\n- Extra row below: iOS AX1–AX2 (the segments become a 2×2 grid of 44pt cells) · Android 150% (a 2×2 grid of 48dp cells) · a web-1440 crop of V1 S1 inside the date sheet's 480px side panel.\n\nACCESSIBILITY\n- Spoken: \"Remind me, 30 days before, selected, 2 of 4.\" A passed segment: \"60 days, unavailable, 60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" A chosen-then-passed segment: \"60 days, selected, passed. 60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" The timeline is one element with the summary \"Reminders on Thu 12 Nov, Fri 11 Dec and Sat 12 Dec.\" (V2: \"Reminders on Wed 21 Oct, Tue 27 Oct and Wed 28 Oct.\" V3: \"Reminders on Sat 30 Jan, Sun 28 Feb and Mon 1 Mar.\") The same facts appear as a list at AX sizes. The S2 explanation line is announced politely when it appears.\n- Non-colour encoding: selection is a text label plus a fill change plus a check, not colour alone.\n- Targets: segments (including disabled ones) are 44pt on iOS, 48dp on Android and 44px on web. The ticks are not targets.\n\nCOPY. The caption is \"We'll also remind you the day before and on the day.\" Dates always show the weekday. Other strings: \"Remind me\" · \"60 days\" · \"30 days\" · \"7 days\" · \"1 day\" · \"60 days before\" · \"30 days before\" · \"7 days before\" · \"1 day before\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\" · \"passed\" · \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"Water bill due\" · \"Notice deadline\" · \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\" · \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" · \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\" · \"Use 30 days instead\" · \"Use 7 days instead\" · \"Suggested\" · \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" · \"We'll also remind you on the day.\"\n\nPLATFORMS. The same on all platforms apart from target sizes and the AX layouts above. On web-1440, the control sits in the date sheet's 480px side panel (drawn in the extra row on 04).\n\nIN CONTEXT (00d · ReminderLeadControl · 05-in-context-and-rules · light)\n- x-date-sheet: the Date sheet for \"Water-heater warranty\", with V1 below the date field.\n- x-date-sheet (lease): the Date sheet for the lease, with V3 anchored to the notice deadline.\n- f10-extraction-confirm: \"Confirm what we read\" for the water bill, with V2.\nAlso consumed by: none beyond these two surfaces.\n\nINSTEAD OF\n- Instead of a single \"Remind me 30 days before\" row, draw all three reminders with their real dates, because three will fire and the person should see each one.\n- Instead of anchoring the lease reminder to Wed 31 Mar 2027, anchor it to the notice deadline Mon 1 Mar 2027, because the notice is what the person must act on.\n- Instead of silently accepting a lead that has already passed, draw the explanation and \"Use 30 days instead\", because a reminder dated in the past never fires.\n- Instead of hiding or silently greying a passed lead, keep it focusable and read and write its reason, because silent dead controls leave people guessing.\n- Instead of keeping the check on a lead that passed after a date edit, draw the chosen-then-passed segment with the word \"passed\", because a check says a reminder will fire.\n- Instead of radio circles at large text, draw selectable rows with a check, because filled vs hollow circles mean provenance.\n- Instead of showing selection by colour alone, draw fill + check + weight, because colour alone fails in greyscale and for colour-blind users.\n- Instead of a timeline drawn to scale, draw evenly spaced ticks with a \"not to scale\" break, because a to-scale 60-day line squashes the last two ticks together.\n\n====================================================================\nARTBOARDS (44, in this order)\n====================================================================\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 01-anatomy · light — Today full card with callouts for heading, receipt line, CheckItems and sizes.\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 02-variants-by-states · light — 5 variants × all ticked / one pending / one failed.\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 03-variants-by-states · dark — dark twin of the full grid (card on dark raised).\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light — AX5 iOS, 200% Android, greyscale of S1–S3, widget-at-AX row.\n00d · QuietDayReceipt · 05-in-context-and-rules · light — PLACE B Today, Birchfield Ct widget and settings crops, plus accessibility, copy, platforms and instead-of.\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 01-anatomy · light — Shapes, height rulers, shimmer band, \"Loading\" container.\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 02-variants-by-states · light — Section, row, instrument and panel × shimmer / static / progressive.\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 03-variants-by-states · dark — dark twin of the full grid.\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 04-ax5-200-greyscale-reduce-motion · light — Large-text heights, greyscale, and a Reduce Motion row.\n00d · WarmingSkeleton · 05-in-context-and-rules · light — Today cold load, roster rows, bill trend, plus the rule panels and fail-closed list.\n00d · InlineUndo · 01-anatomy · light — Collapsed row, 44pt Undo, Android-only snackbar echo inset, fan-out hold caption.\n00d · InlineUndo · 02-variants-by-states · light — 6 variants × pending / undone / committed.\n00d · InlineUndo · 03-variants-by-states · dark — dark twin of the full grid.\n00d · InlineUndo · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light — Stacked Undo at large text, greyscale, and the iOS/Android/web Platforms row.\n00d · InlineUndo · 05-in-context-and-rules · light — Your places, Mail Day triage, household block, plus the rule panels.\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 01-anatomy · light — Dialog and sheet anatomy, outlined destructive button with error border and trash glyph, focus on Keep.\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 02-variants-by-states · light — 4 variants × open / deleting / done.\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 03-platforms · light — One photo on iOS, Android, web-390 and web-1440, plus the Leave home sheet on iOS and Android (light only).\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 04-variants-by-states · dark — dark twin of the full grid on dark base.\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light — Scrolling sheets, stacked buttons, greyscale.\n00d · DestructiveConfirm · 06-in-context-and-rules · light — Photo viewer, mail snaps card, roster, plus the rule panels.\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 01-anatomy-and-precedence · light — Pill anatomy, eight-step precedence ladder, one-banner scenario, zero-shift hidden slot.\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 02-variants-by-states · light — 7 variants × hidden / shown / offline, plus the 7-days-out specimens.\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 03-variants-by-states · dark — dark twin of the full grid.\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light — Wrapped radius-2xl form at large text, greyscale, Android and web Platforms row.\n00d · LandingBannerSlot · 05-in-context-and-rules · light — Invite on Place, expired compare on /start (web-390), claim receipt, plus the rule panels.\n00d · NotificationAsk · 01-anatomy · light — Card row, time chips, status slot, and the primer sheet anatomy (both entries).\n00d · NotificationAsk · 02-card-row-states · light — Card row and time chips × never asked / granted / declined / OS blocked / saving.\n00d · NotificationAsk · 03-primer-and-denial-by-platform · light — Pickup primers (iOS, Android), household primers (iOS, Android), iOS denied, Android denied once, Android blocked.\n00d · NotificationAsk · 04-card-row-and-primer · dark — dark twins of the card row, chips, the settings blocked row and both pickup primers.\n00d · NotificationAsk · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light — Stacked buttons, wrapped chips, scrolling primer, greyscale.\n00d · NotificationAsk · 06-in-context-and-rules · light — Briefing card, primer over the pickup card, settings blocked row, plus the rule panels.\n00d · PushCopy · 01-anatomy-and-levels · light — Tray illustration anatomy, 30/40 rulers, four-row levels table.\n00d · PushCopy · 02-ios-variants-by-states · light — 8 variants × collapsed / expanded / lock-screen public on iOS.\n00d · PushCopy · 03-android-variants-by-states · light — The same grid on Android.\n00d · PushCopy · 04-ios-and-android · dark — Five variants × collapsed / expanded on both platforms, dark.\n00d · PushCopy · 05-ax5-200-greyscale · light — Illustration at large text and greyscale.\n00d · PushCopy · 06-in-context-and-rules · light — Primer, settings row, household notification list, plus the rule panels.\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 01-anatomy · light — Segmented control with the passed 60-day segment, chosen-then-passed inset, three-tick timeline, caption, one-day case.\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 02-variants-by-states · light — Date sheet, extraction confirm, lease × default / lead passed / disabled.\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 03-variants-by-states · dark — dark twin of the full grid.\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 04-ax5-200-greyscale · light — Selectable rows with dates, vertical timeline, greyscale, plus a row with 2×2 grids and a web-1440 crop.\n00d · ReminderLeadControl · 05-in-context-and-rules · light — Warranty date sheet, lease date sheet, extraction confirm, plus the rule panels.\n00d · Notes — Assumptions, invented strings, contract conflicts, missing dependencies, omitted and light-only states, and open questions.\n\n====================================================================\nBATCH PLAN (at most 6 artboards per turn; after each turn, stop and wait for \"continue\")\n====================================================================\nOn this board, component order overrides the house-style priority order (dense default … dark twins last), so that each component the founder accepts is complete, dark twin included, before the next one begins.\nAt the start of every turn, re-read BOARD CONVENTIONS C1–C15 (including the C5 contrast table) and the full numbered sections for that turn's components before drawing.\nTurn 1 (re-read sections 1 and 2): QuietDayReceipt 01, 02, 03, 04, 05 · WarmingSkeleton 01\nTurn 2 (re-read sections 2 and 3): WarmingSkeleton 02, 03, 04, 05 · InlineUndo 01, 02\nTurn 3 (re-read sections 3 and 4): InlineUndo 03, 04, 05 · DestructiveConfirm 01, 02, 03\nTurn 4 (re-read sections 4 and 5): DestructiveConfirm 04, 05, 06 · LandingBannerSlot 01, 02, 03\nTurn 5 (re-read sections 5, 6 and 7): LandingBannerSlot 04, 05 · NotificationAsk 01, 02, 03, 04\nTurn 6 (re-read sections 6 and 7): NotificationAsk 05, 06 · PushCopy 01, 02, 03, 04\nTurn 7 (re-read sections 7 and 8): PushCopy 05, 06 · ReminderLeadControl 01, 02, 03, 04\nTurn 8 (re-read section 8 and the Notes section): ReminderLeadControl 05 · 00d · Notes\n\n====================================================================\n00d · Notes (write these items, then add anything else you had to decide)\n====================================================================\nContract conflicts and decisions made on this board (the founder confirms or overrides each one):\n1. PushCopy: the contract's example strings use \"Lacamas Dr\", \"Maple St\", \"Due Sep 20\" and \"Sun 31 Jan\". This board uses the fixture-aligned strings from the research brief (\"Larkspur Loop\", \"Due Fri 23 Oct\", \"Mon 1 Mar\").\n2. PushCopy V1: the contract body \"Recycling + garbage · City of Camas schedule. Bins out tonight.\" is 63 characters, over the 40 limit. This board uses \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\" (35).\n3. PushCopy V6: the contract's \"Sam paid 3 bills\" conflicts with the glossary rule \"marked … paid\". This board uses \"Sam marked 3 bills paid\".\n4. Title case: the contract says push actions are title case (\"That's My Day\"), while the research brief writes \"That's my day\" and the house style requires sentence case everywhere. \"Open Settings\" is also title case. This board follows the contract for both. Question for the founder: keep title case for these, or switch to sentence case (\"That's my day\", \"Open settings\")?\n5. PushCopy V4 (\"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\") is an invented title for the fixture's AQI 118 alert, which is below the Time Sensitive threshold.\n6. LandingBannerSlot V1: the contract example \"Sam Ortega invited you to the Payne St house\" uses a non-fixture street and the word \"house\", which the glossary forbids. This board uses \"Maya Chen invited you to Larkspur Loop\" and the degraded form \"…a home in Vancouver\".\n7. LandingBannerSlot V6: \"Synced 3 items from your other device\" uses \"synced\", which the glossary lists as a forbidden freshness word. It is kept as the contract string; question for the founder.\n8. ReminderLeadControl V3: the fixture's lease reminder is Mon 15 Feb 2027 (14 days before the notice deadline, and PushCopy V7 says \"due in 14 days\"), but the contract's leads are 60/30/7/1. This board draws 30 days (Sat 30 Jan 2027). Question: add a 14-day option, or change the fixture?\n9. QuietDayReceipt V4: the contract says \"Checked — nothing in the next two weeks\"; the research brief says \"…next 14 days\". This board uses the contract.\n10. NotificationAsk \"Open Settings\" vs \"Open settings\": the contract uses both. This board uses \"Open Settings\" everywhere (see item 4).\n11. NotificationAsk V1: the glossary says \"Not now\" is always paired with a permanent decline, but the contract's card row has only \"Yes / Not now\". This board draws the contract. Question: add \"No thanks\"?\n12. DestructiveConfirm dark: there is no dark error token. Because the label is text.primary (item 14), red appears only on the border and trash glyph, where #DC2626 at 3.70:1 on dark base passes for a non-text edge and glyph. No accent token is used. Dialogs and sheets stay on dark base, where the figure is higher than on dark raised (3.03:1).\n13. WarmingSkeleton dark: dark surface.sunken equals dark base, so the shapes use dark raised (or dark border.strong on raised cards).\n14. DestructiveConfirm label: the contract asks for a red label (\"text.error\", which is not a token), but the house style says semantic hues go on glyphs and borders only. This board follows the house style: a text.primary label at body 16/24 weight 600 (a weight step on an existing size, not a new type style), a 1.5px semantic.error border and a 16pt semantic.error trash glyph. Alternative the founder can choose instead: the contract's red label in semantic.error (4.83:1 on base), which would need a dark error text token (#DC2626 is 3.70:1 on dark base, below 4.5:1).\n15. QuietDayReceipt pending: the contract says one pending dot; this board draws three 3pt dots so it can't be read as a filled provenance mark.\n16. InlineUndo V2 \"Just you, then.\": the glossary forbids \"just you\" as a stand-in for \"Only you\" and names \"Just me\" as the household decline. Kept as the contract string; question for the founder (for example \"Just me, then.\").\n17. PushCopy V1 body \"Recycling + garbage · city schedule\": the glossary allows \"Recycling + garbage\" only in 30-character push titles. Kept in the body to fit 40 characters; question for the founder.\n18. WarmingSkeleton shapes: the contract says \"track outlines\" and \"ring outline\". This board draws filled shapes (an outline-only skeleton reads as empty, per the contract's own \"no frame-only skeletons\") and drops the ring, because research brief section 4 replaced the count ring with an integer plus chips.\n19. WarmingSkeleton threshold: the contract says cold loads of 1–10 s; research brief P11 says about 2–10 s. This board follows the contract (nothing under 1 s). Question: skeleton or nothing between 1 and 2 s?\n20. ReminderLeadControl passed leads: the contract gives no rule. This board uses the PASSED-LEAD RULE: a passed lead is disabled but focusable with the reason read out (per OfflineNotice's \"Disabled controls stay focusable\"), except a lead chosen before a date edit, which gets a third, chosen-then-passed treatment (selection fill and border, no check, the word \"passed\") until replaced; the suggestion is the longest lead still ahead. The same focusable-disabled rule is applied to LandingBannerSlot S3 and the DestructiveConfirm V4 Close during S2.\n21. ReminderLeadControl large text: the contract says \"radio rows\". This board draws selectable rows with a check and no circles, because filled vs hollow circles mean provenance only.\n22. Selection treatment: ReminderLeadControl segments and NotificationAsk chips both use the C9 treatment (primary.50 fill, 1.5px primary.700 border, check, 600 weight). The segment's earlier primary.700 fill was dropped so selection looks the same everywhere.\n23. QuietDayReceipt IN CONTEXT uses PLACE B (Jordan Lee, pickup Thursday, \"Saved place · Only you\", widget \"Birchfield Ct\"), because HOME A has pickup on Tue 20 Oct, so Mon 19 Oct evening at HOME A is not a quiet day.\n24. DestructiveConfirm S2: Escape, Back and swipe-to-dismiss are ignored while deleting; the V4 Close stays visible, disabled and focusable.\n25. InlineUndo V6 (Fan-out hold) is a sixth variant that the contract's variant list doesn't have. It comes from the contract's anatomy rule \"Household-notifying writes (Mark paid) hold their fan-out until undo closes\". Confirm it as a published variant.\n26. QuietDayReceipt spoken label: the contract says \"Checked: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\" This board's S1 label adds the heading and the time (\"Nothing needs your attention today. Checked at 6:00 PM: weather, air, alerts, your calendar.\"). Confirm.\n27. NotificationAsk entry points: the contract uses the primer for indirect entries (the first confirmed pickup, household activity from Mail), and this board draws the pickup primer after \"Yes, Tuesday is right\". Research brief section 2 item 8 says instead that the push ask follows the first \"That's my day\" inline (\"Remind you the night before? 6:00 PM\") and goes straight to the OS dialog. This board follows the contract. Question for the founder: primer sheet or inline row after the first pickup confirm?\n28. NotificationAsk household primer: the title \"Household updates on this phone\" and the body \"Pickup the night before. Air alerts when it's unhealthy. Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\" are invented. \"Arrive quietly\" is this board's plain-language wording for iOS Passive / Android LOW. Confirm the wording, and whether this entry should switch household activity on after the grant.\n29. PushCopy levels: the contract's levels have no row for air below AQI 151. This board adds \"Air below 151: iOS Active / Android DEFAULT\" (research brief section 3) and gives the Android air group two channels (HIGH and DEFAULT), so \"one channel per group\" has that one exception. Confirm.\n30. LandingBannerSlot precedence: the contract ladder (invite > reissue > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > setup > verify) leaves out sync merge (V6) and the claim receipt (V7). This board proposes invite > reissue > claim receipt > compare arrival > mailbox arrival > sync merge > setup > verify. Confirm the order.\n31. NotificationAsk S3 widget row: \"Put Today on your home screen\" capitalises Today to match the tab name. The glossary names the widget \"Today at your address\"; question for the founder whether the row should say \"Add Today at your address to your home screen\" instead.\n32. PushCopy V5 level: research brief section 3 makes bill_paid Active for members who still see the bill as unpaid and due within 3 days. Clark Public Utilities is due Fri 23 Oct, 4 days after TODAY, so V5 is drawn Passive.\nAssumptions: Maya also has a saved place (The Blairmont rental), so street labels show in PushCopy. Jordan's last briefing was sent Wed 14 Oct at 6:00 PM, before his Thursday pickup. The WarmingSkeleton V3a loaded strip includes HOA dues (Sun 1 Nov) and the voter registration deadline (Mon 26 Oct) as HOME A date marks; Comcast (Mon 2 Nov) falls outside the 14 days. The ReminderLeadControl S2 starting dates (Sat 16 Jan 2027; the misread Sun 22 Nov 2026) are invented so the chosen leads were live before the edit.\nMissing dependencies: list here any of FourteenDayStrip, YearBand, KindGlyph, AqiBand, ScaleStrip, PickupCard, MemberRow or the Pantopus app icon that was not yet published and was drawn as a labelled fallback box (C14), and whether the mailbox-arrival pill screenshot was attached.\nInvented strings (every one used on this board and not in the contract or fixtures):\n- QuietDayReceipt: \"air · not back yet\" · \"Checked 6:00 PM · air not back yet\" · \"Couldn't reach AirNow · 6:00 PM\" · \"Tonight's check couldn't reach AirNow · Retry\" · \"Couldn't reach the City of Vancouver calendar · Retry\" · \"Retry air quality\" (spoken) · the S1–S3 spoken labels · \"Last sent Wed 14 Oct, 6:00 PM\" · \"Birchfield Ct\" (widget label derived from the fixture).\n- WarmingSkeleton: \"Loading\" · \"Owner\" (MemberRow caption) · the skeleton bar heights and the bill-trend column pattern.\n- InlineUndo: \"Restored\" · \"Restored The Blairmont rental.\" (spoken) · \"6 pieces sorted\" · \"Clark Public Utilities marked paid\" · \"Sam sees this after you leave this screen.\" · \"Maya marked Clark PUD paid\" (reference thumbnail).\n- DestructiveConfirm: \"Leave Larkspur Loop?\" · all V4 list headings and items · \"Leave this home\" · \"Stay in this home\" · \"Remove Ollie\" · \"Keep Ollie\" · \"Deleting the photo…\" · \"Deleting 5 of 17…\" · \"Removing Ollie…\" · \"Leaving Larkspur Loop…\" · \"Photo deleted. The bill stays.\" · \"17 photos deleted. The bills and their amounts stay.\" · \"Ollie removed.\" · \"You left Larkspur Loop.\" · \"Close\" · \"Close is available when this finishes.\" (spoken).\n- LandingBannerSlot: \"Expires in 7 days · Mon 26 Oct\" · \"Expires tomorrow, Monday 26 October.\" (spoken) · \"You're offline. Review opens when you're back.\" · \"You're offline. Fix opens when you're back.\" · the \"· Review\" action on V6 · \"Close\" on V5 · \"You claimed Larkspur Loop · See what moved\" · \"What moved when you claimed\".\n- NotificationAsk: \"Pickup reminders on this phone\" · \"Household updates on this phone\" · \"Household updates stay off until you turn them on, then arrive quietly.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus.\" · \"Notifications are off for Pantopus. These rows still update inside the app.\" · \"Opens the Notifications page for Pantopus in Settings.\" · \"Put Today on your home screen\" · \"Add the widget\" · \"Saving…\" · \"Saved\" · \"Couldn't save · Retry\" · \"Close\" · \"6:00 PM, selected, 2 of 4.\" (spoken).\n- PushCopy: \"Sensitive groups: AQI 118\" · \"now\" · \"Time Sensitive\" (as an in-illustration word) · \"Date reminder\" placeholder · \"Pantopus · <placeholder>\" for the non-pickup groups · the spoken illustration label \"Example notification…\" · \"Never Time Sensitive for pickup.\" · the Android air-channel line under the levels table.\n- ReminderLeadControl: \"Remind me\" · \"Day before\" · \"Day of\" · \"60 days before\" · \"30 days before\" · \"7 days before\" · \"1 day before\" · \"passed\" · \"Water-heater warranty ends\" · \"Water bill due\" · \"Notice deadline\" · \"Lease ends — reminders count back from the notice deadline\" · \"60 days before was Tue 13 Oct, which has passed.\" · \"30 days before was Mon 28 Sep, which has passed.\" · \"Use 30 days instead\" · \"Use 7 days instead\" · \"Suggested\" · \"Add the date first to set reminders.\" · \"We'll also remind you on the day.\" · the chosen-then-passed spoken label.\n- Shared: the \"<label>, unavailable, <reason>\" spoken pattern.\n- Board chrome: \"host illustrative, not a spec\" · \"Not this\" · \"No action\" · \"action works offline\" · every \"Not applicable: <reason>\" cell caption · \"same height\" · \"height = the consuming row's final height\" · \"under 1 s: show nothing new; keep the old content\" · \"no shimmer; replacements cross-fade\" · \"stays until you leave this screen\" · \"android only\" · \"no red fill\" · \"no red text\" · \"Never two banners.\" · \"hidden = 0pt; the first section stays put\" · \"→ Invitations list\" · \"Appears only after an action that shows the purpose\" · \"Yes fires the OS prompt directly. The OS prompt is not drawn.\" · the primer entry captions (\"after the first confirmed pickup\", \"after household activity from Mail\", \"after the iOS prompt was declined\", \"after the Android prompt was declined once\", \"after the Android prompt was declined twice\") · \"drop ' · Larkspur Loop' for someone with one place\" · \"not to scale\" · the S2 scenario labels on ReminderLeadControl · the callout texts in each anatomy · the \"Platforms\" and \"Reduce Motion\" row labels.\nOmitted, with reason:\n- NotificationAsk on web (no web push in scope; question for the founder).\n- LandingBannerSlot compare-arrival, mailbox-arrival, setup and verify banners (named in the precedence ladder only; their strings belong to their own surface prompts).\n- The OS permission dialog itself (never drawn).