ead disabled but focusable (V1: 60 days; V2: 30 and 60 days), except a lead chosen before a date edit, which uses the chosen-then-passed treatment (V1 S2: 60 days; V2 S2: 30 days). Its V1 and V2 lead-passed cells are real specimens.\n- Every disabled control on the board is focusable with its reason read out and written in readable text. No control uses a radio circle.\n- DestructiveConfirm has no red fill and no red text; red is only on its border and trash glyph.\n- Every string on the board appears in this prompt or on 00d · Notes. Every push string shows its character count, and none exceeds 30 (title) or 40 (body).\n- No hex values appear on the board except the C5 contrast figures. No serif or italic type, no cream or tinted backgrounds, no illustrations of creatures, no confetti, no countdowns, no system-dialog imitations, no placeholder box where a published component exists.\n- Every control shows its dashed hit area (44pt / 48dp / 44px). No tick is drawn inside a filled or hollow circle.\n- 00d · Notes lists items 1–32, the assumptions, the missing dependencies, the invented strings and the omissions (including the light-only list).\n\n====================================================================\nPUBLISH\n====================================================================\nWhen I accept a component, add it to the Pantopus design system under this exact name. The eight names are QuietDayReceipt, WarmingSkeleton, InlineUndo, DestructiveConfirm, LandingBannerSlot, NotificationAsk, PushCopy and ReminderLeadControl. Publish each one with its variants and states named exactly as printed under its specimens on this board (for example \"InlineUndo / removed row / pending undo / ios\"). Publish every specimen in light. Publish in dark only the specimens drawn on that component's dark artboard; the specimens listed as light only under \"Omitted, with reason\" on 00d · Notes are published in light only. Publish only a component I have accepted by name."
